{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england","id":1501560,"title":"Regional Settings - New England","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-01-28T12:37:11-08:00","id":1501560,"title":"Regional Settings - New England","content":"Something I do on my free time is think about VtM and try to flesh out the setting in my head for better use in my games. I\u2019m sure that I\u2019m not alone in this and so I\u2019m interested in getting an idea about what other people are thinking about things.<br /> <br /> Recently I\u2019ve been thinking about regions of North America and trying to get an idea about how I\u2019d handle them in my games and what a hypothetical source book for them would look like and how that could help explore options and flesh things out in the setting.<br /> <br /> So when I decided to take this to the forums, I figured I\u2019d start with a region that actually did receive a sourcebook, New England. I know that Dark Colony is considered something of a mixed bag, so I figured that people probably had ideas about how they\u2019d handle a revised version or an alternate version for that use.<br /> <br /> All that said, here\u2019s some of the things that I\u2019ve been thinking about re:New England VtM as a regional setting.<br /> <br /> \u2022To the North of New England we have Montreal and the Quebec City-Windsor Corridor and to the South we have the Northeast Atlantic Megalopolis (New York City, Philadelphia, Baltimore, DC, etc.); so New England is a region that\u2019s situated between two Sabbat strongholds in the WoD. I personally view Montreal as being rather civil and peaceful as Sabbat domains go, being the theological center of the Sabbat in North America, which I imagine seeps into some of the motifs that New England will have as a region and give us opportunities to have \u2018quiet Sabbat\u2019 influence around. Meanwhile imo the Sabbat is the Atlantic Northeast as the Camarilla is to the Great Lakes; the regions where the \u2018default status quo\u2019 of the sect on the continent most clearly exists. So naturally we can have any more conventional Sabbat antics come rambling up from New York or Philly.<br /> <br /> \u2022New England as a region has become closely associated with Eldritch Horror/Lovecraftian Horror, particularly as far as the horror genre is concerned. For that reason it\u2019s a motif I would want included. I\u2019ve sometimes toyed with the notion of having the fictional city of Arkham, MA exist in WoD but I usually play it safe and have it be cribbed into Providence, RI. So that\u2019s one element to play around with. Scholars of the occult, eldritch mysteries, and unknown powers circulating all around the region; I see this offering all sorts of potential inspiration or plot hooks for Malkavians, Nosferatu, Tremere, Tzimisce, Giovanni, Settites, &amp; Ravnos.<br /> <br /> \u2022I think most people in the US will read some novel set in Puritan New England at some point in their lives if they attended public schools, so I feel like that has to be a motif in play as well. The idea of there being centers of hunter activity, going back to the Puritans comes to mind, particularly as iirc that\u2019s Sullivan Dane\u2019s backstory. It makes me think about not only having Tremere and sorcerers in the area but also a Vigil style compact of Puritan-Christian hunters who have been in the trade since the old English Civil Wars. <br /> <br /> \u2022Another motif I\u2019d want to see explored is the various conspiratorial themes that pop up in New England. Things like Yankees popping up throughout the early Intelligence services in the US, what\u2019s going on at Yale with Skull &amp; Bones, and things of that sort. In the World of Darkness I think those veins are ripe for all sorts of inspirational material. iirc we already know that the Ventrue Upton Rowland is involved in such things, let\u2019s explore that further. Let\u2019s also get into things like Warwick the Nosferatu\u2019s network and whatever vampiric secret societies definitely exist in the region. Maybe a Gehenna cult or two as well.<br /> <br /> \u2022Boston naturally comes to mind as the central city of the region and as such an important vampiric domain to consider. The Giovanni Chronicles make it an important city for the Giovanni and I\u2019m inclined to use some of that. IMO the Giovanni are good fits for the spookiness of New England, the idea of quasi-incestuous Boston Brahmins, the old history of piracy along the New England coast, and as a central node for the Milliner family. The Milliners in particular I think would be useful to use as a vessel for the image of the shadowy mid-20th century Yankees who may or may not have had their fingers on the pulse of the JFK assassination. Boston is also a useful city for the Anarchs imo. With Philadelphia as a Sabbat city, Boston is the city I most associate with old revolutionary history. This leads me to think of an idea which Children of the Revolution also plays with, a society of Anarchs in Boston who more resemble Fortier Chartists &amp; Liberal Reformists then the punks out further west. I would probably have this society of Anarchs be a cooperative loyal opposition to the Prince of the City, whose of a Chartist-Reformist mold on account of the difficulties a hard-line Prince would have operating as such in a region with a prominent Clan Tremere, Clan Giovanni, Anarch Movement, &amp; Sabbat on either side.<br /> -I personally think that William Biltmore &amp; Co. can be salvaged as a Prince of Boston. Tone down the Arthurian &amp; Revolutionary history elements somewhat (but don\u2019t totally remove them) and imo it would be very interesting to play William &amp; his brood as being in touch with the eldritch unconsciousness of the region and that being one of the reasons he\u2019s able to maintain praxis and largely keep the peace.<br /> <br /> \u2022New England is one of the parts of the US with some significant post-Columbian history and that should be taken into account; including the Revolutionary War certainly but not limited to it. I\u2019d want to see Ventrue and Tzimisce who have centuries old power in the rural countryside because the colonies (particularly the Dutch ones) were originally founded as aristocratic holdings. I want to see Brujah &amp; Lasombra pirates. I want to see Puritan and Quaker witch-hunting societies. I want to see trading magnates, both urban like the Boston Brahmins and rural like the family from Dark Shadows. I do want to see something about the American Revolution, particularly the old implications that the events of the Revolution were closely linked with the First Sabbat Civil War, and what the ramifications of that were. I also want to see what role New England played, if any, in the Crusades which would eventually see the Sabbat take power throughout the Atlantic Northeast.<br /> <br /> These are all the things that came to mind to me from my brainstorming about the region of New England for VtM. I hope that some of y\u2019all found it interesting or enjoyable and I really hope that you\u2019ll share any ideas of your own about what New England ought to look like in the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-29T20:28:12-08:00","id":1501661,"title":"","content":"And don't forget Stephen King; he's straight up New Englander. <br /> <br /> I was recently working on a bit of New England, Massachusetts to be exact, a massive-map from a PC-Game editor, (American Conquest), of a possible Puritan-colony or later, Most likely later given the tile-sets. It's basically NWoD, Spirits Book: powerful spirits reside in the land and influence the local mortals; from the native-Americans, to Viking-settlers, to the Puritans. And yes, there's going to be rows of corn. They guide a child to an old Viking book, where they learn Viking magic, Mage: the Dark Ages etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T11:34:46-08:00","id":1501728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england#post1501560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... I also want to see what role New England played, if any, in the Crusades which would eventually see the Sabbat take power throughout the Atlantic Northeast....</div> </div> </div> </div>Clan Novel Lasombra has the Sabbat attack on Hartford and there's a small chapter or two which take place in Waterbury.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T13:18:28-08:00","id":1501739,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, I was just thinking about Stephen King and how he\u2019d also be someone who would be a deep vein of inspirational material, although honestly I think his work in general is good inspiration for any sort of WoD games or Chronicles game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T22:28:11-08:00","id":1501848,"title":"","content":"I will be posting other things on this thread, but for now I will limit this post to commentary on just the Triad.<br /> <br /> It was a major mistake of the original sourcebook to place the Triad as arriving in 1895 and bringing in nameless British vampire goons as a retread of the American Revolution. Nameless goons without motivations aren't good VtM characters - they are orcs. However, it is easy to fix this. Simply bring in the Triad prior to the American Revolution - early 17th century. Let them lead the rebellion against the Ventrue political domination of the New England colonies. They lead the rebellion and win.<br /> <br /> Then in 1895, the Triad become overtly repressive as a result of them reacting against Sabbat incursions to their domains. They get scared. They succeed at repelling the Sabbat, but at a price - they become tyrannical. Their minions aren't nameless goons, but existing Kindred (which alas the ST will have to create) who decided strict repression to stop the Sabbat was worth it. But it alienated a lot of other Kindred, especially as time went by.<br /> <br /> The Triad are still controversial figures. Some in the Camarilla laud them for being effective at repelling the Sabbat at a time when many other domains fall to them. But others complain that they turning back the clock and eliminating many Camarilla reforms that took the Kindred out of the Dark Ages setting. There is merit to both sides.<br /> <br /> So you still have the Ventrue trying to win back influence. You still have some younger resistance to the Triad (though let's not call it the Kindred of Liberty). But it will feel more organic to the region instead of artificial. It builds on the setting's history instead of being an artificial repetition of it.<br /> <br /> I will post more later on other subjects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T23:57:14-08:00","id":1501851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/244784/Dark-New-England-Regional-Sourcebook\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/images/1/244784.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/244784/Dark-New-England-Regional-Sourcebook\" target=\"_blank\"> Dark New England Regional Sourcebook - White Wolf | Storytellers Vault </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/244784/Dark-New-England-Regional-Sourcebook\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/244784/Dark-New-England-Regional-Sourcebook </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Dark New England Regional Sourcebook - Dark New England is a V20 supplement designed to update information and plotlines from several early edition Vampire: Th </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T13:59:05-08:00","id":1501903,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m excited to hear your thoughts Black Fox and looking forward to see your upcoming posts!<br /> <br /> That said the mention of the Triad and their history also reminds me of something I\u2019ve been chewing on wrt New England. That being trying to sketch out with the historical periods of vampiric power ought to look like from the early colonies through to the First Sabbat Civil War and the Northeast Atlantic Crusades.<br /> <br /> One of the things in particular I\u2019ve ended up thinking about is how the vampires of Britain ought to be sketched since it feels clear to me that they\u2019ll naturally influence how the vampires of New England will develop.<br /> <br /> Britain has generally been described as being somewhat apart from the mainland Camarilla of the Old World (if one imagines that the Great Lakes are the Camarilla status quo of North America then I have to figure that the French &amp; German cores are the Camarilla status quo of Old Europe). So since in Vampire, the history of Mithras is analogous with the vampiric history of Britain, I have to figure what\u2019s going on contemporaneously with Mithras in Britain will effect New England.<br /> <br /> (please forgive any inaccuracies with either the history of Mithras or Britain in this post, it was made browsing over the wiki articles of both)<br /> <br /> So Mithras arrives in Britain alongside the Romans, goes into torpor, and rises in time to make himself narratively connected with the post-Norman history of Britain. We know after that Mithras becomes the leading figure of Britain during the Middle Ages, via the Baronies of Avalon, and refuses to compromise his power by joining the nascent Camarilla even after the Anarch Revolts begin (although he does streamline things a bit). I wonder if we\u2019re supposed to view the medieval Baronies of Avalon as a sort of vampiric Magna Carta in this period, based on the name and the idea that Mithras began to take a more active role in directly controlling affairs between the Anarch Revolts and the events of the Giovanni Chronicles in 1666. The mentions of the War of the Roses and Toreador strongholds in Scotland, plus some conflicts between England and Scotland, also makes me wonder if we\u2019re supposed to imagine that the Toreador of Scotland are acting as a fifth column of the Camarilla against the Baronies during the early modern period while Mithras is still holding out. Then there\u2019s the Tudors from up until the start of the period where the American colonies would be coming up and how to consider that factoring in. So from the period of the American colonies springing up you\u2019ve got the Stuarts, the English Civil War, the Glorious Revolution, the Acts of Union, the Hanovers, and the Empire starting to come into its potential. Plus of course the French Revolution is a couple decades off.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s the kind of stuff that keeps coming around in my head when I try to think about how to bring together real history and vampiric history. Trying to have an idea of what cliques had power in what areas. For instance I can imagine one scenario where the Southern Lords &amp; the New England Ventrue/Baronets self-consciously style themselves on the Baronies while the Big Atlantic Urban domains are nurturing larger vampiric populations with Chartists/Camarilla Reformists who seize the energy of the Revolution to further their own ends.<br /> <br /> But this is admittedly all off the cuff. If I really want to weave in those elements of real life history I\u2019d definitely need to do more chewing on them before having any certain ideas. That said however, I hope that it helps explain the sort of ideas that I\u2019ve been chewing on and is the sort of thing which is also of interest to you all.<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11637,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","user":"Gryffon15","date":". 02-01-2023, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T16:45:53-08:00","id":1501905,"title":"","content":"The next thing is to incorporate some actual lore into the setting that is already established, but which for some reason is absent in Dark Colony. You can't have Boston without some reference to canon characters like Jeremy MacNeil, Crispus Attucks, and Marguerite Foccart. Boston and the early days of the Revolution are supposed to be important in what will one day become the new Anarch movement and establishment of the Los Angeles Free State.<br /> <br /> I would hold that originally the Triad were seen as part of this push for freedom. Roman Pendragon and William Biltmore being seen as agents of freedom (Warwick was there too, but is supposed to be unknown). We're told that the clans who challenged Ventrue dominance in New England were the Brujah, Gangrel, and Malkavians so this doesn't change too much. It's only later that MacNeil and others realize that Pendragon and Biltmore have their own reasons to overthrow the Ventrue, and it is not in the cause of reforming Camarilla society but their own ambitions. After 1895 that cannot be denied. In Pendragon's case, he effectively splits the Brujah as many Brujah still flock to him as a strong Brujah Prince looking out for clan interests.<br /> <br /> So MacNeil and his friends become enemies of Brujah like Roman Pendragon who represented the old European feudal elite. While they are no longer present, there are plenty of Brujah who are their descendants in the region. They consider themselves the &quot;real&quot; Brujah against the elder Roman Pendragon and his faction, whom they believe betrayed the ideals of the Revolution by simply becoming another Prince.<br /> <br /> I would change Pug Jackson, instead of being embraced in West Africa and then subsequently enslaved by white Ventrue and brought to the New World (!?!), to being a normal black slave brought to New England and subsequently freed and embraced. I don't understand the logistics or logic of enslaving an existing vampire and bringing him across the Atlantic (to Louisiana, not even anywhere near New England). Pug is canonically 9th generation and embraced in 1734 in Africa. So depending on what generation and age the ST wants him to be, he could be the childe of any number of Anarchs. If you want to keep the generation the same, MacNeil would be the sire though his embrace would be placed far later. Or if you want to change the generation, then either Marguerite or Crispus could be his sire. Or if you want to keep Pug older, you'll need some other Brujah to do the deed. You'll also need to work out the specifics of how he got to Boston (slavery was still legal in Massachusetts at the time of the Revolution). In any case, he should be a contemporary of these other Anarchs. He keeps in contact with his sire and a mentor and is an important Anarch leader in the region because of his personal connections. He should also be given some reason why he choose to stay in the area rather than leaving the others. I'd probably portray him as someone who code switches between a street smart gang leader and an educated, respectable person. Someone who can act both like Denzel Washington's and Andre Braugher's characters in the movie Glory as needed.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs are rather neglected in the Dark Colony sourcebook. While mentioned, they don't have named NPCs in the setting and the Kindred of Liberty are not so much Anarchs as &quot;American&quot; vampires of the Camarilla struggling against the &quot;British&quot; vampires of the Camarilla. The canonical Pug isn't even an Anarch, but a member of the KOL. I think Pug would be a good figure to fix that with only a few changes to his background. You can then build an Anarch coterie around him. I'd probably limit it to some big umbrella coterie where all the Anarchs have banded together because between the Triad and Sabbat, they probably are more concerned with survival than with political disputes. That doesn't mean that individual members would not have differences, but that those are put aside because of the needs of survival. Though I could also see one or two other very small coteries of Anarchs (say 2-3 members) out there as well.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T16:59:14-08:00","id":1501906,"title":"","content":"The Gangrel should be more prominent in the setting. In the history section of Dark Colony, generic talk about the Gangrel is quite interesting, but we only get one example - and he's not even originally from New England!<br /> <br /> Battista Decameron - I like him, but there needs to be a few changes. I keep the character as is except for him being part of a Spanish exploration near modern day Colombia, he was part of Henry Hudson's voyages on behalf of England. He was one of the crewman who remained loyal to Hudson during the mutiny in 1611 and left castaway. He knows the actual fate of Hudson, but never speaks of it. I thought that would tie him in better with the heritage of New England. I adjusted his Generation to 7<sup>th</sup> and made him the childe of the unnamed Wamponoag medicine man embraced by an unnamed Gangrel Methusaleh mentioned in the History section.<br /> <br /> Although Tyrus of the Wolfpack (Chicago By Night) was from Maryland, I have his sire (Gareth) be one of the unnamed \u201cthree progeny\u201d of the unnamed Gangrel Methusaleh who all arrived in the early 16<sup>th</sup> century per the History section in Dark Colony.\u200b Gareth is now gone, but one of his childer (and thus Tyrus's broodmate) is in the area, and has his own coterie that helps protect the region from Sabbat. He too might be some kind of Archon with his own pack of mates/henchmen who patrol the Eastern Seaboard in the same way that the Wolfpack patrols the Midwest. This other childe of Gareth might be an English colonist like Tyrus, a colonist of some other European power during the colonial era (like New Holland or New Sweden), or another American Indian.<br /> <br /> I always thought there should be some powerful Gangrel elders from the days of King Philip\u2019s War, the first contact with the Plymouth Bay Colony, and the like, and representing different ethnic groups. Lots of local history flavor is possible with them, and would reinforce the history of the region. Some stay in the region full time while others wander but visit on a regular basis. One of them might be a good rival for Jeremy Skelton, the Brujah anti-tribu Sabbat who was Abenaki as a mortal.<br /> <br /> That this are was once seeded by the childer of a powerful and ancient Gangrel Methusaleh could distinguish the Gangrel of New England as being of exceptionally potent blood. It would be a good way to distinguish this clan from the other Camarilla clans in the region who arrived scattershot from many places and lines. Having some potent Gangrel in the wilderness of New England could also explain the Sabbat's ongoing attacks in the area (both in order to diablerize them and also why they take so many casualties).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T17:03:06-08:00","id":1501907,"title":"","content":"Here are two other sources of inspiration I would use.<br /> <br /> There was a New England Vampire Panic throughout the 19<sup>th</sup> century because of tuberculosis. In my setting it would also be because of Sabbat creation rites and other activities. I use some roman-a-clefs on some of the more famous cases to fill out Sabbat packs (there is a Sabbat vampire just known as Mercy that has features of Mercy Brown for example, and a Ransom from Frederick Ransom, though their character biographies are fictionalized). The panic ended because of the temporary victory over the Sabbat by Pendragon\u2019s \u201cOperation Longbow\u201d in 1895. It took some time for the Sabbat to recover, and they needed to change tactics.<br /> \u200b<br /> I would also steal as much as I can from the Dark Shadows TV show since it is set in the fictional town of Collinsport, Maine. Although I obviously change the names and revise concepts to be more appropriate for the World of Darkness. Barnabas Collins would make a great \u201cheroic\u201d Ventrue looking out for his mortal family, and I like that the series concentrates more on personal issues than any kind of vampire politics which tends to eat up so much of the game. A small coastal town watched over by a single vampire who ignores the Jyhad is a great character. His home might be a good place for like minded vampires to visit and obtain his advice, or for more political vampires to visit and try to obtain his support. And he might need help from the PCs if a Sabbat pack hears of him and targets him for one of their diablerie raids.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-01T17:22:50-08:00","id":1501908,"title":"","content":"And some notes on the Tremere.<br /> <br /> Since Brown University in Providence is the model for Miskatonic University in Arkham, the main Tremere chantry in the region is based there (not Hartford as per Dark Colony). They investigate a lot of &quot;witch haunted&quot; New England. Their presence in Providence, the stronghold of Warwick, presents some interesting conflict. I have it be the only Chantry in New England, although the chantry does have several safe houses set up around the region so the local Tremere have places to stay. The New Hartford safehouse is believed by non-Tremere to be the &quot;home&quot; of the clan, and that their true chantry in Providence is a secret known only to them and Warwick's Web.<br /> <br /> Evan Rhys (John Reiss) is basically the same Tremere, but instead of being some Austrian in colonial New England, I made him some Welsh colonist. I would change his sire to one of the two Tremere NPCs name dropped in the history section - Madeline Coventry or Baladin. Because why wouldn't you do that? One of the big flaws of Dark Colony is that so much of the detailed history that is provided does not show up in its actual NPCs. This would fix that. Other than the slight name change and some early history, it doesn\u2019t change his function in the chronicle. Although I do have \u201cJohn Reiss\u201d be a mortal alias of his. He is one of the few Tremere who has intimate details of the feud between Coventry and Baladin, and his exact role during that struggle would be left up to the ST.<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200bErich Weiss (Harry Houdini), the Rogue Tremere mentioned in one of the stories in Succubus Club, was originally one of the apprentices in the New England chantry. His unnamed sire is from there. There's no actual connection to New England mentioned in the Succubus Club, but the sire needs to be from somewhere, so why not? Since Erich Weiss went rogue, and it's possible his unnamed sire was punished as a result of an unauthorized embrace, this might just be trivia. Or it could be the springboard for something.<br /> <br /> Some more to come, later.<br /> <br /> EDIT: This is an addition to my original post. I just noticed that there is another Tremere in the story adventure section of Dark Colony. (I had completely forgotten about him as it had been years since I bothered reading that scenariol) That is Zachariah Slane. Zachariah is the # 2 Tremere under John Reiss. He is a Tremere who arrived in Boston earlier than Reiss' appearance in New England. He thinks the Tremere would improve their position if they had a second chantry in Boston. I think this character would a lot to the Tremere. Reiss is more conservative in his approach. He prefers a solid alliance with the Ventrue against the Triad. He sees Tremere power in the region to be based on unity. Zachariah is more risk tolerant. He is willing to consider an alliance with Pendragon to expand Tremere power as long as he supports the establishment of a second Tremere Chantry in Boston. While that would divide the Tremere in two camps, it would expand their influence. The backstory also implies a resentment of Zachariah that an outsider was brought in to control the chantry, and he thinks he should control a chantry of his own.<br /> <br /> That story adventure begins with Zacharian already leaving the Hartford chantry. But I think more STs could make use of him before he decides to take matters in his own hand. Then when he does, the ST could either run that scenario in Dark Colony or do something else. I think he's more useful as an NPC in the general setting than just as an element of the scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  added new text 02-13-2023, 02:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-02T20:37:19-08:00","id":1502003,"title":"","content":"I will just mention Nathaniel Hawthorne as the other writer alongside Lovecraft and King in the New England trinity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T11:18:44-08:00","id":1502030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since Brown University in Providence is the model for Miskatonic University in Arkham, the main Tremere chantry in the region is based there (not Hartford as per Dark Colony). They investigate a lot of &quot;witch haunted&quot; New England. Their presence in Providence, the stronghold of Warwick, presents some interesting conflict.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Something that this idea of having the Tremere and Nosferatu power centers in New England overlap reminds me of is that idea from the original Clanbook Nosferatu that there was some sort of ongoing antagonism between Clans Nosferatu and Tremere. I don\u2019t think that plotthread was really carried out, aside from being used as an in-universe justification for the Chicago flood of 1992 but I do think it could be interesting to use that as a way of fleshing out the idea of a conflict.<br /> <br /> We know that the Nosferatu, alongside the Gangrel &amp; Tzimisce, were on the frontlines of early Tremere experiments with both their own vampirism and the creation of Gargoyles, alongside the early Tremere wars. That\u2019s obviously one cause for conflict but it\u2019s also a bit abstract. Unless you have elders of the victimized clans around to keep the animosity alive, it\u2019s not going to come up very much. I do think there\u2019s an interesting reason to keep that animosity around as a plot element however. The early books seemed to play around with having the Tremere be the actual designated-villains of vampire (or at least Camarilla) society. If you read the Brujah opinions on the other clans in the first two core books, it certainly seems that they reserve more animosity and suspicion for the Tremere then they do the Ventrue. If I had to guess this got lost overtime for a number of reasons, one being the development of Carthage and Rome as sticking points between Brujah and Ventrue as well as Chicago by Night establishing the former clan as the poster child of the Anarchs and the latter clan as the vanguard of Camarilla tyranny via Lodin and his brood. I think though you can get some interesting plots by keeping some of those older Tremere ideas around and that it could be used along the Nosferatu in particular. While the Gangrel can be written off as carrying long grudges because of their oral tradition and their somewhat implied honor culture as well as their general suspicion to anthro-centric magic due to their association with more \u2018natural and wild spirituality\u2019. The Nosferatu on the other hand are different imo. One of the Nosferatu\u2019s whole schticks is that they\u2019re the lead spymasters of vampiric society. I think that\u2019s an interesting avenue to run with when thinking about them and the Tremere. The Nosferatu know things that the other clans don\u2019t and they can tell that the Tremere are always up to something behind the scenes and that they\u2019re not gonna like whatever it is - and the Tremere know that of all the clans, the Nosferatu have the most-accurate understanding of what they\u2019re actually working on, which is certainly not something the Pyramid relishes the thought of.<br /> <br /> The overlap of Nosferatu and Tremere with Providence could provide a good grounding for the basis of that rivalry-mutual suspicion in North American settings I think. It\u2019s not simply that the Nosferatu, ever wary of persecution from outsiders, remember how their clan suffered at the hands of the early Tremere; they know for a fact that the Tremere are still up to something and that whatever it is, the Pyramid has long shown it\u2019s willing to break a few sewer rats to get what it wants. What the Tremere are actually up to is an open question for STs though in my opinion and aside from whatever Vienna is scheming, the answer is probably different in every domain. That said however, of all the North American domains, imo is one of the more thematically fitting ones for the Tremere to be working on Gargoyles. I can also see the slavery motif complementing the US South or the Caribbean but the imagery of living Gargoyles suits the gothic sensibilities of New England &amp; Montreal more then most other NA regions imo.<br /> <br /> All that said, I appreciate everyone\u2019s posts and I\u2019m interested to see anything else people might have in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-03T11:51:49-08:00","id":1502037,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve also been chewing on Black Fox\u2019s posts about the Triad and I think it leads to some interesting ideas for New England as a setting. If I\u2019m making any incorrect assumptions in your reasoning Black Fox, please correct me.<br /> <br /> One of the most interesting parts of New England as a vampiric setting is, from a politics perspective, how surreal and archaic it would seem to most North American Camarilla of the modern era, even the residents of Chicago for example.<br /> <br /> It seems that one of the core vampiric political debates of New England would be whether Mithras (the Ventrue Old Guard/Absolutists and the like-minded) or the Triad (The Leading Barons or the Quasi-Parliament of the Brujah, Malkavian, and Nosferatu) ought to be the final authority in inter-domain political disputes, with the Camarilla proper being something of an after thought/formality for both groups. The Old Guard, primarily represented by the Ventrue who first established domains in New England in the colonial period, arguing that Mithras (or his current representative as the case may be) is the best choice for an ultimate authority, an enlightened vampiric despot who can not only judge barons fairly but mediate disputes between them and the residents of their domains fairly, while preserving the security of all against outsiders. Then you have the Triad, primarily represented by the formal members of the Triad as well as the kindred (primarily but not exclusively of clans Brujah, Malkavian, &amp; Nosferatu) who rejected the tyranny of Mithras and his Ventrue Baron puppets in favor of having the highest authority be a gathering of powerful barons (the Triad) who could not only do whatever Mithras could but also protect the rights of the smaller barons and petty \u2018lords\u2019 against the arbitrary rule of the Despot and their favored kindred. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, while these archaic distinctions are being squabbled over between the Old Guard and the Triad, you have the \u2018Kindred of Liberty\u2019 whose revolutionary cause isn\u2019t some sort of Anarch Free State but just that the Camarilla as such establishes enough potency in the region that conclaves can be called and have their rulings enforced in regional affairs, rather then having it be known that practically speaking, either the Ventrue Old Guard or the Triad will be the ones determining how regional affairs will be run and that the Justicars are at worst a rubber stamp and at best a counter-weight forcing the locals to at least take the Camarilla into consideration before making its decision.<br /> <br /> Then in the mix of all that, the actual Anarchs are those vampires who are too radical and too contemporary to be very energized by the Knights of Liberty\u2019s calls to establish reforms that were progressive two centuries ago, preferring either some sort of Fortier-style Camarilla with Republican Characteristics or even west coast style Anarch Free States and Anarch Communes (Communes could be a good way to fold in the history of utopian socialism and utopian religious communes in New England as well imo).<br /> <br /> All told this would give the kindred of New England a political landscape more analogous to a fusion of the English Civil Wars and American Revolution then decisively being the latter, but I think that makes things more interesting.<br /> <br /> Particularly given the added twist that as of the late 20th century both Montreal to the North and the Atlantic Northeast to the South were all Sabbat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T12:47:14-08:00","id":1502124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1502030#post1502030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that this idea of having the Tremere and Nosferatu power centers in New England overlap reminds me of is that idea from the original Clanbook Nosferatu that there was some sort of ongoing antagonism between Clans Nosferatu and Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had forgotten about that. It's certainly something that could be exploited in my scenario's Providence. It could be very interesting to see how a Tremere versus Nosferatu quarrel plays out because they each have very asymmetric strengths against each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1502030#post1502030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The early books seemed to play around with having the Tremere be the actual designated-villains of vampire (or at least Camarilla) society.</div> </div> </div> </div>There definitely was an emphasis on the Tremere being an antagonist in the early game when things were mostly concerned about what was happening inside the Camarilla. As the Revised era moved the sect conflicts between the Camarilla and Sabbat from a background element to the main source of conflict in games, it turned the Tremere more into the Camarilla's trump card against its enemies, and its earlier role as a source of conflict for other Camarilla PCs was neglected.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T13:21:49-08:00","id":1502132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1502037#post1502037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve also been chewing on Black Fox\u2019s posts about the Triad and I think it leads to some interesting ideas for New England as a setting. If I\u2019m making any incorrect assumptions in your reasoning Black Fox, please correct me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you have some of the general conflicts right, but it is not how I would have articulated it.<br /> <br /> I do agree that the early &quot;Ventrue domination&quot; of New England implies something of New England being yet another fief of Mithras at the time since it's most likely Ventrue from England populating the region in early colonial times. Likewise, both Roman Pendragon and William Biltmore are shown to having angered the English Venture and their overlord Mithras, and them coming to New England and overthrowing the New England Ventrue implies a continuation of that rivalry/enmity.<br /> <br /> But I'm not sure how much residual loyalty the contemporary Ventrue of New England would have to Mithras. First, those ties to Mithras would have been severed 200-250 years ago. There isn't anything in Dark Colony that implies Mithras has been attempting to regain control of the region. Sure an ST could add that, but I don't think it adds anything. The situation is already complex, and I would personally prefer the local Ventrue to now being on their own. Second, Mithras has been absent since WWII, and certainly did not play any role in the setting at the time Dark Colony was published. I think Mithras would have more immediate concerns on his mind than faraway New England though he would welcome a Ventrue return to power there.<br /> <br /> I do like the implied idea that almost all Ventrue of the New England area are probably of the lineage of Mithras, and that could give an extended family atmosphere of the clan in the region.<br /> <br /> As for the Triad, I hold certain opinions. The first is that the term &quot;Triad&quot; is never used by actual characters. People do know there is some sort of alliance between Pendragon and Biltmore, but Warwick is generally unknown and a mystery. His ties to the others are not known. The term is best used only by the ST to understand the secret alliance.<br /> <br /> Now both Pendragon and the Malkavian Prince of Boston are a kind of feudal overlord of other minor Princes (of their own clans), but that is not unusual within the Camarilla. Even Lodin had some authority over Modius in Chicago By Night albeit Modius did retain certain privileges. And Mithras as Prince of London acted in the same way to the other fiefs of England.<br /> <br /> But I don't think these two groups of struggling with one another. Although that is an option as you pointed out.<br /> <br /> Dark Colony has a habit of saying &quot;the Camarilla&quot; when they really mean &quot;the Inner Circle&quot;. That was quite frequent in early VtM sourcebooks. So I don't mind the idea that Pendragon is so dominating that the Justicars aren't really supervising him. Petrodon is all the way out in Seattle intriguing against the Anarchs, and Xavier wanders the Midwest and South, holding his conclaves in New Orleans. Both seem to ignore Pendragon and allow him to dominate New England, either because it is cut off by the Sabbat or that they don't want to rile the hornet's nest. But the idea of Princes upset over the Inner Circle interfering in their business was lead out in the earliest corebooks. With Pendragon we just have the idea that he's been more successful than most at ignoring them.<br /> <br /> Therefore, it might be interesting to present the opposition to Pendragon (through the Kindred of Liberty) as seeing the Camarilla not as a source of repression, but one of liberty that could be curtailing Pendragon's personal power. That might be a nice twist on the normal things. (Although I would probably change the name of the KOL as I don't think it's as clever of good as the writers of Dark Colony thought). It would be a good way of distinguishing the KOL from the Anarchs. The KOL is trying to figure out a way to strengthen the normal tools of Camarilla governance (Justicars, Archons, Conclaves) while the Anarchs do more typical Anarch things.<br /> <br /> So in terms of Camarilla politics, I would emphasize the resistance towards the alliance of Pendragon and Malkavians, while also emphasizing how the Triad's members are beginning to turn against each other, while everyone also fights the Sabbat, Lupines and other external enemies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1502037#post1502037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All told this would give the kindred of New England a political landscape more analogous to a fusion of the English Civil Wars and American Revolution then decisively being the latter, but I think that makes things more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an interesting way to put it, but I agree that it's not really a problem. I am actually not a fan of the idea of playing out a second American War of Independence in New England. Instead I would prefer a theme of the past haunting the present, and play up the historical memory of the region. Show how events that happened in the past are still reverberating today because of ongoing grudges, legacies, etc. So conflicts from the English Civil Wars, the Revolution, War of 1812, and so on are all good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-04T14:19:59-08:00","id":1502144,"title":"","content":"Here are my comments on the Malkavians.<br /> <br /> First, I really like the idea that Boston is somehow a base of Malkavian power in general. I don't know how appropriate that is for Boston, but someplace should be like that.<br /> <br /> Second, I also like the concept of a Welsh bard who somehow uncovered the truth about vampires and was embraced as a result, so William Biltmore is present. But I have him as the Prince of Boston, since he's not old enough to really be a power behind the throne. And if I want to move up the Triad to gaining power in the Revolution, he pretty much needs to become Prince of Boston at that time. He fled Britain to escape the wrath of Mithras, and as a result was a proponent of the American Revolution. As my own addition, I would also make him involved with a scholar of the Arcanum in Boston. Because the Arcanum Foundation House in Boston should be an important part of the setting, and I like the idea of setting up a stereotypical Anne Rice protagonist becoming involved with a character from the Talamasca. As a bard, Biltmore also fits that scholar archetype.<br /> <br /> Third, I am keeping Quentin King just because I like the name. Instead of making him a separate line from Biltmore, I made him Biltmore's grand childe (Skarvan is Quentin\u2019s sire and Biltmore\u2019s childe.) Rather than be from New York, Quentin was a police detective in Boston. As Biltmore is rarely seen and Quentin King handles almost all public tasks, many Boston Kindred feel he is the Prince. Biltmore\u2019s name is known from history and some older Kindred insist he is the actual Prince, but since they only see Quentin King there is considerable debate whether \u201cBiltmore\u201d still exists. Technically he's just Biltmore's Seneschal. But Biltmore doesn't see anyone except Quentin (I would probably make Biltmore's Derangement Paranoia). So many people call Quention &quot;Prince.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Six Knights were not embraced by Skarvan, but by Quentin himself, and is simply the name for his brood of childer (embraced for their rescue of him). They were part of Skarvan\u2019s herd though. Per Dark Colony, one of these is his chief aid in Boston, and the others are \u201cPrinces\u201d of minor cities. Rather than the silly names of Dark Colony, I would give them real personalities while keeping up the Arthurian resemblance. They\u2019ve adopted name associated with the Arthurian legend, but are not obvious about it - Hector, Lionel, Mark, Elaine, Lynette, and Percy. They do see Quentin as a kind of Arthurian figure destined to lead the Malkavians to greatness, or at least to make Boston a new &quot;Camelot&quot;. They're big fans of the Lerner &amp; Lowe musical.<br /> <br /> One major problem with the character of Quentin King is what exactly is his derangement. He seems to be fairly competent, having been a fairly good fighter of the Sabbat early on. He is also mentioned as being an outstanding art critic, and as a result has become a favorite of the Toreador. So whatever he has cannot be too debilitating. I think in Giovanni Chronicles IV, it adds he has the Derangements of Schizophrenia and Delusion, but I don't think that makes much sense. Despite the Arthurian aspects of his character, that did not come from him, but from the Six Knights.<br /> <br /> So I think I'd make him an example of intellectualization. His defense mechanism is to shift into abstract discussions and logic about unpleasant things instead of dealing with things emotionally. This has helped him succeed as a &quot;Prince&quot;, and it's one reason he's become an insightful art critic. The problem is that he is often cold and distant. And sometimes in times of great stress instead of acting decisively about a problem (like a Sabbat attack), he can waste time by over analyzing a problem instead of acting.<br /> <br /> I would not roleplay him so much like Mr. Spock but as Sherlock Holmes (which also harkens back to his background as a police detective.) I'd use a lot of Jeremy Brett's portrayal of the Great Detective as his roleplay inspiration. He doesn't have a Watson, but he does have the Six Knights.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3UOTIW83oXs\" data-code=\"3UOTIW83oXs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/3UOTIW83oXs/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> However, I do have one major problem. How can we deal with his weird connection to the Arthurian mythos and not make mention of a man with the last name of Pendragon? They have to be connected somehow. So far my best idea is that the Six Knights know that Arthur's (Quentin's) father Uther (Roman) is not a good king, and that Uther must go down before Arthur can become the &quot;true king&quot;. So they are manipulating events so that Quentin can eventually replace Pendragon as a the paramount figure in New England. The Six Knights tend not to think logically, but symbolically. <br /> <br /> Incidentally that would make the Welsh bard Biltmore into a Merlin figure. If we continue to go down that route, they might rename many vampire characters into an Arthurian figure if for some reason they think he fills that roll, and then try to manipulate that person into fulfilling their legendary destiny. That might lead to a fun scene where PCs hear these NPCs talking about &quot;Uther&quot;, &quot;Merlin&quot;, &quot;Mordred&quot;, &quot;Bors&quot;, etc. in a way that seems utterly confusing, not realizing they are speaking in code. It would make them seem more delusional than they truly are. But a canny PC might pick up on what they really mean.<br /> <br /> I have not played the Swansong computer game, but I hear it does provide a loose continuation of the Boston in Dark Colony. And by loose I mean while it acknowledges past canonical characters in its history, it pretty much throws all continuity out and starts completely from scratch. It is pretty much its own thing, and ignores any real heritage from Dark Colony. However, I would try to salvage any names and concepts that I find inspiring. Unfortunately, I don't there is much there for the Malkavians. The PC of Leysha and her relationship with her childe Halsey is OK, but rather generic for New England. That could be any Malkavian in any city. The same with making her a &quot;seer&quot;, her past unknown, and having her hail from a completely different city (Lyon, France). She could be acceptable provided we move her embrace to Boston and provide an actual background for her. Likewise, we can always keep the name of Richard Dunham and change his generation and lineage accordingly, perhaps make him the real sire of Leysha. But this is more easter egg type stuff than really utilizing the characters as depicted in the game. I'll mention Swansong more when I talk about some of the other clans.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T10:30:39-08:00","id":1502217,"title":"","content":"Speaking of the Malkavians, this reminds me of a thought I\u2019ve had about New England as a setting, which I mentioned in the intro post but might as well go into a bit more detail about here.<br /> <br /> So, to start off, this concept is heavily inspired by Alan Moore and his Lovecraft Cycle, but not just that. I\u2019d also say that things like Kubrick\u2019s adaption of \u2018The Shining\u2019 and the concept of Mysteries in Mage the Awakening have a role in forming this idea as well.<br /> <br /> Basically the idea is to have one of the plot hooks or mysteries of New England as a setting have to do with some sort of effect of the Collective Unconscious. That the region has some sort of cosmic rippling effect of narrative and symbolism which overlays eldritch secrets and mysteries. I mention it here because alongside the Nosferatu &amp; Tremere being served by the investigatory angles of this concept, it naturally flows through the Malkavians. In my mind, it would serve as a mysterious but evocative force, which helps to explain how Clan Malkavian maintains its prominence in Boston. That the Arthurian Mythos the clan uses, is itself one set of symbolic masks which serve the purpose of being more comprehensible representations of a larger phenomena which the Malkavians are sensitive too, in particular with Biltmore.<br /> <br /> One of the other reasons I\u2019m fond of the idea of an eldritch under current for New England, aside from feeling it compliments the region\u2019s feel fairly well, is that I also feel it provides a good basis for drawing other threads into play. It gives another reason for the occultists and theologians of the Sabbat in Montreal, the Arcanum, and sorcerers (&amp; Mages, if an ST feels so inclined) to be active in the reason and to instigate plot hooks which arise from the efforts to unravel the Mysteries found within New England.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T14:06:08-08:00","id":1502238,"title":"","content":"You might want to associate this mysterious power source to the legends of Norumbega, a legendary settlement once thought to exist somewhere in New England. It could be some extremely hard to find Umbral realm that is connected to New England (and effectively undiscoverable if the ST wants), with only these after effects noticed by some. Maybe knowledge of it was something that lost when the Croatan died so even Uktena and Wendigo Garou have very little knowledge of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T20:18:32-08:00","id":1502278,"title":"","content":"So, one of the other volunteers grew up in Boston, in the projects, and he says things like, &quot;Goin' to Dunkies&quot;: &quot;Bang a Uey&quot;: &quot;Where's my Khakis (Car-Keys)&quot;: &quot;The Bubbler&quot;. <br /> <br /> Also, there are lots of things that, well, could be New England, like Irish-tales or old Western-tales that could, fit into the NE-vibe. If you ran games based off of Grimm's Fairy-Tales, few would know what you were running. Maybe work a Disney-tale into there; I've always said that Snow White was a battle between two powerful-witches; just one managed to enchant seven Dwarves to her side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-05T21:42:35-08:00","id":1502282,"title":"","content":"Oh totally, we haven\u2019t gotten into too much detail with it but one of the back burners I\u2019ve had while chewing on ideas having to do with New England is what things look like for the other main game-lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-06T19:00:40-08:00","id":1502338,"title":"","content":"One issue with Dark Colony is that it does not do a good job distinguishing what are the different domains in the region. It has a lot of information about that, but it is scattered all over the place. There is no map showing them. And it lacks a good coterie chart of the different domains and how the Princes view each other. But this is information an ST definitely needs. So what happens if we look at a map, look up some quick populations in Wikipedia, and compare it to Dark Colony?<br /> <br /> Vampire Population per Dark Colony is 152. This represents the number of vampires the mortal area can \u201csupport\u201d, but then said the actual number can be higher! (How exactly can there be more vampires than the area can support?) Breakdown is Connecticut 35, Maine 20, Massachusetts 60, New Hampshire 18, Rhode Island 10, and Vermont 9. These are spread over 24 listed cities, but even here it says not all cities may have vampires. This number represents a higher population than it should be, so it likely presents both Camarilla and Sabbat vampires. So an ST has a lot of work to do to sketch this out, and the demographic data isn't very helpful.<br /> <br /> <b>Massachusetts</b><br /> The biggest metro are is, of course, Boston and would probably have around 50 vampires. Another 10 could be in the metro area of Worcester which is far enough away to be a distinct metro area and a sizable population. This perfectly matches Dark Colony's suggestion of 60.<br /> <br /> <b>Connecticut</b><br /> The 35 vampires of Connecticut broadly reflects what we would expect from the three metro areas. And let\u2019s face it, these could easily be considered to be one domain. Hartford - 12, Bridgeport / Stamford Metro - 9, and New Haven / Waterbury - 8. This is 29, near but under Dark Colony's figure. I'd probably just put the vampires of 30 and call it a day.<br /> <br /> <b>Rhode Island</b><br /> Rhode Island surprisingly should have more vampires than Dark Colony listed. Providence Metro could field 16 vampires. I think this includes Newport. Much like Connecticut, it's best just to see this as one domain.<br /> <br /> <b>Vermont</b><br /> Dark Colony is schizophrenic on this. While giving us 9 vampires, in the separate section of Vermont it implies vampires here are rare. The figure of 9 probably represents a Sabbat pack that visits the reason from time to time. We know from Rage Across New York that Vermont is home to the Morningkill Royal House of Silver Fangs, and they probably exterminate any vampires here who foolishly stay here. Vermont just lacks the population and density to house vampires per the conventions of VtM. It's largest metro area, Burlington, only has 200,000.<br /> <br /> <b>New Hampshire</b><br /> The four cities on New Hampshire are probably only around 5-6 vampires with only Manchester having more than 1 using the standard Camarilla one vampire for every 100.000 mortals in a metropolitan area. Even with one or two more Camarilla vampires out there, that means the other dozen or so must be Sabbat packs.<br /> <br /> Nashua/Manchester/ Corcord is best seen as one \u201cmetro\u201d zone based on population density, so is probably one domain. It can also be seen as the northern end of the Boston metropolitan area. Concord is actually a bit isolated from Nashua/Manchester, but it is the seat of Pendragon. So he\u2019s like the tip of the spear.<br /> <br /> <b>Maine</b><br /> \u200bMaine is another mostly rural and wilderness state with low population, but it has two metro areas. Portland could have 6 vampires and Bangor 2. Although canon says all of Maine is Sabbat, the Portland metro area is right next to the New Hampshire &quot;metro&quot; area with Portsmouth being a link. It's also not too far from Boston. So I would make Portland part of Pendragon's domain, and possibly make it one of the more contested areas between him the Sabbat. Bangor and backwoods Maine is Sabbat territory when they're not being killed by Lupines.<br /> <br /> So we have five domains total. Who are their Princes and about how many vampires should be in each domain?<br /> <br /> <b>Boston</b> - Biltmore/Quentin King is Prince. 50 vampires total, a large number of which should be Malkavians. I would make them the largest clan in the city. Because Quentin and even Biltmore are a bit non-traditional Malkavians, I'd use some variety in describing the other Malkavians. They would not be as loyal to Quentin as the Six Knights, but they like that one of their own is Prince.<br /> <br /> <b>Worcester</b> - Sir Praxis, one of the Six Knights per Dark Colony. The other Knights\u2019 principalities are likely better seen as personal domains held in the domain of the Prince of Boston. They aren\u2019t large enough to house multiple vampires and are either in or close to the Boston metro area. 10 vampires total. If we want to keep the area as a stronghold of Malkavian power, the Malkavians should be the largest clan here too.<br /> <br /> <b>Providence</b> - Warwick, though it is unclear whether this is publicly known, but if not who do people believe rules in Rhode Island? Obviously the Nosferatu dominate here, but I would also place the main Tremere chantry here although the chantry does have safehouses in other cities, particularly Hartford. 16 vampires total.<br /> <br /> <b>Hartford</b> - Upton Rowlands, officially \u201cPrince of New Haven and Hartford\u201d per the book. I think it sounds better than Prince of Connecticut. 30 vampires. The Ventrue are the largest clan here, although that clan does have members in a few other cities that have much less power than would usually be expected for them. In so far there is a traditional Camarilla domain in New England, it is here.<br /> <br /> <b>Southern New Hampshire/Portland</b> - Pendragon as &quot;Prince of Concord&quot;, which is more of a nominal title. He's prince of a lot more than just Concord. Other vampires in New England understand it is a courtesy title that does not reflect the actual reach of Pendragon's domain. There's around 12 or so vampires in this area. Most of them are probably Brujah loyal to Pendragon. Maybe half of them are his own brood or lineage while the others are just loyal followers. Pendragon\u2019s New Hampshire just does not seem large enough despite his personal importance in the region. A rural based vampire is fine, but the Brujah are not the most likely clan for it. So Pendragon\u2019s Brujah are probably crammed into the Nashua/Manchester area (or Portland) and merely visit the rest of the state\u2019s towns on occasion.<br /> \u200b<br /> \u200bThat is around 118 vampires - Camarilla and Anarchs. That leaves the other thirty to forty vampires in the region to be Sabbat who probably spend more time fighting Lupines than they do the Camarilla. When they do fight the Camarilla, Pendragon's group of Brujah warriors probably win more often than not, and they should be a very effective coterie of fighters.<br /> <br /> With this, an ST can start organizing his domains and building populations for each one. While the standard practice is to include all Camarilla clans in a single domain, I think it is best to keep some domains segregated. Only Boston is really big enough to hold all clans. Pendragon's domain should just have Brujah. Ventrue are mostly kept in Connecticut. Tremere should only be in Providence (under my chantry at Brown University idea) and Connecticut. Providence is the center of the Nosferatu, but they should probably be represented in other domains as well (though possibly in secret).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T14:41:40-08:00","id":1502540,"title":"","content":"Based on some of the earlier discussions in this thread, I have two minds about Providence off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> First I like the idea of Providence having a sort of parallelism with the Nosferatu and the Tremere - that it serves as a nexus between the regional networks of both clans, the former having its Web information network as part of the Triad and the latter having its Pyramid which provides thaumaturgical services to the region and presumably is more loyal to the Camarilla proper (in so far as the Camarilla aligns with House Tremere\u2019s interest of course). With that said, I think Providence might be an interesting case study for what a city might look like when it effectively has two Primogen instead of a Prince, with the Nosferatu under Warwick and the Tremere under the Regent and any conflicts having to be hashed out between these two. You could probably achieve a similar effect by having a put-upon Ventrue or Toreador be the formal prince but one who is ultimately powerless to oppose either Warwick or the Regent. Also given the general motif of mystery and relative isolation from the rest of the region, Providence might be a good place to drop some Settites if one wants to move them off of Cape Cod where Dark Colony deposits them.<br /> <br /> I agree that Boston should be the paramount city of New England and may well be the only city which hosts a member of every Camarilla clan. Something that Boston also makes me consider, and I\u2019m curious what your thoughts are on this Black Fox, is that Boston would also be the place to drop the Milliners. I do think that something interesting could be done with the implication in the Giovanni Clanbook that the Milliners were apart of a plot to kill JFK and Quentin King\u2019s Arthurian motif; something about the whole \u2018Camelot\u2019 element of the Kennedy mythos. Perhaps the Milliners are imagined as the Mordreds of the local Malkavians and maybe Francis Milliner actually does have ambitions to become the real power player in Boston and turn it into his own personal clan (Milliner clan, not Clan Giovanni) fiefdom. Going again into the idea I mentioned, inspired by the Lovecraft Cycle, of having some sort of Jungian Psychodrama play out throughout New England, I definitely think the colors of the Kennedy mythos could be brought into play there, perhaps with the Malkavians imagining a metaphorical (or real) plot by the Yankee Ventrue and the Milliners to usurp power from the Triad, as represented by their \u2018Arthur\u2019 Quentin. I\u2019d need some time to chew on it, but I think that their are legs there that could work, and would do well to include the mood of New England intrigues into the region.<br /> <br /> (Speaking of Mordred, that makes me wonder if the Morgana of the Malkavians would be the Tremere collectively or perhaps Dark Selina could be woven into serving that role).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-08T19:33:03-08:00","id":1502573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1502540#post1502540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that Boston also makes me consider, and I\u2019m curious what your thoughts are on this Black Fox, is that Boston would also be the place to drop the Milliners.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have the Milliners be the only members of Clan Giovanni in the city and the entire region of New England. In my own chronicles, the Milliners were embraced by the Dunsirn as that family is the one responsible for the North Atlantic interests of the Giovanni clan, and the Dunsirn bank in Scotland has a branch in Toronto. The Milliners represent their American operations. The Milliners are probably only 3-4 vampires total. In exchange for permission to embrace and create a little Giovanni clan fief in Boston, the Dunsirns provided Quentin King some boons, and the Milliners in Boston provide services for the Prince of Boston that members of the Ventrue clan would normally provide in a city. The Milliner support of the Malkavian Prince compensates for the enmity of the Ventrue and allows Biltmore and Quentin to sideline them. In exchange, they get a powerful Camarilla patron who allows them to grow and expand in a city as if they were a Camarilla clan.<br /> <br /> The Putanesca family of Clan Giovanni is based in New York City, and they constitute one of the Five Families in my chronicle's version of New York. They are the only other Giovanni nearby, and the two families sometimes squabble. Their spheres of influence are separate (the Putanesca are a criminal organization while the Milliners are respectable Yankee businessmen). But their interests sometimes cross over, and they fight over who has precedence and control.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I have all three of these families - Dunsirn, Milliner, and Putanesca - not be heavily involved in Necromancy. Although it is in-clan, it is something that needs to be intellectually developed and not &quot;natural&quot; as other Disciplines. Canonically both the Dunsirn and Milliner don't really use it, and Sicilian mobsters like the Giovanni shouldn't know too much of it either. There is probably an actual Giovanni family member somewhere that does know Necromancy and keeps tab of the all the other families in northeastern North America for Uncle Augie, probably based in New York City representing legitimate businesses connected to Venice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1502540#post1502540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think that something interesting could be done with the implication in the Giovanni Clanbook that the Milliners were apart of a plot to kill JFK and Quentin King\u2019s Arthurian motif; something about the whole \u2018Camelot\u2019 element of the Kennedy mythos. Perhaps the Milliners are imagined as the Mordreds of the local Malkavians and maybe Francis Milliner actually does have ambitions to become the real power player in Boston and turn it into his own personal clan (Milliner clan, not Clan Giovanni) fiefdom. Going again into the idea I mentioned, inspired by the Lovecraft Cycle, of having some sort of Jungian Psychodrama play out throughout New England, I definitely think the colors of the Kennedy mythos could be brought into play there, perhaps with the Malkavians imagining a metaphorical (or real) plot by the Yankee Ventrue and the Milliners to usurp power from the Triad, as represented by their \u2018Arthur\u2019 Quentin. I\u2019d need some time to chew on it, but I think that their are legs there that could work, and would do well to include the mood of New England intrigues into the region.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have wondered about that myself, but so far haven't come up with a good way to incorporate that. It seems an obvious thing to do, but it would also create a second Arthurian scenario that competes with the original one. Ultimately I think it is stronger than there is only one Arthurian figure that the Six Knights play into. But I'm sure they are amused by the Camelot myth surrounding the Kennedy family. Perhaps they secretly favor the Milliners just because of that even if it does not play a role into their own games and delusions.<br /> <br /> As for what Arthurian &quot;role&quot; they could be considered, I'm not sure. As a group that is from an Independent Clan but locally allied to Quentin (in my vision described above), the &quot;obvious&quot; place would be as one of Arthur's subkings in Britain who rule their own little kingdom but support the High King. That could be King Mark of Cornwall, King Lot of Orkney, King Leodegrance of Camelliard, and others I can't think of right now. I am thinking that Mark of Cornwall might be a good fit. The Tristan/Iseult romance might be simulated by a member of a Camarilla clan embracing a mortal Milliner, and causing the Milliners to go after that vampire. This would not happen normally, but the delusion of the Six Knights would cause them to try to make it happen. They could try and fail multiple times, still seeking the right person to manipulate into playing out that story. They might even try to do it on one of the PCs!<br /> <br /> If you are going to have a Mordred, my instincts would be that he should be Malkavian as Mordred is a blood relative and traitor. I think Effie Feng could fill that role if we consider her to be an actual Malkavian than one of the Gaki. Perhaps as a Malkavian not from the lineage of Quentin (like them), that makes her a &quot;bastard&quot;. The question is whether the Six Knights are trying to defeat Mordred and protect their king, or if their shared delusion means they MUST have a Mordred and are trying to secretly provoke Effie to treason so she can fill that role even while working to also thwart her.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1502540#post1502540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Speaking of Mordred, that makes me wonder if the Morgana of the Malkavians would be the Tremere collectively or perhaps Dark Selina could be woven into serving that role).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tremere would certainly fill the role of magician somehow, and since Biltmore is &quot;Merlin&quot;, then the Tremere have to be one of the antagonistic ones. I remember in some versions there are Nine Witches/Sorceresses of Caer Lloyw who terrorize Britain and are eventually slain by Percival. Since the Tremere are allies of the Ventrue and enemy to Boston, that might be a good reference. Wikipedia tells me Caer Lloyw is also called the Shining Fortress or could be Gloucester, so that would be a very oblique reference they could use for the Tremere that would confuse people. Especially since there is a Gloucester in Massachusetts that one of them holds as a fief under Quentin.<br /> <br /> Dark Selina (as some Sabbat Cardinal, although it is never explained how she entered that sect between Pendragon's attack and her arrival in New England) could be a good Morgan Le Fay figure - but she is supposed to be secret and I don't think the Six Knights should be that well informed. But perhaps they are aware from some defeated Sabbat that there is some female Cardinal in Maine, and that is the extent of it.<br /> <br /> There are many versions of the King Arthur legends, so I wouldn't bother trying to keep things consistent. The Six Knights likely make lots of changes and are indifferent to what versions of the many legends they use. They discard and go back to them as convenient. They are crazy after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  fixed some errors 07-11-2024, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T15:26:54-08:00","id":1502648,"title":"","content":"On the subject of New England, I had been doing some reading through the books to learn more about the First Sabbat Civil War, as it seemed like it was situated to be correlated with the United States Revolutionary Wars and their aftermath, so considering the events of SCW1 would be relevant to the discussion of New England. After doing said reading, I now thinks it\u2019s a \u201cyes and no\u201d situation.<br /> <br /> I do think that when one looks at the old Player\u2019s Guide to the Sabbat and it\u2019s history section, it\u2019s pretty clear that SCW1 is chronologically correlated with the US Rev. The premise seems to have essentially been this: the new world was first been the domain of the still largely Anarch-ic Sabbat, they had attempted to harness the power of the US Rev to further their own ends, but disorganization led them to succumb to infighting and ultimately cause more domains to be lost then were won. This doesn\u2019t seem to quite line up with what we end up learning about.<br /> <br /> For one thing, many US city books have the Camarilla have pretty much been there from word \u2018go\u2019, either with ambitious neonates/ancillae or roaming elders. However I do think that in many cases, in the earliest nights, we can assume that most of these are paper princes. Theoretically those early colonial domains had Camarilla princes but in effect the Sabbat packs who roamed the continent could do as they pleased, mostly with impunity. Montreal by Night (and New York by Night to an extent but it\u2019s a bit confusing to read) show that pretty well I think; although perhaps this is less universal and more meant to be an indictment on the French Camarilla as being ineffective in its colonial enterprises (which might also take on some interesting implications when considering PGttS\u2019s claim that France has the largest number of Sabbat in Western Europe). So we can imagine most of North America, with some exceptions, being de facto Sabbat albeit the occasional de jure Camarilla prince. Frankly I imagine that in these early nights, savvy would-be-princes would have an easier time calling themselves Anarchs or Autarkis and providing basic conveniences to wandering packs then claiming to be Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Mexico City by Night however I think has one of the more interesting cases to consider. If it is to be believed then it seems to me what was called the \u2018First Sabbat Civil War\u2019 was more a consequence of the political circumstances in New Spain more than anything else. After all, the SCW1 didn\u2019t seem to negatively impact the Shepherds of Caine plans for Montreal or Ecaterina the Wise\u2019s plans for New York City. Rather it seems that the infighting between Lasombra and Tzimisce and the struggles with Camarilla coups was more pronounced in New Spain more than anywhere else and that it was the conflicts that came from the difficulties their that spun out into sectarian conflict (at a greater scale then it had probably always existed at any rate). What MCbyN leads me to believe is that the SCW1 spun out from the infighting of Tzimisce and Lasombra elders vying over some of the only good population centers the Sabbat was entrenched in, in New Spain and having that spiral out of control throughout the sect as the leaders on either side use favors as well as political, spiritual, and blood influence to call in allies that ripples across the Americas (and presumably the Old World) and adapts itself to whatever the local conflicts of any particular region were. This only coming to an end when enough of these sectarian elders recognized the uptick of Camarilla entrenchment in the Americas, having for the last few decades been thinning the packs who previously placed limits on Camarilla growth, declaring that hostilities had to end and the sect had to regain its strength (as well as using the claims that disorganizatios, traitors, &amp; infernalists were at fault to help justify the development of a centralized path ecclesiarchy and the formation of an Inquisition).<br /> <br /> Now, going full circle, how do we relate this to New England? Well Dark Colony tells us that the Anglo-Camarilla Ventrue had power in the region, also as has been described in this thread. A coalition of clans, particularly Brujah, but including the Tremere begin to conspire to contest the Ventrue Old Guard for control of the region; and those Brujah &amp; Gangrel involved rally their broods and blood-kin for reinforcements, with a non-insignificant portion of those who show up being Sabbat who hope to work with the rebels to boot the Ventrue and then take power in New England as the Sabbat. We know that doesn\u2019t happen, and taking the adjustment that Black Fox has provided, we can imagine that it was Pendragon and the Triad who suspected/discovered the Sabbat plot in their midst and rooted it out before the packs could seize an advantage in the battle and overcome both the Triad and the Ventrue. (Alternatively perhaps it was Warwick &amp; Biltmore who outed the Sabbat conspiracy before it could take action).<br /> <br /> Something I\u2019m curious about though is how to interpret Dark Seline\u2019s role in such a turn of events. The implication I got from Dark Colony is that she wants to eventually see New England fall to the Sabbat so that she can carry out her vision. I can see two potential avenues for explaining this: 1. one of the other methuselah intervened to ensure the potential Sabbat coup was aborted, 2. Dark Seline allowed Pendragon to defeat the Sabbat (perhaps they didn\u2019t have the juice to outright succeed anyway) to build his credentials and allow him to weed out rivals until it was just a matter of him being the last thing between her and control over New England.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-09T15:30:17-08:00","id":1502649,"title":"","content":"One of the bug flaws in Dark Colony is the lack of individually described vampires. For a region that the book says might have around 150 vampires, the sourcebook describes 16 (counting the Six Knights as &quot;one&quot; character here). In contrast, Chicago By Night described over seventy for a metro area whose total population is likely less than the number in greater New England. I don't think Chicago By Night would be as fondly remembered if we only had the sixteen or so most important vampires described, and everything else was up to the ST.<br /> <br /> The Toreador clan is one of those that comes out the worse merely because we are given only NPC. I like Elsa Linden a lot, and that she is a &quot;Prince&quot; of a small artists colony town on Cape Cod far from the action is a great concept (it is easy to be a Prince when you are the only vampire, or it is only you or your childe). But the Toreadors of Boston that favor Prince Quentin King III are not described, nor are any elsewhere like those who would be part of the domain in New England. Or perhaps build on the idea that scattered throughout New England are small towns that have one Toreador residing in it, content to work on their art and only occasionally leave to meet in a clan Salon.<br /> <br /> We should have Toreador that cover the wide variety of arts and culture New England is known for - literature, philosophy, music, landscape paintings, and heritage conservation. There needs to be a good mix of high art and the low.<br /> <br /> Since the other clans are either feuding among themselves or each other, I would make the Toreador be a unifying presence for the Camarilla of New England. Individual Toreador might favor one Prince or the other, or even support the Anarchs, but I would have the clan be fairly civil to one another and the Toreador as a whole easily meet one time for a salon in Boston and next time at New Haven in some building at Yale. There could even be a lone Toreador who lives in Pendragon's domain, smitten by his old world cavalry officer dashing charm.<br /> <br /> While I would not hold VtM: Swansong as canon in my setting, I am more than happy to steal the names and basic concepts of many characters mentioned in it. So Hilda MacAndrews as a Boston Toreador can easily be taken as well as her childe Emem Louis, a jazz diva, would also fit in nice. Unfortunately there is not much described about them on the White Wolf wiki. Hilda was supposed to have been embrace in 1788 by a &quot;Marie-Marguerite Carreaux de Rosemont.&quot; So Hilda is probably one of the eldest native Toreador. Her sire's French name might indicate she was one of the early Montreal Camarilla Toreador who left early when she noticed it becoming too dangerous. Or perhaps there is a tie between Hilda's Scottish surname and the Toreador in Scotland and their &quot;auld ally&quot; France. That's a nice separate lineage of Toreador than the one Elsa Linden came from (as her sire is Annabelle from Chicago from the time she and her sire first arrived in America).<br /> <br /> But there could easily be another dozen or so Toreador. Because we all have our own ideas about good characters, I'll refrain from adding any of my own here. But if someone has a particular strong concept tied into the actual Boston/New England culture scene and history, it'd be welcome.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure about what I'd do about Sabbat Toreador. Most Sabbat in the region seem to be nomad packs who might be based out of Montreal or New York City. There is not really a major metro area that is clearly Sabbat since I think Portland, ME should be held by Pendragon even if it is contested. But the Bangor metro area can hold a few vampires, and it might be interesting to put a non-combat coven there that could explore the Sabbat Toreador depravity and act as a relative safe haven for packs to rest and recuperate there.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T20:19:57-08:00","id":1502727,"title":"","content":"The Nosferatu are one of the more detailed clans with three members. I think Warwick is a great character. And I love the imagery involved in Trajan's Web. Strand Masters. Veins. District Overseers. These are evocative terms. This is all great stuff. In my chronicles, while every Nosferatu warren has its local &quot;information system&quot; where they exchange gossip and some easy spying, there are also actual spy networks within the clan, and Trajan's Web is the largest and most successful. Trajan, Warwick's sire, is an incredibly important Nosferatu whose Web covers most of Europe and the Mediterranean beyond. Warwick is his top agent in North America who is slowly trying to bring in key Nosferatu in other North American cities as part of the Web. In my opinion, it's a shame other material did not do more with Trajan and his Web.<br /> <br /> Kurt Densch and Jara Drory on the other hand are perfectly fine NPCs, but not particularly interesting. Both are hurt by origins that start their story far from New England - in Berlin and Croatia respectively. This is a missed opportunity to bring in more local flavor to a regional sourcebook. Both characters could easily have been found in any other city. There is also a problem that their repressed romantic feelings for each other was already a motif in the earlier Chicago By Night books with the repressed romanticism between Khalid and Elzbieta. This also follows the quasi-romance between Kristian and Anastasia in Milwaukee By Night. I know that Nosferatu finding comfort in each other's arms, but still fearing rejection, is an attractive motif for people. But it was such an obvious and overused one that it isn't as special as the writers thought. These don't make the characters bad, but these kind of characters can be created by practically any ST, and Dark Colony needed more distinctive characters.<br /> <br /> Dark Colony does make mention of another character found in the original Clanbook: Nosferatu published around the same time. And this is Prudence Stone, an American colonist embraced around the Salem Witch Trials. Thought to be a witch because of her possessing the Second Sight, she was saved from execution by another Nosferatu named Osric. Prudence now lives in Boston and helps key the Sabbat at bay. Her oracular abilities also keeps the clan in North America apprised of danger, and is considered to be something of a clan matriarch.<br /> <br /> Prudence is a great character with lots of local flavor, and she should play an important role in New England. Her only mention in Dark Colony is that her acceptance of Warwick helped him establish the Web when he first arrived in New England. I would not make Prudence part of Warwick's Web, but she is his friend and ally. However, as a resident of Boston and not Rhode Island, she is better known to Quentin King, possibly even acting as a Primogen. And her warnings to Quentin - and perhaps Pendragon as well - is one reason they are able to prevent the Sabbat from overrunning the place.<br /> <br /> We know very little about her sire, Osric. But I would create an NPC with that name. Osric is a great Anglo-Saxon name, and this character can help establish the region's historical ties with England. He could have been embraced anytime between the Anglo-Saxon Conquest to the Norman Conquest. It'd be interesting to make him yet another refugee from Mithras, perhaps not an actual political opponent, but someone who wanted more freedom from Mithras's heavy hand over England. He would also have been a contemporary of the Tremere Madeline Coventry and some of the elder Gangrel. So we would have a Nosferatu with deep knowledge of the region going back to colonial times, who would have known all of the key players in history even those who have been destroyed or moved on, and could act along with some other elders as a possible resistance or independent power group from the Triad.<br /> <br /> In fact, if we want Warwick and his web to be secret, it could be Osric who is considered to be Prince of Providence, or at least the most well known name of a Nosferatu to the Kindred of the other clans. Osric might be more an elder statesman than day to day ruler than Warwick, firm allies, or they might even be opposed to a certain degree. The ST could do a lot.<br /> <br /> So that is five solid or great canonical NPCs, and at least three separate lineages that could sire vampires (including a PC). That is a good foundation for an ST to build additional Nosferatu around and fill out the clan.<br /> <br /> If there are other mentions of Nosferatu NPCs in the New England region, I'd be interested in reading about them to determine if I would want to add them in my version of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-10T20:35:33-08:00","id":1502728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1502648#post1502648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of New England, I had been doing some reading through the books to learn more about the First Sabbat Civil War, as it seemed like it was situated to be correlated with the United States Revolutionary Wars and their aftermath, so considering the events of SCW1 would be relevant to the discussion of New England. After doing said reading, I now thinks it\u2019s a \u201cyes and no\u201d situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one complicating issue is that the First And Second Sabbat Civil Wars are an artifact of the Revised era. Revised created more details that did not exist in the original Sabbat Books. For example, in Revised it is said Joseph Panders obtained recognition of his &quot;clan&quot; in the Third Sabbat Civil War. Originally it was mentioned as happening in the &quot;last Sabbat Civil War.&quot; So the details were more sparse when Dark Colony was written.<br /> <br /> So an ST can go in several ways on how they want to incorporate the Sabbat in early New England history. Although we should remember that the Sabbat at this time was not the increasingly centralized Sabbat after the second civil war ended around the 1920s. These Sabbat were probably much more like Anarchs although with a burgeoning Caine mythos centered around Vestgeir, and all packs were doing their own thing with only the Black Hand keeping the sect in tact.<br /> <br /> I see this time period as being one that is very fluid with any &quot;control&quot; being nebulous given the small populations involved. The Sabbat retreat to the New World was mostly disorganized, but the Camarilla's was more planned. As a result, the Camarilla took control fairly quickly. Much of the writing about the Sabbat controlling Colonial America is probably best seen as in-character propaganda.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1502648#post1502648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I\u2019m curious about though is how to interpret Dark Seline\u2019s role in such a turn of events. The implication I got from Dark Colony is that she wants to eventually see New England fall to the Sabbat so that she can carry out her vision. I can see two potential avenues for explaining this: 1. one of the other methuselah intervened to ensure the potential Sabbat coup was aborted, 2. Dark Seline allowed Pendragon to defeat the Sabbat (perhaps they didn\u2019t have the juice to outright succeed anyway) to build his credentials and allow him to weed out rivals until it was just a matter of him being the last thing between her and control over New England.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark Selina is a confusing character. It's not clear to me whether she is now awake or still in torpor. Everything about her screams Sabbat, but the implied backstory with Pendragon seems to indicate she was not Sabbat at the time of his embrace. Otherwise why would Pendragon have become so accepted in the Camarilla domains? So did Dark Selina somehow join the Sabbat after she was awakened from torpor? If so, how did she join and make her way to the New World? Or is Dark Selina somehow still in torpor, but masquerading as some Sabbat Cardinal and manipulating the Crimson Tide (which is never actually described as the only Sabbat we're given is of two other packs). It is entirely possible that Dark Selina was meant as an example of one of those string pulling Methusalehs who is beyond sect politics, and is manipulating vampires of both sects to do what she wants. It's just that her vision of future vampire society makes her see the Sabbat as a more useful tool, easier to manipulaye.<br /> <br /> I think an ST would first have to determine the exact status and role of Dark Selina, and then determine how that affects the Sabbat.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-11T23:47:35-08:00","id":1502812,"title":"","content":"The Venture like the Toreador only have one NPC detailed in Dark Colony.<br /> <br /> Upton Rowlands is a Ventrue controlling Yale and the social club the Gemini League. I really like this character more than I should. He's one of the relatively few Ventrue who actually fit the corebook clan description of Ventrue embracing within their own mortal family. He is also a great concept as someone with deep ties to the American elite as a result of his influence in Yale. I absolutely make him the controller of the Skull &amp; Bones secret society, and he controls a lot of influence from that. He only embraces from two groups - his own family and that society. (I now try in my chronicles to not use real world people or organizations as being vampires or vampire controlled, so I would prefer to replace the name &quot;Skull &amp; Bones&quot; with some ersatz replacement - but I don't think I can come up with a better name!)<br /> <br /> Another important concept is the Gemini League. While it is supposed to resist the influence of the Web and extend Ventrue power, we're not exactly told what it is. The best I can tell is that the name Gemini is in reference to the two clans of Ventrue and Tremere (though this may not be the case). In my chronicles, I have the Gemini League be an important social club/fraternity throughout New England that Upton controls, much like Skull &amp; Bones. However, Ventrue influence and control is not known and thus serves as a secret means to expand the clan's power. The Tremere are aware of it and are also working within it to recruit mortal allies, contacts, retainers, and even recruits like the Ventrue. The two clans cooperate while also being rivals. Too bad Warwick already knows about it, making it a tool of limited influence.<br /> <br /> Upton Rowlands is a great concept, but there should be a dozen or more Ventrue in the setting so we have a huge gap. Any ST will need to close that gap. Obviously we can add a few more Ventrue who are also members of the Rowlands family or members of Skulls &amp; Bones. But we also need other Ventrue unrelated to him.<br /> <br /> We can pull some names at least from Swansong. That can give us the Underwood dynasty of the Venture (Berel and James), and Hazel Iverson as another New England Ventrue; all of whom are in Boston. So we can probably make them as the descendants of the Ventrue who lost control of Boston after the American Revolution. If they are associated with a university, it'd be Harvard and not Yale. STs would need to develop them to make them interesting concepts.<br /> <br /> They probably resent Upton Rowlands as being the clan leader of the region, and seethe that they are kept out of power in Boston. In my conception of the setting, they are also beset by the Milliners of Clan Giovanni. They publicly support Upton and his attempts to reclaim power for the Venture clan, but don't actually want him to succeed. What they really want is to regain power in Boston and become superior to Rowlands dynasty. Upton, of course, realizes this and tries to manage the situation as best he can.<br /> <br /> As I mentioned before, I have not actually played Swansong and only know these references from the White Wolf Wiki. It's likely there are some additional Ventrue mentioned that could help an ST quickly create some additional vampires of the clan, but I just don't know what they are.<br /> <br /> Overall, I would keep the Ventrue in Boston rather small. The Malkavians and their allies want to keep the Ventrue weak there. But in Connecticut they should be the largest clan, the sole remaining place of Ventrue power throughout the Eastern Seaboard since the rest of New England is dominated by other clans, many other cities are controlled by Sabbat, and many important Ventrue in DC are actually Lasombra. As such, I'd make Upton Rowlands an extremely important Ventrue in North America especially as he exercises control over Skull &amp; Bones. In my setting, he's one of the two most important Ventrue on the continent with only Horatio Ballard in Chicago being his equal. Upton is an important figure not just in New England, but elsewhere. In fact, one can make the argument that he is ironically more important on a continental scale than he is in New England itself.<br /> <br /> Also mentioned earlier, I would want another Ventrue as a Barnabas Collins type of vampire somewhere in New England.<br /> <br /> Over all, I still find the clan fairly underdeveloped compared to what I think it should be, especially in Connecticut. These Ventrue should be the ultimate Daughters of the American Revolution, blue blood, old money, American Ventrue with roots back to the Mayflower. There needs to be deep history here, rivalries between dynastic families, and plenty of feuds and intrigues especially between the Ventrue of Connecticut and others elsewhere in the region. Out of the 30 or so Kindred of Connecticut, I might make 8-10 of them Ventrue which is a large percentage, but it mostly makes up for their small numbers elsewhere. I'd make the Ventrue in Boston one of the smaller clans in that city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T17:26:59-08:00","id":1502900,"title":"","content":"The Brujah are another clan with three described NPCs. That includes Roman, his spymaster Jacques Sirque, and Pug Jackson.<br /> <br /> The Brujah are traditionally depicted as the largest clan in the Camarilla (and indeed among all vampires regardless of sects), and it makes sense to do the same in New England. With an estimated population of around 120 Camarilla vampires, we could have as many as 24-30 Brujah in total. These would have to be divided among three main groups - Camarilla Brujah loyal to Pendragon (predominantly in his southern New Hampshire-Portland domain), Camarilla Brujah that are anti-Pendragon, and Anarchs. Let's look at each of these groups in detail.<br /> <br /> Pendragons's New Hampshire/Portland domain probably holds between 6-12 vampires, the vast majority Brujah because he needs them to fight the Sabbat. And if this is the guy who dominates much of New England, we could be talking about half of all Brujah being loyal to him. However, we know very little about his followers. We know Pendragon is a natural warrior and leader, and Jacques is a respectable spymaster. But all his other followers are nameless goons. In the single &quot;story&quot; adventure of Dark Colony, his Brujah followers aren't even given names - just identical stats as &quot;Redcoats&quot; divided between &quot;Lieutenants&quot; who lead 2-3 &quot;Dogs&quot;. These aren't characters, but orcs - disposable goons that only exist to fight the PCs and other NPCs and to be killed by them.<br /> <br /> I'll probably have one of the squads routinely visit Boston and Worcester, to rest and relax from fighting Sabbat, to make sure that vampires don't put too much pressure on the mortal population of New Hampshire, and Portland, and just to keep tabs on his ally, Biltmore. Another squad sometimes raids northern New Hampshire or Maine to kill Sabbat. The Prince of Boston just deals with these rotating Brujah visiting his domain because it is worth it to keep the Sabbat away. And on some occasions, a war coterie leaves Boston to help Pendragon out. Likewise, Pendragon is helped by various individual Gangrel who dwell in the New England woods and hate Sabbat too.<br /> <br /> In order to keep Brujah casualties to a minimum despite them constantly fighting Sabbat, I would say that Pendragon utilizes the visions of the Nosferatu Prudence Stone in Boston to arrange ambushes. Biltmore passes on that information to Pendragon, and Pendragon exploits this knowledge. Many times a Sabbat pack attempting to perform the Creation Rites and create a large number of vampires are attacked in the middle of it, leading to the loss of an entire pack or much of it. They lose a lot of members this way, and they don't understand how Pendragon manages to pull off these ambushes. Is there a traitor within the Sabbat? Of course, Prudence Stone cannot produce these visions upon command, which frustrates Pendragon. But he exploits them when she does produce one.<br /> <br /> Now I do like the general idea that Pendragon has divided his followers into small tactical units (squads) of 3-4 vampires who can act in military fashion. One squad could patrol New Hampshire, another squad Portland, and another squad the rest of New England to do his bidding there when necessary, That would be a dozen Brujah with the potential of even adding another squad. They can rest, enjoy life, and then go out and fight Sabbat when needed.<br /> <br /> The problem is that these Brujah need to be real characters, not orcs. The most important of which is motivation - why they are fighting for Pendragon to begin with. How has he kept their loyalty? We know from his background that Pendragon once attempted to conquer Britain. (I would interpret his name &quot;Pendragon&quot; not to be his mortal family name, but his vampire name / nickname as a result of his wanting to depose Mithras and rule the island. It might have even started as a mocking name given to him by his enemies before being embraced by him.) By the description of Britain in the first World of Darkness book, the Brujah were not a powerful clan on the island. The Ventrue, Tremere, and Toreador were the important clans. Other than in Liverpool, the Brujah were weak - typically used as &quot;patsies&quot; by one of the other clans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T17:27:39-08:00","id":1502901,"title":"","content":"So we could construct a story where Pendragon is seen as a great Brujah hero in Britain, someone willing to defy Mithras and the three powerful clans in a brave, but ultimately doomed, attempt to promote Brujah interests. While Pendragon had to flee into exile, his name is still highly regarded by the clan in Britain. Thus his war is seen as yet another attempt at a creation of a Brujah utopia again cruelly crushed by the hated Ventrue and Tremere. It is not material whether Pendragon ever bothered to articulate any kind of just rule as opposed to his own pride and ambition. What matters was his brief period of glorious success and eventual escape to New England. He could be seen as a Napoleonic type figure except that his exile was not done by his foes, but engineered by himself as an escape.<br /> <br /> It's even likely that Pendragon and Jeremy MacNeil knew each other very well. MacNeil might even have been a follower of Pendragon at one point. They are both charismatic warriors, but Pendragon is much more an organized soldier than the highland warrior MacNeil could ever be. Plus Pendragon is still a product of the English aristocracy and could never accept someone like MacNeil as a true equal. Eventually their divergent personalities and outlooks would drive them apart sometime after the American Revolution. MacNeil considers Pendragon to be a traitor to the cause. Pendragon thinks MacNeil is a romantic fool.<br /> <br /> This allows us to have Pendragon have both an original coterie of devoted Brujah followers who came with him to America, and a source of new British Brujah replacements who &quot;grew up&quot; on stories about him. Of course, besides British Brujah, I would also have some American Brujah who are their childer. Eventually Pendragon's followers are going to create new vampires to replace their losses and expand power.<br /> <br /> I also want to make some other comments on Pendragon. First, while I like the idea that Pendragon was a British officer in the War of Spanish Succession, I think his embrace in 1703 is a little too early. The British had not fought many battles by that time. It was limited to several successful (and brief) sieges along the River Meuse from Benlo to Liege. Not much opportunity for a man to truly make his name like Roman supposedly did. And rather far from Zurich where he was embraced by Dark Selina. Instead, I prefer the idea that Roman accompanied the British Army down south and fought in the Battle of Blenheim, the most decisive battle in the War of Spanish Succession, in August 1704. That would allow Roman to have spent time learning how to fight wars under the Duke of Marlborough (considered to be one of the great military geniuses of the time - and an ancestor of Winston Churchill), win renown in a famous battle, and be much nearer to Zurich which he could have conceivably visited at the end of the campaign season in the winter of 1704/1705. Second, I am rather pedantically bothered by his name &quot;Roman&quot;, which would be an unusual name for an Englishman for this time period. I would probably change is to the similarly sounding, but more English, name of &quot;Rowland&quot; should I ever run a chronicle here. But I'll continue to keep it as Roman for this thread so I don't confuse anybody.<br /> <br /> Pendragon's long term goal is to defeat the Sabbat of New England, crush the Anarchs, and set himself as Prince in a unified Dominion of New England by holding a Conclave that endorses his rule. Then he'll drive the Sabbat out of New York and add that to his domain, maybe even retake the entire Eastern Seaboard. Eventually use that prestige to become Brujah Justicar, and use that position to help him achieve his real ultimate goal - return to Britain and establish his rule there. Pendragon is extremely unlikely to achieve all his goals, but he could very well achieve some of them.<br /> <br /> These two posts are already long, so I'll continue my thoughts on the other Brujah of New England later.\u200b<br /> <br /> EDIT: Stupid me. I just realized that the Rowland name is already used for the Ventrue dynasty of Upton Rowlands. It's probably why the name stuck in my head. It's likely too confusing to have a Rowland Pendragon and Upton Rowlands. I'll have to find another name I like. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  I just realized I was stupid... 02-15-2023, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-13T18:40:10-08:00","id":1502980,"title":"","content":"What about those Brujah not supporting Pendragon? If we say that Pendragon has the loyalty of around half the Brujah of New England, the other half is in opposition divided between Camarilla and Anarchs I'd probably make one of these groups larger than the other, the larger one being whichever the ST wants. <br /> <br /> While it is not clear in Dark Colony whether Pug Jackson is an Anarch, or just a Brujah with lots of connections to Anarch, I'd make him the de facto Anarch leader. He would lead the Anarchs in Boston. I'd also have a much smaller group of Brujah Anarchs in Connecticut, maybe just 2-3 total.<br /> <br /> Most of the anti-Pendragon Camarilla Brujah would also be in Boston/Worcester, but I'd still have at least 1-2 in Connecticut, maybe depending on how the other Clans fill out that domain. But given the Ventrue dominance there and the many Brujah elsewhere, this is clearly the spot where they are needed the least.<br /> <br /> I imagine various Brujah could trespass in Rhode Island, but given a presence of Tremere there (in my chronicles, but not canon) and a massive Presence of Nosferatu, they don't last long unless they secure an invite.<br /> <br /> I don't know if there are any prominent Brujah mentioned in Swanswong that I'd be tempted to steal for my version of the setting. But we definitely need more names and concepts. Those we can't steal, we'll have to invent on our own.<br /> <br /> I'd make sure that we'd have a wide variety of potential Brujah lineages for the Brujah here to showcase how many Brujah have been in and out of New England over the many years. Pug Jackson could obviously represent the lines of either MacNeil or Foccart, so I'd make sure the other one was represented as well. I'd also pick a few Brujah lines from vampires who did not come from Britain as they would not be so enamored by the exploits of someone like Pendragon. Foccart came from France so perhaps there were other French Brujah as well. We could also utilize the Dutch from New Amsterdam in colonial times. Or use the mass waves of emigration that arrived later that could act as cover for the arrival of Old World vampires first arriving. With New York in Sabbat hands, Boston might have been a much safer and preferred arrival port from the perspective of Camarilla vampires. Obviously there would be a huge number of Irish, but I'm not acquainted with a strong Brujah presence there. I think smaller, though still noticeable, immigrant groups came from Germany and Italy and Russia (Jews more than ethnic Russians). I think there's also been some noticeable immigrants from the Christian populations of the Ottoman Empire (Armenians, Lebanese, and Arabs). I also know that Boston had one of the larger Chinatowns in America in the 19th century, but that is a dubious origin for vampires in the WoD unless the ST has replaced the &quot;Kindred of the East&quot; with actualKindred. That could generate a good mix, even if it is only as someone's sire who has since moved on. (This could be used for other clans as well, but I think it'd fit the idea of Brujah coming and going, and providing an easy explanation for Brujah not interested in Pendragon is he is supposed to be a big icon among the British Brujah.)<br /> <br /> I'd also make sure to showcase the changing nature of &quot;revolutionary&quot; Boston that attracted this type of Brujah or that one as time went by. Boston has a lot of events that can contribute to its &quot;radical&quot; heritage - the Revolutionary era, the Abolitionist movement, anti-Catholic riots, the Anarchism of Sacco &amp; Vanzetti, Vietnam era protests, etc. Placing vampires in the right historical local context is very important to ground a setting in its region. Have vampires who lived through and participated in these events when they were mortal. It's also a huge intellectual capital of the United States because of its famous universities, and those would attract a different sort of Brujah. Maybe there is a Brujah like Critias in Boston, but who represents Italian scholarship from its medieval universities or the Italian Renaissance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T15:15:28-08:00","id":1503170,"title":"","content":"Talking about Roman \u2018Rowland\u2019 Pendragon in the English context got me to think about another British Brujah who might be interesting in this context, Robin Leeland, the Vampire Robin Hood. Now honestly as goofy as that idea might be in isolation, it\u2019s ultimately no worse then having a character called \u2018Roman Pendragon\u2019 and honestly Robin Hood is too juicy a figure not to include influence of in the Brujah of Britain imo. We know that Robin is the progenitor of a whole strain of Brujah Anarchs that migrated into the new world, including anyone who could claim a heritage through either Marguerite or Crispus (who, regardless of whether or not one chooses to believe the vampire is the historical Crispus Attucks, he should probably get a mention in the vampiric history of Boston). Robin is described as still being active in Europe, having popped up around the 11th century, and being focused on undermining the Elders of Europe and the Brujah Old Guard. He might demonstrate another ideal of English Brujah culture that may still exist within New England - the nomadic poacher and squatter who snubs illegitimate authority and survives via cunning, martial ability, wilderness survival skills, and camaraderie. I\u2019d be tempted to include some Anarchs in New England of that vein, perhaps drawing some sort of through line of tactics from the old Anarch Poachers of the Middle Ages to the Weather Underground/SLA type Anarchs of the 60s/70s. <br /> <br /> Something else I noticed in World of Darkness is that the Brujah are considered to be the vampires who first backed the creation of the Parliament as a means of counter-balancing the central authority of London. While Pendragon himself is far too young to have been involved, that might serve as a form of historical legacy he can invoke to justify his authority alongside the triad, representing a (relatively) more open rule outside of the stranglehold of Ventrue hegemony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T18:38:41-08:00","id":1503197,"title":"","content":"The line of Robin Leeland should definitely be represented in New England. He was the sire of Marguerite Foccart who was in turn the sire of Crispus Attucks. I suggested Pug Jackson could be changed to be the childe of either them or Jeremy MacNeil. If he is, then he could sire more of the line. But if he's not, then I agree that the ST should create others from that line.<br /> <br /> It's not clear when MacNeil, Foccart, and Attucks left Boston. They may have left at different times. I believe Marguerite returned to France during its Revolution so she likely left very early - perhaps right after the War of Independence ended or even on some French ship during the late stages of the war. <br /> <br /> Crispus was involved in the Underground Railroad, and while he likely travelled the Eastern Seaboard a lot, he may have kept Boston as the home he always returned to until after the Civil War. If we have Crispus stay in Boston until the Civil War - perhaps even up to 1895 when Operation: Longbow happened (although in my scenario, 1895 does not represent a new invasion of British Kindred, just the members of the Triad becoming more ruthless and domineering) which caused him to flee. In that case, Crispus might have sired multiple childer that stayed in Boston, though not all of them need have survived. If so, it is possible that Crispus knew and worked alongside Quentin King and the Six Knights, perhaps even helping them depose and destroy the Tremere Prince of Boston, Baladin. That was probably around 1825 or so when Quentin became Prince, as Dark Colony says Baladin arrived in 1795 and feuded with Coventry for around 30 years.<br /> <br /> But for MacNeil we're just told that he was forced westward by Ventrue expansion. As we know from Dark Colony, there certainly wasn't a Ventrue expansion in New England so it is possible MacNeil left on his own before being pushed out in the Midwest. In an earlier thread on Anarchs, I mentioned that it makes sense that MacNeil would have known Kyle Strathcona, and that they may have quarreled when Kyle was member of the Camarilla first and later Sabbat. If MacNeil didn't leave New England on his own accord, perhaps it got too hot for him with Sabbat attacks. But I think it more likely MacNeil wandered someplace that was more exciting. He's not mentioned at ever being in Chicago, but perhaps he made his way to Ohio or Detroit or St Louis as they expanded. Of course, in my scenario moving Pendragon (and the other members of the Triad) to New England much earlier so they could participate in removing the Ventrue from power during the War of Independence, it might have been Pendragon who &quot;encouraged&quot; MacNeil to leave, seeing him as a threat to his own plans for power.<br /> <br /> I think there's a lot of options for STs to play with in filling out the details for their specific chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T19:24:32-08:00","id":1503201,"title":"","content":"I think I covered all the Camarilla clans. And while I will eventually get to the Sabbat, I want to use this post for ideas on &quot;seasoning&quot; the setting in general with colorful NPCs. This isn't necessarily clan based. It's just concepts in general that could be interpreted using various clans. I see this as having too components. The first is just local concepts that should be included in the chronicle simply because it is in New England. The second are the exotic vampires that shouldn't be there (like a Muslim ghazi, African witch doctor, or a Romanian child in Chicago), but provide interest.<br /> <br /> So here are some character concepts I thought should have been included in Dark Colony, but which I don't remember seeing.<ul><li>An American soldier from the War of Independence or the French &amp; Indian War</li> <li>A Hessian mercenary</li> <li>A New England lawyer-politician in the vein of John Adams or Daniel Webster</li> <li>A Transcendentalist writer/philosopher</li> <li>A Boston abolitionist</li> <li>Someone involved with the Hartford Convention near the end of the War of 1812</li> <li>Someone involved with the New England shipping/fishing/whaling industry</li> <li>Someone who can represent the Boston Irish, although perhaps not a stereotypical police officer or politician</li> <li>Someone representing the financial and insurance industry</li> <li>Someone representing the old industries of textiles, shoes, clocks, leather, flour, etc. that provided the basis for the early industrial economy</li> <li>Someone representing the new industries of medical research, computers, scientific instruments, robotics, pharmaceuticals and other high value/highly educated workforce</li> </ul><br /> I know others will have lots of their own ideas. But characters like this would help ground the NPCs to the local setting. I find too many NPCs in vampire city books tend to be generic that could be anywhere.<br /> <br /> While I like most of the NPCs to be native to the region (somewhere around 2/3 would be ideal), not all vampires can or should be native. But here I think it is important they add something to the setting. I am much more accepting of really old vampires not being native because 1) vampires had to come from somewhere else first, 2) it helps cement the idea that vampire elders on their own society distinct from the mortal world, and 3) provocative characters can hold the imagination of the players.<br /> <br /> There are two ways of adding such characters. The first is simple - create your own. We all have our own ideas so I won't waste people's time describing my own. But the second is to look for underappreciated and minor canonical characters already introduce whose destinies are unknown. The Dark Ages By Night books are a good example. A lot of them have good characters who were easily overlooked because they were not the main drivers of the chronicle plot.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't pick the most popular or metaplot-involved characters. Lucita, Anatole, and Mary the Black don't need to end up here. But what about someone like Nerea of Spain in Constantinople By Night? She's given no destiny. She's just a thirty year old Brujah Neonate who fled a blood hunt in her native Barcelona for killing her sire/lover in a fit of jealous anger, and regrets it very much. It's implied she senses doom coming to the city and intends to go down in flames with it as atonement for the murder she regrets. But at the same time, she also dreams of finding true love again, so her destruction is not assured. What happens if she is now a thousand year old elder living in Boston. She's survived several conquests of Constantinople, seen the creation of the Camarilla and Sabbat, and travelled the Mediterranean world. Sensing the coming of the Second World War, she made her way to Boston to survive. She is still searching for a new true love.<br /> <br /> Or maybe the Lasombra Magdalena Castelucci Borcellino from Jerusalem By Night. The daughter of a Venetian shipping dynasty with great social skills and a natural at intrigue who was embraced by Narses. She eventually returns to Italy and becomes a successful player of politics, but disappears around the time Gratiano diablerizes the Antedeluvian. But there are rumors she has survived as one of the Lasombra anti-tribu. What happens should see be one of the Kindred in Connecticut? Maybe she decided she would like to pit her skills against a real challenge - the members of the Triad and especially the spymaster Warwick. Maybe she harbors resentment against the Giovanni because of their power in her native Venice, and she wants to pick apart their promising acquisition of the Milliners while thwarting the Putanesca of New York. Or perhaps she finds it delicious to help a prominent Ventrue dynasty (the Lasombra's old rival), and by helping them put them in her debt. What should happen if the Sabbat ever learn that one of the Lasombra anti-tribu is nearby? I think it could add a lot.<br /> <br /> Of course, STs might not find my picks interesting and have their own candidates. And that's great. I just think there are some hidden gems out there in the older Dark Ages books that might make interesting characters if you transplant them to New England. Build on these interesting, but neglected characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-15T21:52:38-08:00","id":1503204,"title":"","content":"One thing I liked in Chicago By Night, that is absent in Dark Colony, was the \u201clayering\u201d of the Jyhad. You had the obvious conflict of the Prince and the Anarchs. There was also the conflict between the Prince and Primogen. Then the manipulations of the two Methusalehs. But individual vampires also had their own concerns about the Antedeluvians, the Jyhad, worries about Gehenna, interests in Golconda or diablerie, and so on. Dark Colony lacks this complexity. Almost everything centers on the conflict between the \u201cRedcoats\u201d and the \u201cKindred of Liberty\u201d with some additional high level conflict between the patrons of the Triad (who are not even in New England). There is very little else other than the struggle between the Sabbat and Camarilla, and even that is tied to the Methusalehs behind the Triad.<br /> <br /> So I think we need to add these extra levels. One part of this is to consider the possible roles of the Gehenna Cults (from the Elysium sourcebook) in New England (though this is not the only way, there should be more). <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493307-gehenna-cults-of-elysium\">I had done a thread earlier on this, but only using possible examples from Chicago By Night.</a> I\u2019ll now consider it in the context of Dark Colony. The paucity of NPCs means we have less to go by, but let\u2019s see what we could do.<br /> <br /> First up is the \u201cEden\u201d social club which hides the cults of the Royal Edenic Groundskeeper and the Imperial Order of the Master Edenic Groundskeeper. None of the NPCs in Dark Colony seem to make good members of the actual Gehenna cults themselves, but I could see elders of both Boston and Connecticut being members of \u201cEden\u201d. I like the idea that potentially opposing Kindred like Quentin, Upton, and Elsa Linden might be members of the same social club that only hosts the social elite (high status and their court favorites) of the New England Camarilla. Perhaps they even \u201ccross\u201d borders so to speak to appeasr at alternating Elysium events, this one at Yale, next time at Harvard, afterwards the Boston Lyric Opera, then some Cape Cod resort, and so on. It would give opportunities for these Kindred in different domains to meet and interact. Maybe even Roman Pendragon shows up from time to time. And if an ST wants to introduce an actual member of one of the Gehenna cults (perhaps merely visiting to the region), then they could easily do so.<br /> <br /> Likewise, I don\u2019t see candidates for the Way of the Ancient Lawgivers. Nobody seems particularly interested in the First City, the Antedeluvians, or Gehenna. It is something to keep in mind for an NPC created by the ST. But I would also say that it is not necessary to try to include every Gehenna Cult in a chronicle. They should be selected judiciously so it is OK if this cult is ignored entirely.<br /> <br /> I mostly feel the same about the Servitors of Irad, but with one possible exception. I think Pendragon himself might make an interesting member. Unlike the Lawgivers, the Servitors do not exclude Brujah. And many of Pendragon\u2019s actions fit the profile of the Servitors. He wages war against the Sabbat and Anarchs just like the Servitors would. He is also an extremely divisive figure within the Camarilla, and the Servitors want to keep the elders divided. One can even argue his role in \u201cdestroying\u201d Dark Selina would be something the Servitors would approve of, and it could have attracted their attention to him. Furthermore, even if Pendragon is a member, it is not necessary for him to be a <i>sincere</i> member of it. He might have just seen it beneficial as a way to garner support.<br /> <br /> If this is to be more than just trivia though, and something that drives the setting and affects the PCs, we might want to expand the organization. Giovanni Chronicles IV introduced the Cappadocian/Giovanni vampire Marianna in Boston. Perhaps that gives Pendragon an interest in protecting her or acting revenge upon the Giovanni Clan. Or perhaps one of the pretexts the Triad joined together is that another one or all of them were members of the Servitors. Or at least one other (perhaps ST created) NPC in the region is also a member, and that makes Pendragon and her secret allies. <br /> <br /> If we go with the earlier example of Magdalena Castelucci Borcellino being in the setting, perhaps she is a also a Servitor of Irad. Maybe she believes Lasombra is not destroyed, and he humored Gratiano to test him. Gratiano failed, and he found only an empty tomb. He and his ilk and therefore marked for destruction no matter how powerful the Sabbat Lasombra seem. Her intrigues against the Triad are really directed only against Warwick (and perhaps Biltmore). When she intrigues against Pendragon, it's more in the sense of harassing a friend, not trying to stop him. Pendragon tolerates it because he knows at some point he must turn against his erstwhile allies.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think the remaining three Gehenna cults - Twilight Cult, the Ninth Wave, or the Cult of Enlightenment have much to offer New England. They are either too obsessed about specifics (gypsies, magic, or the scrolls) that it makes them an ill fit, or would require an emphasis on things that relegates the local aspects of the setting to non-importance. But it\u2019s entirely possible someone else could integrate them well into New England.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T14:42:10-08:00","id":1503264,"title":"","content":"I think that of the latter three established Gehenna Cults that the Ninth Wave or perhaps a spin-off or splinter from such a group, could be useful for a New England setting, in that it would serve as another means of involving relatively ground level vampires in the search into the occult and understanding it\u2019s workings for reasons other than being a Tremere or a Malkavian.<br /> <br /> One could also imagine something like the Ninth Wave serving as a way to tie the implied networks of witch covens and lovecraftian mystics and cults into the vampiric fabric of New England. IMO it pops up enough to be worth fleshing out how those outside the Tremere are effected by it and might interact with it.<br /> <br /> That said I do agree that having Eden around and taking on the narrative role of something like Freemasonry or an Ivy League fraternity that allows the elite members of New England vampiric society to gather.<br /> <br /> The presence of the Gangrel methuselahs mentioned further above in this thread also seems like something that could be worth getting into. Perhaps some sort of Gangrel tradition in the region centered around a few remote standing stones and the notion of elder blood gathered in the region. The old world nature associated with the region and the particular vein of folk horror that gets tied into New England makes it seem suitable to me, although I\u2019m not sure how one would implement it other then as a reason for New England to be a prominent place for Clan Gathers. Perhaps a strong Gangrel tradition in the area could be used to represent the idea of a Gangrel-Tremere conflict, with the elders gathering on the misty moors watching the warlocks warily and nursing grudges from the creation of the Tremere. One might also use a congregation of Gangrel to represent something analogous to the idea of a hereditary witch cult or Diana-cult (regardless of the concepts real world validity, it can be good inspiration for the WoD).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T17:42:37-08:00","id":1503284,"title":"","content":"You bring up some interesting ideas. You are right that you could use the Ninth Wave as a means to explore &quot;magic&quot; in the region, and you can easily build on establishing relationships between Boston and Edinburgh (the headquarters of the cult) by having some prominent Scottish vampires who were members and put them now in Boston. There already is a strong presence of Scottish vampires in the area's history. Since the Tremere have an established history in New England, and their NPCs are one of the few here with long presence and the Ninth Wave was not established until the late 19th century, I personally would keep the Tremere involvement limited in any local Ninth Wave cult. John Reiss and the others have their own established interests. But perhaps one of the newer Tremere could participate as a secret means to do his own investigations away from the controlling oversight of Reiss, Zachariah, and others. Making the center of the Gehenna cult in Boston among the Malkavians and Toreador there. And of course the Ninth Wave's connection to Tennyson and Tennyson's Idylls of the Kings plays perfectly into the pseudo-Arthuriana of the Six Knights. I admit I had not considered that angle before, but it definitely fits. <br /> <br /> In terms of the Gangrel, since this area was one of the first places for the Gangrel clan to arrive and begin embracing new people could mean that certain places which housed the first Gangrel Gathers of the New World could have become hallowed by tradition. Some of those places simply have a lot of heritage to them. And an ST could invent various traditions and stories of things that happened there or were decided there. <br /> <br /> However, rather than simply repeating European Gangrel interests, I would probably emphasize the presence of the early Native Americans who were brought into the clan. They would provide a different perspective in Gangrel culture. Probably less interested in historical clan grievances against the Tremere that happened in Europe centuries before Columbus, and more interested in their local clan history, early encounters with the Sabbat, and perhaps mystic knowledge remembered from their mortal days. Personally I would find it more interesting if the Gangrel clan was one where the local elders were mostly Native American while the younger neonates tend to be from European descent. 500 year old Gangrel are not particularly old by vampire standards so we tend to think of elders mostly from the Old World. But I think it would help cement a more local flavor. Having elders who were Abenaki, Mohican, Pequot, and Wampanoag (along with Battista), even if of various ages, would alter the perspective of the PCs in thinking about the elders of that clan. Maybe even make one of them an Archon, Justicar Xavier's lone representative keeping an eye on the area. Hell, you could even make one of them a Croatan kinfolk (when the tribe still existed) who knows a lot of old lore and secrets about that Garou tribe. Keep it on the down low as an easter egg, but show something like a turtle tattoo done in the indigenous style while they were still mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-16T18:11:25-08:00","id":1503286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1503204#post1503204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I liked in Chicago By Night, that is absent in Dark Colony, was the \u201clayering\u201d of the Jyhad. You had the obvious conflict of the Prince and the Anarchs. There was also the conflict between the Prince and Primogen. Then the manipulations of the two Methusalehs. But individual vampires also had their own concerns about the Antedeluvians, the Jyhad, worries about Gehenna, interests in Golconda or diablerie, and so on. Dark Colony lacks this complexity. Almost everything centers on the conflict between the \u201cRedcoats\u201d and the \u201cKindred of Liberty\u201d with some additional high level conflict between the patrons of the Triad (who are not even in New England). There is very little else other than the struggle between the Sabbat and Camarilla, and even that is tied to the Methusalehs behind the Triad..</div> </div> </div> </div>Over the years, I've often considered the idea that any Vampire setting really needs some sort of 3 (or even 4) dimensional politics/conspiracy/Jyhad map. Something that starts at the surface level with the various neonate doings and open stuff like the Prince vs local anarchs and keeps going deeper (important Anarch actually works for the Sheriff) and deeper (Anarch leader and Prince are actually allied against a faction within the Primogen) and so on, down to something like &quot;4th gen Toreador buried under the city is locked in an astral battle of Warhammer against an ancient demon using the entire city's population as game pieces.&quot;<br /> That way, you can have a sense of what PCs might get caught up in depending on age and Status, and what sort of stuff they are likely to uncover from there.<br /> I wonder if there's any sort of software for that. \ud83e\udd14","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-17T22:13:21-08:00","id":1503355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1503286#post1503286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Over the years, I've often considered the idea that any Vampire setting really needs some sort of 3 (or even 4) dimensional politics/conspiracy/Jyhad map.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely think there should be layers. But I am leery of making everything dependent on ultimately on the machinations of powerful, ancient vampires. I've found Players in general to be limited in their aspirations in understanding the Jyhad. They tend to simplify rather than seek higher conspiracies. And many players don't like that everything being explained by a Methusaleh did it. Too many times I have pushed that angle, and the result was the players being confused and angry as a result of unexpected blowback. So I have learned to temper things. Maybe that's just my own stupidity.<br /> <br /> So while I like having multiple Jyhad layers, I actually shy away from CbN's portrayal as everything ultimately is derived from the feud between Menele and Helena. In fact, I've been a player in three CbN chronicles and not once has that come into play. Either the ST didn't play up that angle, or didn't push it as the players were not interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T10:20:26-08:00","id":1503384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1503284#post1503284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, rather than simply repeating European Gangrel interests, I would probably emphasize the presence of the early Native Americans who were brought into the clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it not mentioned that other Clans - like the Nosferatu, the Tremere, or the Malkavians - could very well show a simillar preference and attitude in regard to Embracing natives and locals?<br /> ( And similar or comparable attitudes and also ideas could be important in regard to Ghouling, as well. )<br /> It does not seem to me that the Gangrel Vampires would be be that unique about these tendences and preferences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T11:09:53-08:00","id":1503390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1503355#post1503355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I definitely think there should be layers. But I am leery of making everything dependent on ultimately on the machinations of powerful, ancient vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I just use that as an example, partially because early Vampire seemed to fall back on that kind of thing too often IMO. Really, for a city, I'd put the plot ceiling (or would that be floor since we're going down? \ud83e\udd14) at the Prince and Primogen/elder layer.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T11:54:05-08:00","id":1503394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1503384#post1503384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it not mentioned that other Clans - like the Nosferatu, the Tremere, or the Malkavians - could very well show a simillar preference and attitude in regard to Embracing natives and locals?<br /> ( And similar or comparable attitudes and also ideas could be important in regard to Ghouling, as well. )<br /> It does not seem to me that the Gangrel Vampires would be be that unique about these tendences and preferences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly other clans could. There's no problem having character examples in the other clans. Dark Colony even has a Brujah anti-antribu who was an Abenaki. But I mention this for the Gangrel because there is a huge gap between their first arrival and when we see the other clans in the region as mentioned in Dark Colony. A Gangrel Methusaleh and three of his childer arrived in the region in the early 16th century. The next two clans, the Tremere and Ventrue, don't arrive until around 1635 a century later, and they are pretty much confined to the very few and low populated British colonial cities like Boston. More clans don't start arriving until the early 18th century. And while the book just mentions clans and not individual vampires, the population of Boston is only in the thousands in this time period, still under 20,000 by the time of the American Revolution. So we are talking a handful of Kindred total.<br /> <br /> o the Gangrel were pretty much alone for over a century or even two, had very potent generation to spawn from, and had the entire indigenous population of New England before them. The Methusaleh and his trio of childer left the region after around 30 years, but they created two Indian Gangrel before they left. And they won't be needing to require permission of a Prince to embrace. They'll only slowly integrate into the Camarilla and adjust once the European colonists/immigrants begin to dominate the region.. To me this suggests possibilities that we don't get from the other clans.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-18T12:32:09-08:00","id":1503395,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that New England should probably have at least one Gangrel lineage descending from a vampire who came to Vineland.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T17:01:27-08:00","id":1503646,"title":"","content":"Before I get to the Sabbat itself, I want to comment on the Camarilla\u2019s defenses. After pulling everything together, I think the New England Camarilla actually has a solid defense. Pendragon and his followers seem to be a fairly potent fighting force. Quentin and his Six Knights had their own successes back in the day. The Tremere chantry has some old and potent members who have been there for over two hundred years. Warwick has an outstanding regional intelligence network that goes beyond the typical Nosferatu. There should be some fairly potent Gangrel who act as a reliable scouts. And the seer Prudence Stone provides an additional unexpected intelligence advantage.<br /> <br /> The frontlines have been fairly solid for around a hundred years. (Dark Colony is often too vague with history, we\u2019re told of no noteworthy battles after the Battle of Bloods Brook in Lebanon, NH in 1896.) Furthermore, the Kindred here have had extensive combat experience against the Sabbat since the colonial era. To them, the Sabbat is not some mystery or unknown bogeyman. They know their tactics, have inflicted some major defeats on them, and know what to expect. They have overcome any fear and shock long ago. When the wave of Sabbat Crusades caused many American cities to fall in the sixties and seventies, New England was not impacted.<br /> <br /> In other words, the New England Camarilla has been a major outlier. It is the one nut the Sabbat has not been able to crack despite notable successes elsewhere.<br /> <br /> This should inform our decisions when we go about developing the local Sabbat.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T17:04:53-08:00","id":1503647,"title":"","content":"As we consider the Sabbat, one thing we must keep in mind is that some of the information in Dark Colony is either contradictory or confusing. Dark Colony is an early product, and thus some of its statements do not match later canon as it was developed. While we willw ant to utilize information on the Sabbat close to New England as detailed in Montreal By Night, New York By Night, and other sourcebooks, we must understand that things will not align and STs must make certain decisions.<br /> <br /> First, let\u2019s consider Dark Selina. We\u2019re told Dark Selina is a rising power in the Sabbat. We\u2019re even told she is a Cardinal. But we also know she is lying in torpor in Switzerland, and that her support of the Sabbat (through Jeremy Skelton) is one of a \u201cmysterious benefactor\u201d.<br /> <br /> Does this make any sense? Why would the Sabbat make a torpored vampire a Cardinal? How would they even know she still exists? Or put her in charge of New England as she is in Switzerland? It doesn\u2019t. Pendragon is known to be Dark Selina\u2019s childe, yet he seemed to have been accepted among the Camarilla in Europe. He was not seen as an anti-tribu. Rather than be Sabbat, I think Kindred saw her as one of those powerful Methusalehs that remained outside any sect - a menace definitely, but not a member of that sect (likely because she was so old and powerful she disdained the limitations of belonging to any sect - to her the Sabbat is just another tool.)<br /> <br /> Instead, it seems more likely to me that Dark Selina is not actually a Cardinal, but that she is somehow \u201ccontrolling\u201d or \u201cmanipulating\u201d a local Sabbat Cardinal. Primarily to keep her pawn Pendragon alive. (If we want a reason why the Sabbat has not been more successful in New England, this could be it.) She's also directly manipulating Skelton by influencing his thoughts and actions.<br /> <br /> We know Pendragon is also being \u201cmanipulated\u201d by Dark Selina. That is a common conceit in VtM, but one usually associated with vampires of the same lineage as the Methusaleh. Critias served Menele because he is his childe. Annabelle serves Helena because she was sired by Maria who was Helena\u2019s childe. That implies that Jeremy Skelton, 8<sup>th</sup> generation Brujah antitribu and his (destroyed) sire French Sabbat Marcel DeBreau, is also of Dark Selina\u2019s lineage. Skelton might be only distantly descended from Dark Selina (who must be 5<sup>th</sup> generation), but it makes sense. We\u2019re also told that Skelton\u2019s sire was a powerful seventh generation Sabbat feared by others. Skelton cannot be the only childe of Marcel, or that Marcel\u2019s sire might be Sabbat as well. So there very well could be another Brujah anti-tribu descended from Selina who is a Cardinal that Dark Selina is manipulating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T17:07:24-08:00","id":1503648,"title":"","content":"Second, we need a real organization for the New England Sabbat. Namely, who is their Cardinal and where is he based? At the time of Dark Colony publication in 1993, this was not established. Kyle Strathcona as Cardinal of Canada did not appear until 1997. I don\u2019t think Francisco de Polonia, Cardinal of the Eastern American Territories, existed until 1999/2000 when his name began appearing in various Revised products.<br /> <br /> I also want to note that the history of the Sabbat in New York City as later detailed in products like New York By Night does not match what was earlier established. Rage Across New York mentions important Sabbat like Shawnda Dorrit, Priscus of Manhattan (Brujah) and Bishop Violet Tremain (Tzimisce). They are completely absent in NYbN. Under a Blood Red Moon mentions a New York Sabbat Bishop named Gustov who is a mentor/contact of Anita Cartwright. He too is not mentioned. Whether intentional or an oversight, the New York Sabbat we know from Revised does not exist in Dark Colony. How these versions are reconciled will be up to the ST.<br /> <br /> So who do the New England Sabbat fall under? I don\u2019t think it makes sense for them to have their own Cardinal. New England is too small an area. And Strathcona rules the Sabbat of Canada, not America. The Cardinal of the Eastern American Territories makes the most sense, but if the Cardinal is a Brujah of the line of Dark Selina then Francisco de Polonia cannot be the Cardinal yet. When I look up Polonia\u2019s page on the White Wolf wiki, it says he did not become Cardinal until after the East Coast Crusade in 1999, but it does not name who was the Cardinal before him. If anyone knows, it oculd be useful.<br /> <br /> In any case, I would put the Sabbat of New England was under the auspices of another Brujah anti-tribu Cardinal, probably based in New York City who was the predecessor to Polonia (who is only the Archbishop of New York at the time). He might be a broodmate of Skelton, the sire of his sire Marcel, or some other descendant of Dark Selina not directly in the line of Skelton. Now that we\u2019ve established that, we can consider some other things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T17:09:44-08:00","id":1503649,"title":"","content":"Third, who rules the Sabbat in New England? Shouldn\u2019t there be a Bishop or even Archbishop? Dark Colony is silent on this. We know Jeremy Skelton is an important figure as leader of the Crimson Tide (which seems to be an alliance of packs, not a pack/coven itself), but he only has Status 2. From the Players Guide to Sabbat, we know a pack priest or leader is Status 1. Status 2 is \u201crespected\u201d, equivalent to a Templar or Paladin. Bishops and Archbishops are at 3 or 4. So Skelton clearly is not a Bishop. It is possible that Skelton is actually a Paladin to some Sabbat leader, or just considered to be equivalent in status because of the prestige of leading Crimson Tide. Pick whichever option you like best.<br /> <br /> Skelton\u2019s base is in Maine and northern New Hampshire. So there should be someone with a title like Archbishop of Bangor or Portland. In Dark Colony, Portland, Maine is definitely Sabbat. I will make it a contested city in my own chronicles simply to boost the numbers of Pendragon\u2019s Brujah. But simply because it is contested does not mean there cannot be an Archbishop there especially because it would have been solely Sabbat until Pendragon launched Operation Longbow in 1895.<br /> <br /> Maine does not have much of a population. Using Dark Colony\u2019s numbers, there are probably only 30 or so Sabbat total compared to 120 or so Camarilla/Anarchs in all of New England. So the Archbishop would not have many Bishops assisting her. Maybe zero or just one. Bangor is distant enough from the Portland metro area, so it might have its own Archbishop covering 3 vampires or so. But I don\u2019t think an Archbishop should have so few Sabbat under her, so I\u2019d make the ruler there a Bishop who reports to the Archbishop who might be called Archbishop of Maine or even New England rather than just Portland.<br /> <br /> I think that is it for the terms of Sabbat organization. We need to create the Archbishop, and one or possibly two bishops (the ruler of Bangor and someone else to assist the Archbishop on other matters). Now we move to the packs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T17:14:58-08:00","id":1503650,"title":"","content":"Fourth, we need to fill out more packs. Skelton\u2019s Rangers and Mowgli\u2019s Order are interesting. But we only have their pack leaders and a little general information on their packs. So there is lots of work for the ST to do.<br /> <br /> In the coterie chart section (which strangely comes before the NPCs, not after as was done in other books), we have a chart for the Sabbat. Unfortunately, the chart description does not refer to the things on it which hurts in usefulness. But it seems like there are three additional packs under Skelton\u2019s Rangers. These other packs are the Flayers, the Stand, and Fugue. They are probably allied with Skelton as part of the \u201cCrimson Tide\u201d alliance of packs, and probably dominated by him (while Mowgli's Order is allied, but much more independent.) It could mean Skelton, while not having the title of Archbishop, may have effectively usurped his power. Or that the Archbishop defers a lot to Skelton while she concentrates on other things not dealing with the fighting of the Camarilla. Or that she is dominated by his power, possibly resentfully so.<br /> <br /> We\u2019re not given any other information about these three packs, but I will be using them as the other Sabbat packs/covens in the region. So that is five packs total for around 30 vampires. That leaves us decent pack sizes for all of them with an average of six.<br /> <br /> I would make at least one pack a founded coven in Portland (around the Archbishop), and another founded coven in Bangor. Pick whichever name out of the Flayers, Stand, and Fugure, that you like. Dark Colony heavily implies that Skelton\u2019s Rangers is based in Portland, but they also seem to travel a bit. Mowgli\u2019s Order is obviously a nomad pack, but again one that stays within the region. That leaves one remaining pack for our five which I would make another nomad pack, perhaps one that does leave the region sometimes to travel to Montreal or New York City (or both).<br /> <br /> And of course, there is no problem if the occasional nomad pack originating from outside New England shows up briefly.<br /> <br /> Filling out these others packs will be a job for each ST. I would only recommend that since Jeremy Skelton is on the Path of Power &amp; the Inner Voice, and Mowgli is on the Path of Honorable Accord, that we look for other Paths as the basis for the other packs. While packs do not need to follow just one Path, I think there should be strong representation of the Path of Caine and Path of Death and the Soul. I've always thought these two Paths define the Sabbat. And since Mowgli\u2019s Order seems to be comprised only of Country Gangrel, we might want to put one of the city covens as having members of the City Gangrel to provide some additional conflict.<br /> <br /> One thing I like is that the two representatives of the Sabbat are of the anti-tribu, and not of the two main clans of Lasombra and Tzimisce. It provides some nice distinction. So while I would not exclude members of those clans here, I would probably emphasize the presence of the anti-tribu here more, especially in terms of leadership. I will note that neither Skelton or Mowgli have Vicissitude listed in their Disciplines, but both do have Obtenebration. So likely there is some Laosmbra presence at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-21T17:16:05-08:00","id":1503651,"title":"","content":"Fifth, let\u2019s add some Revenants. We\u2019re specifically told that there are Obertus in New England in the Storytellers Guide to the Sabbat published the same year as Dark Colony so it is unfortunate they are not mentioned. In Ghouls\u201d Fatal Addiction we\u2019re given the fictional hometown of one Obertus as Haverhill, MA. So in my chronicles, that is the small town of Obertus in New England. So I\u2019d plant Haverhill somewhere in rural Massachusetts in Dunwich country. For the most part the Sabbat ignore it, but every so often a pack uses it to hide out or a Bishop or Sabbat scholar asks one of the Revenants there for help on some scholarly issue.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not a fan of stacking too many concepts into the same region. There does not need to be representation from every Revenant family. So I\u2019d probably leave the Zantosa and Bratovitch out. But I would have Grimaldi present in New York City blood bond to one of the Tzimisce Bishops of New York. They are close enough to provide assistance for the Masquerade as needed.<br /> <br /> At this point, I think I\u2019ve addressed all the major things that should be addressed about the Sabbat. But if I missed anything, please let me know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T22:03:27-08:00","id":1503731,"title":"","content":"Just personally, I always felt like the story of 'Salem's Lot (with a different name) should have been part of WoD New England's history. By that I mean that sometime in the Ford administration, a Sabbat pack managed to turn an entire isolated small town into shovelheads over a period of a few weeks and then unleashed them against surrounding Camarilla areas. And the whole thing probably ended up as a colossal failure (hence why no one does this sort of thing). Such a mob of cannon fodder is too hard to control, some probably turned on and diablerized each other or fell to the Beast, packs of lupines probably destroyed a bunch of them, and so on. The Camarilla probably had to cover up the loss of the town, alongside the New York Grimaldi and other concerned parties. And it is sort of forgotten.<br /> <br /> But there are still files on the incident sitting in storage rooms at the FBI SAD office, the Arcanum's Boston chapter house, and the morgue of the Midnight Star tabloid (from Orpheus). Waiting for some hunter to come across them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-22T22:30:14-08:00","id":1503733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1503731#post1503731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just personally, I always felt like the story of 'Salem's Lot (with a different name) should have been part of WoD New England's history. By that I mean that sometime in the Ford administration, a Sabbat pack managed to turn an entire isolated small town into shovelheads over a period of a few weeks and then unleashed them against surrounding Camarilla areas. And the whole thing probably ended up as a colossal failure (hence why no one does this sort of thing).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is a very good idea. Salem's Lot is exactly how I envision a lot of Sabbat packs want to operate. It has a lot of appeal, and I think a New England setting should borrow a lot of inspiration from Stephen King. <br /> <br /> However, personally I have a hard time figuring out how to deal with the whole Masquerade aspects of that. The one thing I hate about STing VtM is when the PCs do something so monumentally stupid it blows the Masquerade up, and if I don't want to shitcan the entire chronicle, I - never the PCs it seems - have to figure out how to handle it so the game can continue. I might just combine the tropes of it being a small town dying anyway do to economic factors plus a brush fire that gets out of control. Maybe the Grimaldi (through various fronts) in the end arranges to buy the property for &quot;future development&quot; and let's it sit. Being a small town in the backwoods of Maine, maybe the replacement Archbishop has enough control of the media and government that they can explain it as a natural, normal death of a small town by people leaving.<br /> <br /> The other aspect is how to make it such a clusterfuck that the Sabbat won't do it again. Like the old Archbishop heard about it, and went there to investigate or thank the pack for its &quot;victory&quot;, and then got eaten so the whole thing became a huge embarrassment and Skelton had to come down and torch them all. But not before Pendragon takes advantage of the chaos to attack and destroy a pack or two who show up afterwards to deal with it (the shovelhead packs never quite got to the stage where they actually attacked anything Camarilla). This would be a good thing that Prudence Stone could have foreseen in her visions and warned everyone about. Make it a major Sabbat defeat that set back the sect for decades. I think it has to blow up in the Sabbat's faces so bad that the sect just won't tolerate anything so monumentally stupid in the future. Getting the details on this matters. Maybe there are still some vampires buried leftover from the Creation Rites that occasionally wake up from torpor and manage to claw their ways out and harass people.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T10:16:58-08:00","id":1503759,"title":"","content":"I figure if this did happen, then the town likely was destroyed by a massive fire, likely started by lupines or would be mortal vampire hunters. Official records would be doctored to show that economic factors of the early 70s had already caused a large portion of the town to move out of state and because the town was so out of the way, the land is just sort of abandoned and in some sort of legal limbo (with certain factions working to keep it that way). In the mid 70s, this probably barely makes the state wide news, and only as a forest fire. But among nearby towns, it has become part of the local folklore, the stuff outsiders dismiss as the superstitions of ignorant yokals. (See &quot;One for the Road&quot;.) <br /> <br /> As for the Sabbat, I feel this is some &quot;brilliant new idea&quot; an ambitious young turk gets every hundred years or so, not realizing that it has been done before - a Wild West ghost town, an abandoned colonial settlement, a lost 16th century European village - and always fails. And always for the same reasons: The mob can't be controlled, usually gets destroyed before doing anything useful, and attracts the wrong kind of attention from lupines and witchhunters (and maybe even ghosts and MiBs). And usually the Camarilla mounts an effective counterstrike in the chaos. So the local Bishops who are all old enough to know better have to punish those involved (assuming they survived) and lecture the kids about why this plan never works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T14:04:17-08:00","id":1503773,"title":"","content":"Another aspect of the Sabbat I push in my chronicles is the idea that almost all vampire hunters (of whatever persuasion - mortals, Lupines, Mages, Children of Osiris, etc.) hunt Sabbat and not Camarilla vampires because the Sabbat is just so much more obvious. This isn't a deliberate choice just pragmatism. So it's probably best to provide a lot more detail on Sabbat history and their current opponents so the Sabbat NPCs (or PCs if an ST goes down that route) understand what they are facing. They have a lot more opponents than just the Camarilla, and they strike during the daytime.<br /> <br /> Have some battles when some Lupines wiped out an entire pack. Create some past names and put down specific dates and locations where it happened. Garou Gifts provide a lot of the same &quot;here's the plot for the game&quot; stuff that Prudence Stone's visions have so shovelhead ceremonies and the like can easily bring the attention of Lupines. There are probably two separate septs - the Silver Fangs of Vermont (the Morningkill family) and a mixed tribal sept in northern Maine so the Sabbat suffer from both. There are supposed to be Black Spiral Dancers as well who help Mowgli'd Order at least. So if an ST wants to build on the relationship between the Sabbat and the BSDs (something generally ignored in VtM games in my experience), that could be used as to why the Lupines aren't more successful in wiping them out.<br /> <br /> Make Caiaphas Smith into a true boogey man for the Sabbat (the original Hunters Hunted state that Smith concentrates his hunts in New England where the Sabbat is his bitter enemy) with many instances of him destroying entire covens during the daytime in their own lairs (he need not be alone, but have various groups who help him - likely different groups arrayed to avenge the one friend or family member they lost). Maybe even have the Sabbat think this isn't the same man, but a family as it isn't possible for the same man to be hunting them for 150+ years, and provide all sorts of alternative legends about him - he's a revenant, a ghost, a clever Lupine who doesn't change. And of course, the Sabbat don't know his name, they just know a general, but vague description. Maybe the Justicar's edict of avoiding Caiaphas at all costs is less about depriving him of vitae so he'll die, and more about allowing him to live so he'll continue to wipe out Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Have the Arcanum collect a great deal of information about the various Sabbat disasters and know a lot about their activities and perhaps names of longstanding Sabbat. Maybe someone from the Arcanum is leaking to Caiaphas or others simply out of fear and self-preservation while they wouldn't betray information gathered on the more &quot;civilized&quot; or &quot;interesting&quot; vampires of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> And given the large Catholic population of Boston and Massachusetts, the Society of Leopold should have a very active cell. Most of New England falls under the Ecclesiatical Province of Boston except for Connecticut and Rhode Island which is under the Ecclesiatical Province of New Hartford. So there might be two different experiences with the society of Leopold in those two areas assuming the cell is based in Boston and limits their activities to what falls under their Archbishop (which happens to be the Sabbat hotbeds). Boston is one of the four oldest Cenacula of the Society of Leopold.<br /> <br /> And there might be various independent vampire hunters out there. Family lore passed down from the Vampire Panic of the 19th century. Am actual Revenant who wants to avenge his family's murder at the hands of the Sabbat (and perhaps the specific vampire who lead that pack at that time). Or someone whose friend or family member was just recently threatened or turned.<br /> <br /> This can go a long way to explain why the &quot;frontline&quot; has so little changed in a century. The Sabbat keeps losing packs and covens and need to recover. Maybe the Sabbat of Bangor have an issue because they lose the entire coven every twenty years or so. Maybe Skelton and Mowgli are the only noteworthy Sabbat because they are among the few who actually survived during this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T14:41:12-08:00","id":1503776,"title":"","content":"In hindsight, I think it would be interesting for the Society of Leopold in Boston to have this really strong blue-collar working-class ascetic to it, especially when contrasted against the local Arcanum's upper class Brahmin Ivy League feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T15:26:15-08:00","id":1503780,"title":"","content":"Black Fox's ideas of New England would make the Sabbat more of an underdog than the Anarchs. Seems more apt for a Sabbat Chronicle like what Cajun Khan would do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-23T17:28:28-08:00","id":1503786,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Sabbat is quite the underdog. They have a solid core of territory (which the Anarchs don't), get reinforcements from the other Sabbat strongholds, and have some experienced leaders. It's just that we need to explain why for a century there's been no progress on either side. The Camarilla isn't making any head way either. It's just that the Camarilla does not have shovelheads it can just throw at the problem. The Sabbat does, so you need a way to eliminate any shovelhead advantage and reset them to zero after a while. Lupines and hunters are one way to do that.<br /> <br /> But certainly every ST will have their own comfort level as to how the Sabbat fares against its other foes in order to explain a stalemate.<br /> <br /> I do think the Sabbat must conduct raids in Boston or in New Hampshire against Pendragon, it's just that they cannot be destroying the Kindred of the Camarilla to the extent that it causes them to seize ground. If shovelheads are destroyed, the Sabbat can just create more easily. If a Camarilla Kindred is destroyed, it takes more effort to replace numbers because such Kindred have 5-20 years under their belt. The Camarilla is on the strategic defensive here and the Sabbat on the strategic offensive even if the Camarilla has the greater local strength.<br /> <br /> I admit I find the idea of a century long stalemate and the lack of details as to what has happened to be a major weakness of Dark Colony. There's been little thought in terms of how often the Sabbat attacks, how many casualties, how losses are replaced, etc. It's a stalemate because the writer likely ran out of ideas and just froze the setting after 1895. Ideally we'd have some battles happening around the 1920s and the 1960s with certain towns being lost or regained. <br /> <br /> Or we get some details on Sabbat politics that explain the Second Sabbat Civil War devastated the New England Sabbat, or that the New England packs were part of the brief Third Sabbat Civil War against the Lasombra and Tzimisce before they got crushed by the betrayal of the Panders. Turn the reasons for the stalemate away from outsiders and more internally if you prefer that. The best approach is probably some consideration of both. In either case, the ST has a lot to do on her own.<br /> <br /> Now some of this may be due to Dark Selina purposefully sabotaging the Sabbat because she's still deciding between Pendragon and Skelton as her primary pawn. But the better solution is probably that the Sabbat is not on the continuous offensive. But as they build up their strength, they end up losing some of the resources they've been building (for whatever reason) that either cancels the attack or causes it to be not as effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T11:56:40-08:00","id":1531969,"title":"","content":"I just wanted to pop in and thank all of your for putting together one of my very favourite threads in this part of the forums: it\u2019s been interesting to see your notions for fleshing out a region with one of the more interesting High Concepts (\u2018Supernatural New England as the Border Marches of Vampire North America\u2019) that received an official write up that did not make the most of that \u2018Savage East\u2019 concept.<br /> <br /> It also inspired me to imagine the late, great Dame Angela Lansbury (circa THE MANCHURIAN CANDIDATE) as a lady vampire, so thank you for that one as well! (A bonus points to anyone who can guess what Clan my mental image of this character belongs to and a very special no-prize if anyone can guess exactly which character I\u2019m thinking of before my next post on the old Dark Colony*).<br /> <br /> <br /> *<i>Incidentally, this is one of my favourite titles for a regional sourcebook in the White Wolf lines: it has a delightfully spooky ring to it.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T22:03:36-08:00","id":1531995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1531969#post1531969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">this is one of my favourite titles for a regional sourcebook</div> </div> </div> </div>I happen to think <b>Dark Colony</b> is a good title. As a sourcebook, not so much, but obviously given my posts I've been able to take some things from it.<br /> <br /> There are some good things in there, but overall I'm disappointed in the sourcebook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1531969#post1531969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also inspired me to imagine the late, great Dame Angela Lansbury (circa THE MANCHURIAN CANDIDATE) as a lady vampire&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There are very few female vampire NPCs in Dark Colony. If it was anyone, I would guess the already destroyed Georgia Rowlands, sire of Upton Rowlands, simply on how Angela looks. She has that old money appearance (but probably more from Murder She Wrote in the 1980s than the Manchurian Candidate in 1962). Since Georgia Rowlands would not be anything reminiscent of Lansbury's character in Manchurian Candidate, it would have to be someone else.<br /> <br /> But it doesn't fit Effie, Jara, or Elsa (or Dark Selina who is not given an image) who are the only mentioned female NPCs. So maybe it's a character from Swansong or one of the other NPCs from other sourcebooks mentioned? But as a manipulator of others, then Dark Selina might work best though I would never have imagined Angela Lansbury as her, choosing instead a more traditional femme fatale image.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T06:23:45-08:00","id":1532009,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, you are correct sir!<br /> <br /> I admit that MURDER SHE WROTE is a key reason Dame Angela Lansbury occurred to me as a plausible casting choice for \u2018Aunt Rowlands\u2019 - old fan jokes that Mrs Fletcher may find murder everywhere she goes because she\u2019s actually <i>committing</i> some of them abound, so it struck me that imagining Georgia Rowlands as somebody with a reputation for both solving mysteries and getting away with murder might lend an interesting twist to a character that doesn\u2019t seem to have been exhaustively detailed.<br /> <br /> Especially if, once every half-century or so, she turned out a novel (Published under a series of cover identities) about COMPLETELY MUNDANE characters getting involved in a COMPLETELY MUNDANE mystery with a COMPLETELY MUNDANE solution that sent Cainite New England half-wild trying to puzzle out if this was a roman-a-clef or not.<br /> <br /> <br /> For the record, I was thinking of THE MANCHURIAN CANDIDATE because Dame Angela is more horror-adjacent in that role (and much more blatantly Establishment-looking); it also occurred to me that Georgia Rowlands would have been embraced at a relatively young age (Since that seems to be the usual custom amongst the Kindred).<br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, I\u2019ve been operating on the assumption that \u2018Aunt Rowlands\u2019 (One imagines that she had an immense social circle of younger persons who instinctively call her \u2018Aunt\u2019 whether or not they\u2019re actual blood relations) was embraced at some time during the American Revolution - with her sire quietly seeding New England with vampires young enough to be expendable, but shrewd enough to quietly rebuild Clan Ventrue\u2019s position in the region after the Brujah did a number on them during the Revolution &amp; War of Independence.<br /> <br /> One further assumes that, while Aunt Rowlands did a yeoman job in this respect, one of her peers preferred to settle into obscurity and focus almost exclusively on the dramas of his own mortal relations, becoming the \u2018World of Darkness Barnabas Collins\u2019 mentioned in previous pages.<br /> <br /> More on him later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T07:24:22-08:00","id":1532025,"title":"","content":"Now I\u2019m not great expert on DARK SHADOWS in any incarnation, but the notion of a \u2018World of Darkness Barnabas Collins\u2019 fascinated me, so here\u2019s what I\u2019ve come up with for the concept so far:-<br /> <br /> <br /> - As mentioned above, I tend to assume that he is of the same generation as Georgia Rowlands and quite probably embraced at roughly the same time (Intended to serve as a \u2018holdout\u2019 in a New England where Ventrue were at the nadir of their fortunes), though their sire may have taken precautions to ensure that these holdouts were only vaguely aware of each other, as a security precaution against their getting together only to be mobbed.<br /> <br /> <br /> - The name \u2018Bartholomew Stephens of Kingsport\u2019 occurred to me as a possibility: I thought this had the right element of New England Gothic and one liked the idea of making the name an homage to both Barnabas Collins &amp; Mr Stephen King.<br /> <br /> <br /> - I\u2019m assuming that a key reason Bartholomew Stephens has remained largely under the radar in terms of vampire<br /> politics is that he\u2019s situated on the fringes of a no-man\u2019s land where Lupines and the Sabbat keep (or kept, depending on the edition) the Camarilla at arm\u2019s length and are too busy hammering at each other to worry about a single, fairly-discrete vampire.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, it\u2019s possible he\u2019s worked out some kind of arrangement with non-Kindred forces and leverages that to keep Kingsport (I\u2019m not sure about the name, but I needed a working title) mostly to himself, so far as vampires go.<br /> <br /> <br /> - One further assumes that, unlike Barnabas Collins, Mr Stephens is NOT a time-traveller and has been active enough to live through various historical periods as they happened; this is mostly a product of my awareness that Barnabas Collins\u2019 long period of imprisonment would be difficult to replicate without making his Humanity frightfully low.<br /> <br /> <br /> - In terms Humanity, I would tend to put the character somewhere around \u20186\u2019: not quite human, but more than human enough to feel more than the Thirst for his family and various other associates (Though of course not all those feelings are positive and a universal good).<br /> <br /> <br /> - It has occurred to me that showing him with one or two childer/body doubles might allow one to homage the fact that DARK SHADOWS has gone through more than one incarnation (With each of these individuals freely using \u2026 and sometimes misusing ... the name \u2018Bartholomew Stephens\u2019 to keep opponents &amp; rivals guessing).<br /> <br /> <br /> - One should also admit that my notion for his feeding restriction was \u2018French-speakers\u2019 (As a nod to the character\u2019s uncomfortable relationship with Angelique and Maine\u2019s significant population of French-speaking individuals), but this <br /> might be a trifle too specific.<br /> <br /> My pet theory is that a Ventrue\u2019s feeding restriction should say something - usually something uncomfortable - about the deeper reaches of their psychology: the best possible choice should leave those who uncover it less than comfortable with the revelation, ESPECIALLY when they know the character fairly well.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Finally, one gets the mental image of his experience with non-Sabbat vampires being mostly limited to local Gangrel, since they offer a fascinating contrast with the very Old World Mr Stephens.<br /> <br /> <br /> That\u2019s all I have for now and hopefully it isn\u2019t too feeble a skeleton on which someone else might further flesh out these bare bones (I\u2019m not sufficiently familiar with the franchise to make more detailed suggestions).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T17:54:51-08:00","id":1532068,"title":"","content":"I'd have to give a lot more thought to the best way to utilize a Barnabas Collins type character so that he would be useful in play - someone the PCs could conceivably meet, and more importantly would want to interact with. Otherwise he's just useless as an RPG character. But this is what I currently think.<br /> <br /> Barnabas (or Batholomew or however he is named) lives in a coastal town of around 10,000 people. So there's not much room for any vampire other than him. His feeding has to be very non-invasive for him to feed without discovery. If he ever has childer, the childe would probably have to leave and dwell somewhere else. However, since Barnabas is a key figure of sympathetic vampires, I'd probably have him not sire any childer at all.<br /> <br /> However, he might indeed employ one or more &quot;body doubles&quot; as younger men who pose as him or one of his sons in order to explain his eventual &quot;replacement&quot;. Rather than remain in town, they'd travel throughout Maine on business - dealing with property or other investments. Not sure where he finds them. He may just ask some legal firm to employ such subterfuge, but giving them permission, power of attorney, etc. to conduct business on his behalf. Maybe he's thought to be agoraphobic or something, unwilling to live his ancestral home. There might even be a belief that there is something &quot;wrong&quot; with the house that causes all the men who inherit the place to succumb to the same seclusion. It may even be thought haunted (and maybe it is).<br /> <br /> The small town he lives in would be considered his exclusive domain, but he wouldn't be called Prince because that's just silly when you're alone. But he might have the same Status as Elsa Linden though.<br /> <br /> He'd probably live in the family estate in town, constantly reinventing himself as yet another generation when his current mortal identity gets too old. He's known to be a recluse. His mortal descendants would live elsewhere - perhaps not even in the same town. Though he'd host regular family reunions of some kind, and every generation he'd invite a family (or at least some &quot;nephews&quot; and &quot;nieces&quot; or distant cousins) of his descendants to move in and live in with him. He might blood bond some, but never ghoul them. Most likely he'd just use Dominate and Presence to maintain control. He would have one or two retainers, but they'd likely be people who feel loyalty to him personally rather than be subjugated by him. Someone whom would keep a secret because he or she owed him a big favor. But perhaps they might also be some especially beloved family members he offered to ghoul in order to keep them alive.<br /> <br /> I agree that he might host the occasional local Gangrel, and he might be seen as a friend of the clan, willing to let them stay for a night and share stories. It might be a good spot for non-political Camarilla vampires to meet away from all the intrigue of the Triad and its opponents. In any case, that friendship would be needed anytime a random Sabbat pack might enter the town.<br /> <br /> I have no preference for the Ventrue feeding restriction, but I do think an exclusion based on French speakers could work. Our fictional town might have a significant minority of people who speak French at home, perhaps it even has the last French language newspaper in New England, though perhaps only published monthly or quarterly and being only a few pages or perhaps being online only now. Perhaps the town is known for its preservation efforts for the French language with French taught even in elementary school or a small parochial Catholic school that has French immersion (the schools may get a small number of boarding students whose parents send their kids here precisely in order to become fluent). All, of course, supported in some fashion by Barnabas. Maybe 10% of the population or so speaks French at home.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what a good hook might be to make Barnabas or the city something that PCs might want to visit at some point. Does Barnabas have some kind of important or secret knowledge that would cause people to seek him out? Does the town have some resource - a rare bookstore, a private library, a place of occult power, a haunted house - that would cause people to seek it out and thus gain permission from its &quot;Prince&quot; to be there? Is Barnabas some kind of important, but hidden, business man or local political influence that his name keeps popping up as a person of interest that could cause one or more PCs to investigate and prompt them to find out more or get his support? Maybe he happens to be the eldest Ventrue in New England, and therefore even though he eschews politics and involvement in Kindred affairs, the Ventrue clan sometimes calls on him to mediate disputes between the Ventrue in the region. Something else? Likely it would have to be some combination to provide enough hooks that at least one of them could attract a PC to want to interact with him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 03-06-2024, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T14:53:42-08:00","id":1532118,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> , thank you for taking the time to put together an excellent reply! In return for your own thoughts:-<br /> <br /> - Given the close ties between the character and his family (Not to mention DARK SHADOWS\u2019 habit of recasting members of the ensemble as members of the same family) it\u2019s quite possible these \u2018Body Doubles\u2019 are male relations whom he\u2019s he\u2019s particularly close to and to whom he bears a significant resemblance (His close relationship with his kin may well be a case of \u201cDoing well by doing good\u201d as this proximity allows him to masquerade as younger members of the family, at least for a time).<br /> <br /> <br /> - The title \u2018Squire\u2019 (In the sense of a country gentleman of influence and significant estate, but no claim to hereditary title rather than what one wit dubbed a \u2018Murder Caddy\u2019) occurs to me as a plausible alternative to \u2018Prince\u2019 or \u2018Baron\u2019 though \u2018Sheriff\u2019 might be more Yankee.<br /> <br /> If this title were bestowed, it would probably be through the Good offices of Roman Pendragon*, given he seems to be the farthest North of all the Camarilla Princes (Though it\u2019s<br /> possible this could be an effort to set up an exclave by one of his opponents in the Ivory Tower) and would logically welcome a chance to establish a base (or at least cultivate an ally) in the region, possibly as an olive branch to Clan Ventrue.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>*Incidentally, I assume that \u2018Roman Pendragon\u2019 as a whole is a nom de plume, \u2018Roman\u2019 presumably being adopted as a way of asserting that Clan Ventrue do not have exclusive title to the Legacy of Rome (Incidentally, it\u2019s interesting to note that Roman Pendragon\u2019s effort to break the Ventrue stronghold on the British Isles seems to have occurred during a period when Mithras was absent and his seneschal Valerius was acting Prince of London: in fact the period between 1848 and 1885 CE sees Valerius open London up to the Camarilla - in the wake of a Sabbat attack - triggering something of a land rush, which may have provided the key opportunity for Pendragon to make his move)</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> - In terms of plot hooks that would persuade PCs to enter \u2018Bartholomew Sharp\u2019s house as a guest (and possibly even return), there\u2019s always the chance of a family connection (A PC could be related to the old man, either directly or through a relationship with some family member); they might, as you noted, be looking for the \u2018Last Homely House\u2019 in an area with very few options for vampires (In the same way that Beorn from THE HOBBIT is almost the only option for shelter in a howling wilderness, but not the easiest host to get on with); they could very well be seeking to learn how one survives and prospers as an autarkis; given the sheer wealth of weirdness in DARK SHADOWS, they might be looking for advice on how to deal with other supernatural beings when running for cover is not an option; and I believe that there\u2019s at least one plotline where the House of Collins is sitting on buried treasure, so there\u2019s always that to catch Our Heroes\u2019 interest.<br /> <br /> If nothing else, \u2018Kingsport\u2019 might be an excellent site for a \u2018Breather Episode\u2019 where the PCs can take a dip in a little soap opera, rather than get chewed up by Vampire Power Polltics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T15:37:22-08:00","id":1532120,"title":"","content":"By the way, I\u2019ve been working to try and sketch out some characters based on the various concepts you posted a few pages back, as well as one or two characters mentioned in this thread but with no article on the White Wolf wiki: amongst the latter was the \u2018Osric\u2019 (Clan Nosferatu, of the 8th Generation) mentioned as having sired Prudence Stone.<br /> <br /> - Per your suggestion that he would have been sired at some point between the arrival of the Saxons in England and the Norman Conquest, I imagine that he was Embraced when the Great Heathen Army ravaged the English-speaking kingdoms my idea was that the Fenrir were hip-deep in the whole business, vampires got nervous and embraced childer (Whether as reinforcements, meat shields or an insurance policy against their bloodline dying out I leave to your imagination).<br /> <br /> <br /> - I like the idea of his having been long associated with the port of Dunwich, for reasons that should be obvious to any nerd with a fondness for Weird Tales from New England (Though in a sourcebook one might disguise this Lovecraft reference by running with the theory that Dunwich was the former capital of East Anglia known as \u2018Dommoc\u2019 making the character \u2018Osric of Dommoc\u2019 during his breathing days).<br /> <br /> In any case, the history of Dunwich as a significant port on England\u2019s east coast that was almost literally chewed away by the sea until it was a mere village is a splendid element to include as background for a character straight out of a horror<br /> movie (and the loss of his home base forcing Osric under the praxis of another Cainite would provide an excellent stressor pushing him towards the New World, once the opportunity presented itself).<br /> <br /> <br /> - Assuming that Osric was embraced during a Werewolf Panic, it\u2019s possible he may have had a sideline as a \u2018Lupine Expert\u2019 amongst his Clan, which would provide another strong incentive to move into the New World (Possibly at about the same time King Aaron Everstone was making England a very dangerous place for things he didn\u2019t like, while the loss of the Croatan left a serious gap in the defences of the Eastern Seaboard).<br /> <br /> It\u2019s quite possible Osric might have been amongst the first of his clan in the area for the simple reason that he not only had experience of surviving in Werewolf country, but as a Nosferatu could move around this sort of region without attracting any dangerous degree of attention.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Going by the story of Prudence Stone\u2019s origin, he<br /> might simply have been a reasonably-high Humanity Kindred who enjoyed the idea of getting out from under the Jyhad; alternatively he might have taken a keen interest in Mistress Stone\u2019s foresight because he was keeping a weather eye on the Tremere and eager to acquire assets that would counter their occult supremacy.<br /> <br /> Certainly one supposes he was in the Americas (and possibly to stay) by the later 1600s (If memory serves, the Witch Trils tended to occur in the latter part of the 17th century).<br /> <br /> <br /> - It\u2019s also possible that Osric was a Nosferatu of the old school, who favoured lairing in the wilder regions of the world (Caves, rather than tombs or ancient ruins) which would definitely have boosted his chances of survival in New England (Especially if he preferred to feed on beasts more often than humans, which was likely an increasingly-unfashionable choice as population numbers continued to climb).<br /> <br /> <br /> - I\u2019m assuming that he and his descendants would be a little to one side of Warwick\u2019s net: not necessarily hostile, but independent and quite capable of making life difficult for the Nosferatu leg of the Triad if they tried to make life difficult for their clanmates (Not least because they were rather older in New England).<br /> <br /> It\u2019s possible they were able to do business with Clan Ventrue when the latter had the catbird seat in this area and have quietly continued to keep up relatively positive relations (Possibly complicated by local Ventrue\u2019s ties to the Tremere).<br /> <br /> You\u2019ve noted that Prudence Stone could act as a sort of Pythia for Roman Pendragon: I wonder if she does so as part of a quid pro quo that allows her bloodline to mostly go it\u2019s own way independent of Warwick\u2019s network?<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, these are the notions that have occurred to me for old Osric: I\u2019ll do my best to post a character concept for one of his possible descendants tomorrow, which I\u2019ll preview and sum up with two words.<br /> <br /> \u2018Innsmouth Look\u2019.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T17:37:58-08:00","id":1532128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1532118#post1532118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The title \u2018Squire\u2019 (In the sense of a country gentleman of influence and significant estate, but no claim to hereditary title rather than what one wit dubbed a \u2018Murder Caddy\u2019) occurs to me as a plausible alternative to \u2018Prince\u2019 or \u2018Baron\u2019 though \u2018Sheriff\u2019 might be more Yankee.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely like the idea of using the title of &quot;Squire&quot; for him. It indicates a certain amount of respect and acknowledges domain while not giving undue prestige like how a Prince does, or imply that other vampires owe him some kind of fealty. (I'll probably start using that title for other vampires in similar position in my future chronicles.) It's probably valued at something like Status 3. (I imagine Elsa Linden's Status 5 as de facto &quot;Prince of Cape Cod&quot; is because of the much greater population of Barnstable County (200k or so) that can provide for multiple vampires, plus lingering respect for her earlier stint as Prince of Manchester.)<br /> <br /> It's probably something used informally by any Kindred who know about him rather than something bestowed by another vampire.<br /> <br /> As &quot;Prince of Concord&quot;, Roman Pendragon would certainly be the closest Camarilla Kindred to him, and it would make sense there is some kind of social interaction between the two even if it is only the odd phone call or message sent. But I think it would be best to separate the two mostly. There is likely some arrangement between them that allows a patrol of Pendragon's to travel through the domain on their way to fight the Sabbat of Maine, or allow them temporary shelter if coming back from it. Provided they honor the tradition of Domain and do not do anything else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1532118#post1532118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">given the sheer wealth of weirdness in DARK SHADOWS, they might be looking for advice on how to deal with other supernatural beings when running for cover is not an option</div> </div> </div> </div>There should probably be some kind of weirdness going on in the town, but not to the extent Collinsport had in Dark Shadows. The need for a daily gothic supernatural soap opera is different than from an RPG. But if it had a small coven of three Verbena witches (plus some local ghosts), that is probably more than enough to allow the ST to justify some odd thing or two as needed. The Verbena coven likely knows the secret of Barnabas, and they might appreciate him as a rather harmless vampire &quot;overlord&quot; who keeps trouble out of their small town.<br /> <br /> Another possibility is to provide Barnabas with some kind of magical aid, like the enchanted items mentioned in the original Storyteller's Handbook. Early VtM made occasional mention of magic items (also see the original Sabbat Storyteller's Guide), but this seemed to be quickly dropped and rarely mentioned again. Probably because the game writers feared a D&amp;D style magical treasure loot. But used judiciously, I think the rare and appropriate item can help the setting's mood. If Barnabas has something like a Ring of the Inscrutable Eye, or some custom made ST item, it not only would give him an edge needed to maintain his domain against interlopers, but it might provide him enough rumors about his insight, power, Disciplines, etc. that could attract the attention of PCs.<br /> <br /> <br /> Something I forgot to mention is that being based on a sympathetic vampire, our Barnabas might be rumored to be someone who knows something about Golconda, or possible ways to become human, or knows people from secret sects that have mysterious powers to preserve Humanity and some such. Having one such character in a city/region sourcebook is usually a good idea. And I don't remember Dark Colony having one. So that plus an assortment of other possible reasons we mentioned are probably sufficient hooks to make the PCs aware of the character and provide enough interesting opportunities that one or more PCs may want to explore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T04:45:32-08:00","id":1532152,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, I\u2019m glad that you liked \u2018Squire\u2019 - I\u2019m assuming it\u2019s a phrase mostly deployed by relatively old but not ancient vampires (Likely those dating from the Early Modern period to the Industrial Revolution): I\u2019d suspect younger vampires (or more urban Kindred) might think of Bartholomew Stephens as \u2018Boss\u2019 (Older vampires might think of him as a \u2018Franklin\u2019 - \u2018a free landholder, not of noble birth\u2019, though some of the classical scholars might also favour \u2018Patrician\u2019 - in the sense of someone very well born, but without specific rank).<br /> <br /> <br /> Speaking of the actual Soap Opera, I\u2019m assuming that in the World of Darkness it\u2019s not a very faithful reflection of Bartholomew Stephen\u2019s history, but a reasonably accurate depiction of his personality &amp; family situation (and might well have provided ammunition for those who like to keep the option of prosecution for Breach of the Masquerade hovering over a possible rival\u2019s head, whether they use it immediately or not).<br /> <br /> Also, I\u2019m now fascinated by the question of how DARK COLONY\u2019s very own \u2018Barnabas Collins\u2019 fits into the politics of Clan Ventrue: would Upton Rowlands regard him as a potential rival, as a mildly vexing independent or as a useful neutral party in inter-Clan feuding?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T22:17:22-08:00","id":1532230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1532152#post1532152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I\u2019m now fascinated by the question of how DARK COLONY\u2019s very own \u2018Barnabas Collins\u2019 fits into the politics of Clan Ventrue: would Upton Rowlands regard him as a potential rival, as a mildly vexing independent or as a useful neutral party in inter-Clan feuding?</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously you can do anything you like in your chronicles. It's a throwaway mention of something I thought could be put into the region. So there are lots of ways to implement it. But in my imagination, &quot;Barnabas&quot; is quite absent from both Kindred politics in general and Ventrue politics in specific. Of somewhat potent blood and age, so he can't simply be discounted or stepped on. Uptown is clearly the leader of the New England Ventrue with a large brood in Connecticut supporting him (as much as any sire's childer supports him). His only rivals are the fewer and lesser Ventrue of Boston who were defeated during Operation: Longbow (moved in my timeline from the 1890s to the American Revolution), but resent his dominance. Upton sees Barnabas as a relic who never realized how to wield power, but he still keeps his eyes open just in case because Barnabas does have the power of the blood, and thus could potentially be a threat if he ever changes.<br /> <br /> I see Barnabas as someone who could possibly act as a neutral third part to mediate disputes between the Connecticut Ventrue and the Boston Ventrue. Just powerful and respected enough to serve the role, but not powerful enough to impose an arbitration. Barnabas, being almost solely concerned with his own mortal family and his local community, would resent such obligations, but fulfill them anyway. Barnabas would never volunteer to act as such a role. But Upton (or more likely the weaker Ventrue of Boston) might appeal to him to mediate in some dispute.<br /> <br /> I think &quot;Barnabas&quot; works best as an isolated figure wrapped up in the local events of &quot;Kingsport&quot;, but with just enough interesting things going on there that PCs might decide to investigate. Ultimately, it's a &quot;sidequest&quot; or minor part of the setting from the greater regional intrigue of Dark Selina, the Triad, Cam vs Sabbat, etc. If he gets involved in that, he becomes a much greater part of the setting. Now if someone really likes this and wants to build on that inspiration, it's not wrong. My personal taste is just to keep him a minor Easter egg, but still make him relevant as an RPG element.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-07T22:29:56-08:00","id":1532232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1532120#post1532120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of his having been long associated with the port of Dunwich</div> </div> </div> </div>It's definitely a neat call out that I think a lot of players would like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1532120#post1532120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming that Osric was embraced during a Werewolf Panic, it\u2019s possible he may have had a sideline as a \u2018Lupine Expert\u2019 amongst his Clan, which would provide another strong incentive to move into the New World (Possibly at about the same time King Aaron Everstone was making England a very dangerous place for things he didn\u2019t like, while the loss of the Croatan left a serious gap in the defences of the Eastern Seaboard).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there's anything tying Osric into the Lupines, but there's nothing wrong with using that as a hook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1532120#post1532120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s quite possible Osric might have been amongst the first of his clan in the area for the simple reason that he not only had experience of surviving in Werewolf country, but as a Nosferatu could move around this sort of region without attracting any dangerous degree of attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree he could very well be the first Nosferatu in New England.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1532120#post1532120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s also possible that Osric was a Nosferatu of the old school, who favoured lairing in the wilder regions of the world (Caves, rather than tombs or ancient ruins) which would definitely have boosted his chances of survival in New England (Especially if he preferred to feed on beasts more often than humans, which was likely an increasingly-unfashionable choice as population numbers continued to climb).</div> </div> </div> </div>I can easily see the monster Grendel in Beowulf as being a Nosferatu, so I have no problem with many Nosferatu being based in the wilderness and hiding in all sorts of caves, marshes, and other unpleasant places. I think that would be the norm prior to modern sanitation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1532120#post1532120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, these are the notions that have occurred to me for old Osric: I\u2019ll do my best to post a character concept for one of his possible descendants tomorrow, which I\u2019ll preview and sum up with two words.<br /> <br /> \u2018Innsmouth Look\u2019.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another interesting look, especially since you've already tied him to Dunwich and Lovecraft's stories.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-08T13:09:22-08:00","id":1532250,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/\">Black Fox</a>, thank you for your kind replies and for taking the time to think over my notions - I enjoy embroidering on the ideas of others and love to develop a setting, so it\u2019s a positive delight to know that you enjoy some of my concepts.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> That mention of the Innsmouth Look is, of course, a segue leading into another character for New England\u2019s Nosferatu, since the Clan\u2019s particular curse is the perfect excuse to imagine an extended family of New England vampires disfigured in a way that suggests that, while every single human being has ancestors who emerged from the oceans, sea life made an appearance somewhat closer to the present day in the family tree of <i>these</i> particular specimens.<br /> <br /> - I\u2019m assuming this lineage started with a vampire whom I shall refer to as PEAQUOD, in life a seagoing man who shipped aboard the New England whaling fleet in the early decades of the Nineteenth Century (He has, on occasion, noted that he served with Herman Melville, but does not boast the connection and has never specified his exact position*) until an encounter with the Supernatural somewhere in the Pacific resulted in his being discharged.<br /> <br /> Making his way home at length, he seems to have arrived in the United States with a fund of strange stories and strange knowledge (Of the sea, amongst other things) that persuaded his sire to consider him for the embrace (Not least because his knowledge of the sea and his own seamanship was expected to prove useful): some claim he might even have brought his sire into New England in the first place (though variations on the same rumour claim he only returned a native son or daughter to their old familiar home).<br /> <br /> *<i>Rumours that he might have been the Edward C. Starbuck discharged under what one source describes as \u2018mysterious circumstances\u2019 on Tahiti have never been confirmed or denied by Peaquod himself, a man of discretion amounting to secretiveness</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Who that sure ought to be I\u2019m not entirely sure: my first inclination was towards Osric, but it struck me that making Patience Stone \u2018Peaquod\u2019s\u2019 sire would not only be a delightfully New England Gothic element (A \u2018witch\u2019 from the old days creating another Creature of the Night), but would also allow Goody Stone to keep in touch with the regional HQ of her Clan (With her childe acting as go-between and, if necessary, an escape route).<br /> <br /> If I remember correctly, this would make her childer of the 10th Generation.<br /> <br /> <br /> - I\u2019m assuming that Vampirism put something of a crimp in Peaquod\u2019s seafaring (Especially during the days when a crewman had to be available at all hours, rain or shine, on an open deck), since one assumes he would be loathe to feed on his shipmates and even more reluctant to ship out as cargo, rather than crew.<br /> <br /> One imagines that he would become more of a shadowy influence on the shipping industry, as owner of various vessels (Whaling - until the industry collapsed - fishing and merchant shipping), while running his own small boat up and down the coast as circumstances and the requirements of his Clan demanded.<br /> <br /> Presumably he embraced Childer to act as local agents in various New England ports (So that he and they could work a rotation throughout the region, making sure that there was at least one messenger/escape route in each major port - and, in Special Emergencies, to put together a wholly-vampire crew), who might well have embraced childer of their own, spreading their subtly-fishy look throughout the region to the point where even HP Lovecraft noticed (Though he never got a close look at them and, so far as we know, if there was ever a cult of Deep Ones, it was not comprised of Nosferatu).<br /> <br /> *<i>I would, in fact, suggest that Lovecraft combined rumours of the Setite colony at Cape Cod with the \u2018Innsmouth Look\u2019 of Peaquod and his descendants, all embellished with his own vivid imagination</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> - I tend to imagine that Peaquod\u2019s job is to keep up Nosferatu sea-power (Not to mention keep the various New England Nosferatu in touch with developments on the docks), but that he\u2019s also willing to hire out to non-Nosferatu Kindred should they require the use of a small boat.<br /> <br /> Also that this latter service as Ferryman is partly based on his strong desire to keep abreast of the grisly &amp; macabre: one assumes that Peaquod, with all the superstitions of a seagoing man reinforced by centuries of life as a Vampire and many another experience of Supernatural Weirdness, would act as something of a Miner\u2019s Canary for coteries delving into the more obscure mysteries and unexplained phenomena along the coastline - when he starts giving exposition on the haunted past of a location it\u2019s wise to listen and when he decides that things are getting Dangerously Weird you would be very wise to join him as he makes an escape.<br /> <br /> Assuming, of course, that you reach the boat before it disappears over the horizon: Peaquod\u2019s fund of knowledge is extensive, but it\u2019s accuracy has been known to vary - because when you\u2019re the only survivor of an expedition, having taken great care to be left guarding the boat, you\u2019re not going to know all that occurred.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Oh, and one imagines the character to be played by Mr Robert Shaw, circa JAWS; it might therefore be amusing to suggest that his unhappy experience with the supernatural in the Pacific Ocean might somehow have been connected with the Rokea.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hopefully this isn\u2019t too slender a character sketch, but the mental image of a New England Salt with more than a hint of the Classic Horror Movie \u201cDon\u2019t say you weren\u2019t warned\u201d Local Exposition and an even stronger hint of the Lovecraftian should work reasonably well for VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE \u2026 or so I trust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T14:02:23-07:00","id":1532453,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> and any other interested parties, I\u2019m still trying to work out my notions for the various New England archetypes suggested on a previous: the following individual is based on \u2018A New England lawyer-politician in the vein of John Adams or Daniel Webster\u2019.<br /> <br /> - I hope nobody will scream \u2018Vanilla!\u2019 and attack me with an ice-cream scoop for having taken one look at this suggested archetype and thought \u2018The Devil and Daniel Webster\u2019. <br /> <br /> - Which is to say that my mental image of this archetype is a concept I like to call \u2018Solicitor-General for His Wickedness\u2019 and can be safely summed up as a legal eagle so sharp that rumour has it he received vampirism as a result of Old Scratch putting him on permanent retainer, following the embarrassing incident which barred him from New Hampshire (or at least from making mischief against New Hampshire men) until Doomsday.<br /> <br /> This is probably, but not confirmably, a colourful exaggeration,<br /> <br /> <br /> - As you might imagine, my second impulse was to make this fellow a Follower of Set/Ministry lick, since the Setite\u2019s \u2018Evil is Good and Good is the real Evil\u2019 philosophy presented a very natural extension of the original inspiration for this character.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m assuming that this character was a late 18th/early 19th century Lawyer/Politician (Somebody who got his start either at the same time as the USA or not long after) who was something of an up and comer, but fell fatally ill and - on being approached by a client to settle an unusual case out of court - found himself arguing his way into vampirism in preference to to encroaching mortality (Presumably having paid a suitably folkloric price in this Devil\u2019s bargain).<br /> <br /> <br /> - From that night to this he has been honing his skills as the ultimate bargainer and plea-bargainer; the thin end of the wedge that allowed the Followers of Set access to the \u2018smoke filled rooms\u2019 of the nascent United States and their senior legal troubleshooter in North America (At least in the US &amp; Canada).<br /> <br /> One imagines him as a man wrestling with the trappings of Setite belief even as he more or less adopted their philosophy (Finding it easier to accept that he had sold his soul to The Devil, rather than becoming part of the Bloodline of an Ancient Egyptian deity) which likely means that his senior and prestigious role as legal council to the Once &amp; Future Setites may have come only AFTER The Ministry made it\u2019s debut, allowing his unorthodox beliefs to become acceptable to the Clan\u2019s mainstream.<br /> <br /> <br /> - In any case, I\u2019m inclined to name him for one of the \u2018Jury of the Damned\u2019 from the short story which provided him his original inspiration (In-universe, this may actually be a product of his being prominent enough in life to require a non-de-plume once he arose from the grave); my preference would be \u2018Thomas Morton\u2019 (An early headache for, and critic of, the Puritan Fathers who seems to have preferred the First Nations of New England to his other neighbours) or \u2018John Smeet\u2019 (The name of an apparently-fictional Reverend who seems to have been hanged for strangling several someones).<br /> <br /> I\u2019m especially tempted by the latter, given that a fictional character allows one more room to invent (and, in the World of Darkness, this character might even have inspired Mr Benet to include the name in his tale - a tuckerisation of a contemporary villain whose crimes were hushed up as a historic malefactor).<br /> <br /> So our Setite, instead of finding his political career cut short by illness, may have been cheated of his chance at rising high in the service of the United States through being caught out in a nasty habit of strangling the unsuspecting! (It\u2019s possible the perfumed handkerchief referenced in the original story could be interpreted as a souvenir from an unlucky victim).<br /> <br /> <br /> - Hmmm \u2026 this may confuse the timeline a little: \u2018The Devil and Daniel Webster\u2019 was published in AD 1936, rather than in the 19th century as I had supposed.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the \u2018Solicitor-General\u2019 having to argue his way out of a Masquerade breach as a result of this incident might be an excellent addition to his background, no matter when he was actually embraced.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Incidentally, I had rather assumed that the Setite enclave at Cape Cod is something of a \u2018Safe House\u2019 and an informal embassy for the Clan in Camarilla territory (With local Followers of Set being unusually careful not to tread on Camarilla toes, since the Sabbat are more than a little too close for comfort and the Camarilla are a crucial shield against a Black Banquet with some visiting pack of Sabbat).<br /> <br /> I wonder if, making a virtue of necessity, the local Sabbat enclave is something of a \u2018Potemkin Village\u2019, intended to convince visitors that the Setites are an amoral lot, but tolerable neighbours (Whilst the Followers of Set rest from their labours and plot out future developments as they lay low).<br /> <br /> Time, after all, is on their side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T22:34:57-07:00","id":1532481,"title":"","content":"I love the movie &quot;The Devil and Daniel Webster&quot; (also sometimes known as All That Money Can Buy, Here Is the Man, Mr Scratch, or Daniel and the Devil). Walter Huston is great as Mr Scratch. I have it on Criterion Collection's DVD. It's one of my favorites. I first saw it on PBS in 1984.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WjgEKFqbObk\" data-code=\"WjgEKFqbObk\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/WjgEKFqbObk/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> However, my interpretation of such a character would not be as Setite &quot;devil's advocate&quot;, but more as the traditional lawyer-politician in the Federalist/Whig pattern. Probably Ventrue as the stereotype, but nothing wrong with one other of the traditional Camarilla clans. Brujah, Malkavian, Tremere, or Toreador could all equally fit quite easily. Whatever the clan, he'd be a hard bargainer, a collector of boons, and a canny opponent in Elysium. But likely a staunch opponent of the Setites as a member of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> The book and movie's &quot;Jury of the Damned&quot;, is of course, fantastic. And certainly can be its own inspiration as vampire NPCs in a New England setting. If every member of the Jury of the Damned was an NPC, it'd add a lot to a chronicle. Although I'd personally omit a few who were too well known.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0UKag0tlpRY\" data-code=\"0UKag0tlpRY\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/0UKag0tlpRY/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> But I won't say your interpretation is &quot;wrong&quot;. Everyone has their own tastes, and I have a perverse pleasure in seeing other people take my brief ideas and interpret it in their own tastes and biases. My opinions or tastes are not any more wrong or right than yours, so have it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T08:09:32-07:00","id":1532502,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, I\u2019m happy to accept that my own notions are mere suggestions and even more happy to discuss alternate takes on the archetypes (What I would really love to see is several creative types post their take on each of these archetypes, so that we can compare notes: either our takes on an archetype would be easy to reconcile into a single, more fleshed-out composite or we\u2019d have a whole selection of distinct versions who could coexist as friends, rivals, friendly rivals or immortal nemeses).<br /> <br /> One should also admit that I came within a few keystrokes of suggesting Mr Walter Huston for the role of \u2018Solicitor-General to His Wickedness\u2019 (It\u2019s interesting to note that his grandson, Mr Danny Huston, would also make a solid casting choice for my mental image of this character - though I suspect he\u2019d make an excellent Upton Rowlands).<br /> <br /> <br /> Concerning your own suggested Clans, I\u2019d suggest making the archetype a Ventrue only if he were to be depicted as a might-have-been/has-been type, somebody who was enough of a failure to explain why Clan Ventrue didn\u2019t make a more powerful comeback in the region, but with enough successes to make it clear why this person attracted a following (For some reason President Franklin Pierce occurs to me in this context - a man of tragic personal history and considerable personal achievement who ultimately serves as an example of the \u2018Peter Principle\u2019, in that he kept being promoted until ultimately being placed in a role that completely exceeded his powers).<br /> <br /> <br /> Of the other suggested Clans, I suspect that a Brujah makes the most sense on a thematic level - this could very creditably depicted as a character embraced with the notion of his supplying the stabilising influence that would allow Brujah Revolutionaries like Jeremy McNeil to keep doing their thing as a way of keeping New England Brujah country, whilst their childer worked to set that hegemony (and the United States) on a more stable footing in a rather more orderly fashion.<br /> <br /> You know, this is an archetype I can absolutely imagine having some ties to Critias and his ilk, especially if they are of Clan Brujah (Though I tend to assume Critias would prioritise Philadelphia, since he arrived in the New World at approximately the point where it would be the National Capital, and he would almost certainly regard the more populist revolutionaries of New England as rather \u2018below the salt\u2019).<br /> <br /> <br /> It does occur to me that making the \u2018Lawyer-Politician\u2019 a Toreador would neatly explain how they might have served as an inspiration for \u2018The Devil and Daniel Webster\u2019 (and one assumes that this variant of the archetype would have been embraced in admiration of their oratorical abilities, Public Speaking having long been a performance art - though fallen on sad days, since politicians work to produce political soundbites more than political speeches).<br /> <br /> <br /> Finally, I should admit that my decision to make the \u2018Solicitor-General\u2019 (The name is a nod to the Common Law, as well as a highly influential position, but is also meant as a sly nod to Soliciting as a criminal offence) a Setite was mostly bred of my desire to do something interesting with the Followers of Set in New England (and my suspicion that this Clan would allow more sly allusions to dealing with the Devil than any other - not to mention the slightly comical clash of cultures between the convictions of a Pulp Vampire Cult slightly influenced by Ancient Egypt and a Devil\u2019s Advocate out of New England folklore).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-13T08:11:25-07:00","id":1532503,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll do my best to post a shortlist of the Archetype/Clan associations I have in mind for the rest of your list (Possibly with a few alternates in the mix as they occur to me), either tonight or tomorrow, in the interests of comparing notes.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-14T16:36:09-07:00","id":1532623,"title":"","content":"Here are some of the \u2018rough sketches\u2019 for those archetypes suggested on a previous page, basically the \u2018Character Concept\u2019 name that occurred to me and a possible Clan - though in some cases only a name &amp; concept occurred to me.<br /> <br /> One concept not mentioned in the list of archetypes which struck me as very New England was \u2018Puritan Runaway\u2019 - that is, somebody who wearied of the New England quasi-theocracy and decided to head into the wilderness.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s quite easy to imagine this character being snapped up by the Sabbat, assuming the Gangrel don\u2019t take an interest in them.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2018A veteran of the French &amp; Indian or American Revolutionary War\u2019<br /> <br /> ROYAL AMERICAN (Ventrue) A veteran Loyalist who may well have served in both conflicts, but like Robert Rogers wound up on the wrong side of history (Bonus points if he bears a resemblance to Mr John Carradine in DRUMS ALONG THE MOHAWK).<br /> <br /> FRONTIER WOLF (Gangrel) A scout during the French &amp; Indian War who may well have been making war along what is now the New England/Canada border ever since, but is more likely to favour the Camarilla over the Sabbat - because while they don\u2019t want company often, when they do want it they prefer civilised company.<br /> <br /> REDCOAT REVOLUTIONARY (Brujah) One of the many deserters from His Majesty\u2019s forces who was persuaded to enter the American service: unlike most of the others, he\u2019s been a Rebel with a variety of causes ever since.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2018A Hessian Mercenary\u2019<br /> <br /> AMERIKA-J\u00c4GER (Tremere) I believe that the \u2018Hessians\u2019 entered British service only after His Majesty\u2019s forces were ousted from Boston, so I wonder if this military contractor may have seen service elsewhere in the Thirteen Colonies, but been \u2018acquired\u2019 after some disaster (Like Saratoga) left them at a loose end.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, one thought \u2018Tremere\u2019 because the Warlocks do need soldiers and may well have appreciated a professional without local ties to compromise their loyalty to the Clan.<br /> <br /> My mental image of the character might have returned to Germany at some point, only to be ousted by the Prince of Berlin when that horrible man started his purges (and having returned to New England because he had some experience of the local personalities).<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2018New England lawyer-politician\u2019<br /> <br /> BY THE BOOK ANARCH (Brujah) A scholarly member of a frequently-roughneck Clan who made his bones pleading down the penalties inflicted upon their Clan mates by local princes and seeking to improve the excessively Feudal status quo prevailing in Camarilla territories.<br /> <br /> Might be an especially interesting twist on the archetype if this is a Political WIFE who found the Embrace offered her opportunities not open to her in life.<br /> <br /> <br /> JUDGE OF THE UNSEEN (Tremere) An educated gentleman who tried to have evidence acquired by \u2018Supernatural\u2019 sources dismissed from consideration during the Witch Trials (or at least seriously reconsidered), having done sufficient due diligence to attract the interest of Clan Tremere.<br /> <br /> Had been doing his best to avert future Witch Hunts while ferreting out Malevolent Sorcerers ever since.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2018A Trancendentalist philosopher/author\u2019<br /> <br /> EVERYDAY MIRACLE (Malkavian) My brief research into this particular school of thought taught me enough to recognise a relatively optimistic view of the world somewhat difficult to sustain amidst a society as inherently Damnable as that of the Kindred.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, given the philosophies\u2019 deep attachment to the idea of divinity pervading all nature and humanity, a Malkavian character deeply attached to this philosophy would be a potentially interesting case study in a person adhering to their beliefs even under the most stringent tests \u2026 especially if they believe that God literally speaks to them and what they hear worries them!<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2018A Boston Abolitionist\u2019<br /> <br /> BOSTON BEGUM (Ventrue) Since we have no fewer than two black, Brujah conductors on the Underground Railroad, it stuck me that making this character a Boston lady (The other pillar of the Abolitionists, back in the day) might be interesting.<br /> <br /> It also struck me that, since one assumes that the Slave South could well have been a stronghold for Ventrue antitribu of the most feudal sort, showing an \u2018Old Money\u2019 Ventrue seek to \u2018do well by doing good\u2019 in the interests of tearing down the semi-feudal order of the Old South (In the interests of creating a more modern United States) might offer an interesting angle on the Abolitionist movement.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, the name is a nod to the \u2018Boston Brahmin\u2019 (With a \u2018Begum\u2019 being an Indian rank for a Royal lady).<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2018Someone Involved with the Hartford Convention\u2019<br /> <br /> GREEN MOUNTAIN REBEL (Brujah) Someone who served the Vermont Republic before it was officially part of the United States and was perfectly willing to see it become part of British North America if the Pennsylvania crowd didn\u2019t see sense: the perceived follies of \u2018Mr Madison\u2019s War\u2019 saw them revive the idea of New England going it\u2019s own way, but once again forestalled by events as they developed.<br /> <br /> Doubled down on All-American Unity to compensate, then found their career stalled out in the long-term because this drove them collaborate enthusiastically with the Slave South (At least to the extent of backing some unseemly concessions), with rumours of their being an outright Copperhead during the War Between the States being kept current by rivals.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2018Someone involved with the New England shipping industry\u2019<br /> <br /> YOUNG IRONSIDES (Brujah) Claims to have served on \u2018Old Ironsides\u2019 itself and verifiably a naval officer in the War of 1812 - has been Roman Pendragon\u2019s amphibious operations expert and one of his lieutenants since being convinced that the man wasn\u2019t so British as to compromise the interests of the United States.<br /> <br /> His coterie-patrol are affectionately known as the \u2018Sea Dogs\u2019.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2018Boston Irish\u2019<br /> <br /> TEAGUE (Brujah) An Irishman of Protestant ancestry who played some role in the protests culminating in the \u2018King Street Incident\u2019 (and who STILL resents Lawyer John Adams\u2019 rather rude description of the protestors during his arguments in defence of the British regulars involved.<br /> <br /> Sometimes claims to have been an indentured servant auctioned off to the highest bidder, but usually only as a way of downplaying their acute disinterest of being roped into the Underground Railroad while Irishmen were being attacked and mistreated in the streets of Boston.<br /> <br /> Has been a stalwart (or depending on your perspective part of the scenery) on the Boston docks for a very long time.<br /> <br /> <br /> PURITAN WHISPERER (Nosferatu) An Irish American who, having arrived in Boston as a very young child in the 1820s, was well-placed to serve his community and advocate for the tidal wave of new Irish who arrived as a result of the potato famine.<br /> <br /> A good Catholic lad and contributor to the Parish newsletter, he was lucky enough to stumble onto vampires feeding off the sickly &amp; vulnerable in the quarantine hospitals on Deer Island only after he\u2019d made himself useful by making life more difficult for Caiphas Smith - the latter being almost as eager to pillory Catholics as he was to prosecute his war on the Undead - resulting in his becoming a deeply unhappy Kindred.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, his transformation gave him plenty of time to polish his writing, make life a little easier for his old community AND put his pre- and post-mortem knowledge of Old Smith to good use.<br /> <br /> <br /> WILD COLONIAL (Brujah) Smiling Jack, being a vampire powerfully against all manner of authority, has been known to signal his defiance of a local Prince by embracing childer without asking consent.<br /> <br /> Being a git, Smiling Jack frequently leaves these childer to face the consequences of his actions: luckily for this particular creation, Roman Pendragon needed recruits and was willing to accept this roaring puppy as one of his Hounds.<br /> <br /> This Wild Colonial Boy has been dividing his time between wrecking the Sabbat and running amuck on Rest &amp; Recuperation ever since \u2026 and him a former Altar Boy too.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2018Someone representing the financial &amp; insurance industry\u2019<br /> <br /> INSURANCE DOUBLE AGENT (Giovanni/Milner/Hecata) Given the role of the Milner-Giovanni as \u2018bankroll\u2019 for the Triat in preference for the still-somewhat hostile Ventrue of New England and given the intelligence gathering opportunities offerred to insurance agencies in a time &amp; place where various damages need to be collected and/or hushed up, it seemed credible to imagine a Milner quietly making themselves useful by keeping an eye on the Insurance Business.<br /> <br /> Bonus points if they DO NOT run the occasional \u2018Insurance Job\u2019 for the extra dollars.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2018Someone representing Old Industries\u2019<br /> <br /> STAKEHOLDER (Toreador) That name is a pun on the ease with which somebody associated with the furniture business can lay their hands on the traditional instrument for dispatching a vampire and I will be making NO APOLOGIES.<br /> <br /> Now please excuse me while I twirl my moustache and point out that there\u2019s something inherently interesting in a Kindred who has had an eye for woodwork since the items in question were the Next Big Thing and hasn\u2019t given up that interest now that they\u2019re antiques.<br /> <br /> Bonus points if the whole business has left them an old, much-resented antagonist of the New England Garou, for reasons that should be obvious.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2018Someone representing New Industries\u2019<br /> <br /> BIG GUN (Ventrue) Given that Colt have had premises in Hartford, Connecticut since the mid-to-late 1850s, this might technically be more at home with the Old Industries - in any case, given the Ventrue stronghold in Connecticut and their sensible focus on the Sinews of War, it\u2019s not hard to imagine them working to acquire an interest in the local gun industry.<br /> <br /> Whether that gun industry is now owned by Pentex I leave to the reader\u2019s discretion.<br /> <br /> <br /> YESTERDAY\u2019S GENIUS (Tremere) As a scientist you are entirely prepared to accept that technology has moved on even faster than you expected it to, but you don\u2019t have to like it.<br /> <br /> Still, you\u2019re more than smart enough to pick up some new tricks and happy to see what can be done about exploring the places where Science mingles with the Sorcerous, all in the interests of the Clan.<br /> <br /> It STILL bothers you when a certain sort of person flinches or giggles on hearing the surname \u2018West\u2019 connected to such a mind, but you\u2019ll be d****ed if you ask those cretins why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28339,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","user":"Atticus Cleanclaw","date":".  Formatting alteration 03-14-2024, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-16T20:30:08-07:00","id":1532749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1532623#post1532623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One concept not mentioned in the list of archetypes which struck me as very New England was \u2018Puritan Runaway\u2019 - that is, somebody who wearied of the New England quasi-theocracy and decided to head into the wilderness.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a neat idea as well. It's an interesting initial concept, and the vampire could have developed in many different ways since then. That person would definitely be an elder by now. So one of the more influential Kindred if it survived, or just as an interesting vampire that started a local lineage descended from it.<br /> <br /> You have a lot of good stuff beginnings based on the initial historical concept to become a good character. Some of your selections are very original and not obvious but still make sense given their concepts, so double points for those.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-18T04:55:27-07:00","id":1532806,"title":"","content":"Thank You most kindly <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> - I wanted to try putting a little spin on the archetypes, rather than just go with the most straightforward translation (I\u2019m also planning to look through the old Clanbook Archetypes thread to see which of them would work best in Dark Colony, though it may take me a little while to sort through so many possibilities).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T05:25:38-07:00","id":1532845,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve just been reminded that there was at least one presumably-Major (Possibly former) player in the Kindred society of Boston whom I don\u2019t believe to have been previously mentioned in this thread: Sir Matthew Lubbock, a Toreador of the FOURTH Generation, sire of Christopher Houghton of Los Angeles.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Matthew_Lubbock\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Matthew_Lubbock</a><br /> <br /> <br /> He seems to have been active in Boston from the Revolutionary War era, but I\u2019d bet that his childe\u2019s disgrace would have encouraged him to either enter torpor or leave the continent, possibly leaving childer or grand-childer in the area.<br /> <br /> His fate remains an open question, but it\u2019s also interesting to wonder if \u2018Sir Matthew Lubbock\u2019 is a non-de-plume for one of the known Toreador methuselahs of the Fourth Generation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T05:26:42-07:00","id":1532846,"title":"","content":"Almost forgot to add: if a vampire of this generation were known to be active in the area, then it\u2019s easy to understand why the Sabbat would remain active despite having mixed to no luck making gains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T17:02:12-07:00","id":1532877,"title":"","content":"Christopher Houghton is one of the least interesting aspects of Los Angeles by Night. There's no reason for him to be such a powerful generation like 5, and that makes his 4th generation sire, Sir Matthew Lubbock, a cipher. (Sir Matthew is actually called LUDLOW in the text, but called Lubbock on the character sheet as Christopher's sire). (Lubbock is an English name. Ludlow is a Welsh name.) All other methusalehs tend to be ancient vampires with mythological names, meaning they either were those figures of legend, inspired them, or were mistaken for them. Instead all we know is that he woke up from torpor in the late 17th century. So we know Sir Matthew has been around since at least the late 1300s. So is he incredibly ancient, having gone through extended series of torpors, and only uses Sir Matthew Lubbock as an alias to fit in? Or is that his real name? If so, it's highly unlikely the Toreador Antedeluvian sired him - he would have diablerized his way to 4th generation.<br /> <br /> Lubbock is referred to as &quot;one of the Toreador hostages in London&quot;. This is in reference to lore first mentioned in the original World of Darkness where the 1693 Treaty of Durham that ended the conflict between Ventrue and Toreador in the British Isles. The Toreador would be safe in their traditional stronghold of Edinburgh, and in return they would not seek power in London outside Elysium or support the Tremere. Any Toreador in London now held the status of &quot;hostages&quot;. Presumably if the Toreador reneged, Mithras would have killed all the London Toreador. As such, I cannot think Sir Matthew must be all that powerful. He's clearly weak enough that Mithras felt he could destroy him and all other Toreador in London. We also know that when Bonnie Prince Charlie did land in Scotland and rebelled, that Mithras did eventually destroy some London Toreador in reprisal and blood bond others to him. So when Sir Matthew left afterwards for Boston, it must have been in response to the failure. It was his way of avoiding being destroyed or blood bond to Mithras.<br /> <br /> As such, I believe he must have diablerized his way to 4th generation, and is likely far less powerful than Mithras. Possibly during the time of the Anarch Revolt. He seems influential enough in Toreador salons that he must have some status, so it is likely he's an elder. He might have been an early Anarch Toreador that defected to the Camarilla, or he diablerized some 4th generation Anarch/Sabbat. But I think that period of time is when he must have done it. Still that begs the question of what 4th generation vampire could he have diablerized?<br /> <br /> The basic story of Lubbock and Houghton is OK as long as you don't make them 4th and 5th generation. If they were say 6th and 7th, it'd work much better IMO. The only reason for Christopher to be 5th is that the writers seemed incapable of not having some powerfully potent blooded vampire secretly responsible for everything that has happened. The setting suffered for essentially including a joke comment about the status of Hollywood movies as &quot;art&quot;. I think he'd just be as effective in that role as someone around say Tyler's, Khalid's, or Annabelle's power level in Chicago. No need to have such potent blood.<br /> <br /> However one may change the details of their generation, I don't think there's a problem to include Sir Matthew and Christopher to be in Boston between 1746-1830 or so. If neither sired any children, it's just a curiosity. So the best thing in my opinion is to have at least one local Toreador descended from one of them. Again, if so better for them to be of less potent generation. We might also want to tie Sir Matthew and Christopher to other Toreador refugees from London arriving in Boston. In any event, the arrival of these Toreador just prior to the American Revolution makes them natural allies of Brujah like Jeremy MacNeil and others who overthrew the original Ventrue princes here. So some nice things can happen by including these characters. I'd personally just make their generation less potent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-22T15:40:49-07:00","id":1533021,"title":"","content":"That seems a sensible idea - one must admit that the mental image of Sir Matthew (By whatever surname) being more or less Lazlo Cravendale played with an emphasis on the \u2018horror\u2019 in \u2018horror-comedy\u2019 (and possibly even putting on a deeply suspect Scots accent to boot) visited me at some<br /> point and declines to leave (With deeply chummy, honey-voiced menaces).<br /> <br /> Oh God, now I\u2019ve gotten a mental image of Sir Matthew and Critias of Clan Brujah having a discussion of <i>erastes</i> and <i>eromenos</i> that is, with Christopher watching from the sidelines and occasionally being admired, deeply creepy.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Concerning Christopher Houghton himself, a review of LA BY NIGHT on another forum suggested that he might well be a parody of the tendency to depict some shadowy ancient of potent bites being behind everything and I really like the idea: LA BY NIGHT sounds quite gleefully OTT to start with, so making the local shadowy mastermind <i>exactly</i> the sort of Cainite who would cultivate a city where katanas &amp; trench coats are not optional and mayhem a nightly facet of existence (and an affectionate parody of \u2018A methuselah did it!\u2019 plotting to boot) works for me.<br /> <br /> I should probably admit that making \u2018Hollywood Dracula\u2019 the LA Kindred\u2019s answer to \u2018Emperor Norton\u2019 of San Francisco wins that sourcebook a warm place in my heart, whatever it\u2019s actual quality: this is 100% more entertaining than the ACTUAL World of Darkness Dracula (and probably 75-88% of other Draculas).<br /> <br /> <br /> - I tend to lean more towards \u2018Matthew Lubbock/Ludlow\u2019 (Ludlow is, if memory serves, specifically a castle in the Marches of Wales) an alias employed by a Methselah; this makes his inclusion as one of the Toreador hostages in London more interesting, since it suggests that he\u2019s something of a \u2018Ringer\u2019: a vampire potent enough (or thought to be potent enough) that Mithras himself might actually think before ordering the execution of his hostages (or at least enough of a Tough Nut that Mithras would lose a few teeth biting down).<br /> <br /> It also occurs to me that having Sir Matthew quit London following the \u201845 as much because he couldn\u2019t be bothered to risk his neck for the sake of clan-mates foolish enough to get caught up in something as quixotic as Jacobite pretensions might be darkly amusing (Especially if this comes as the anticlimax to Mithras &amp; Sir Matthew spending a century or so genteelly trying to puzzle out which of them is more murderously potent without ever quite coming to blows).<br /> <br /> <br /> - On a more serious note, it\u2019s interesting to wonder if Sir Matthew played some role in Roman Pendragon\u2019s failed putsch in Victorian Britain: it\u2019s easy to imagine the former embracing the opportunity to simultaneously put some distance between his Idiot Fail Childe\u2019s Ultimate Failure AND pay off some grudges against Mithras by making mischief in Edinburgh (Which, going by the White Wolf wiki\u2019s list of Princes seems to have been contested between rival princes at some point during the Victorian era), for the sake of making it easier to overthrow the Ventrue supremacy in the Isles that Mithras et al had so proudly established.<br /> <br /> <br /> - As for the possibility of there being a childe or grand-childe of Sir Matthew in New England, it\u2019s easy to imagine Christopher\u2019s Grand Project being an effort to win his sire\u2019s support for Christopher\u2019s appeal to finally be allowed to embrace a child\u2019s of his own (Though it\u2019s not impossible Christopher might have made life more difficult for everyone by illegally embracing a childe and then trying to get his sire to pass the new Kindred off as his own).<br /> <br /> Doubtless any local descendant would STILL hide his face in shame at the mere mention of Christopher\u2019s complete failure as a Toreador (I am, of course, convinced that neither Christopher or his Sire would be taking very much attention in the fairer sex, even when everything else about a possible Childe is open to speculation).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-22T15:43:51-07:00","id":1533022,"title":"","content":"By the way, that thread on various Pregenerated characters a little down the front page of this sub-forum is taking a bit longer to work through than I thought, but I have been able to identify one archetype with explicit ties to New England so far (She is, admittedly, a Tremere with family ties to Salem whose character concept is \u2018Professional Witch\u2019 but there would have to be at least one of those about the World of Darknesses, I suppose).<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-22T23:41:50-07:00","id":1533032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1533022#post1533022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, that thread on various Pregenerated characters a little down the front page of this sub-forum is taking a bit longer to work through than I thought, but I have been able to identify one archetype with explicit ties to New England so far (She is, admittedly, a Tremere with family ties to Salem whose character concept is \u2018Professional Witch\u2019 but there would have to be at least one of those about the World of Darknesses, I suppose).<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates?p=1391102#post1391102\">Professional Witch</a> from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> thread of Pre-made Vampire characters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-05T11:30:46-07:00","id":1533625,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, I do indeed - one must admit that I\u2019ve been remiss in not yet completing my read through of that thread with an eye to picking out archetypes especially suited to the Dark Colony: my working notes indicate that the College Professor (Brujah), The Archon in Training (Gangrel), The Horror Writer (Toreador) and the Anarch Wannabe (Ventrue) struck me as especially fit for the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-06T13:44:12-07:00","id":1533717,"title":"","content":"I think those would all be good concepts for the New England setting. One can easily turn them into viable NPCs with local flavor.<br /> <br /> If we assume that there is a long standing presence of elder Gangrel with potent blood on the East Coast, combined with a safe zone for the Camarilla in southern New England, and an active counter-insurgency against the Sabbat in order to keep it safe, then that might be a perfect place for training for future Gangrel Archons. Maybe a former archon present in the region doing it on his own, or someone sent by Justicar Xavier to oversee the region while Xavier travels across the rest of the United States. Certainly a local Wolfpack equivalent can be justified with someone else doing the job of Archon Tyrus and a small hierarchy around her.<br /> <br /> Given the Brujah Prince of &quot;Concord&quot; and the Ventrue losing power in Boston and only keeping Connecticut, a Ventrue &quot;anarch wannabe&quot; in the Boston area would make sense. With any Ventrue still residing in that domain likely subservient to more powerful vampires of other clans, a Ventrue neonate who decides going anarch is the only viable way to obtain local power has a certain logic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T05:53:20-07:00","id":1533811,"title":"","content":"As it happens I was also drawn to the \u2018Chantry War\u2019 between the backers of Madeline Coventry and \u2018Baladin\u2019, whom the Tremere sent to replace her (With the Salem chantry backing Coventry and Boston accepting Baladin\u2019s authority: I wonder if Providence would have done it\u2019s best to keep clear or would instead have sought to play each side against the other?).<br /> <br /> Actually, there\u2019s more than a few unanswered questions hanging over this incident from the Dark Colony\u2019s history that leave me wondering if the reason for Coventry being ousted (or at least given her marching orders) was because the Tremere leadership (Fairly or unfairly) suspected that Madeline Coventry was a bit <i>too</i> close to the Sabbat, after spending so long in the wilds, a long way off from the pyramid.<br /> <br /> My understanding of the timeline is:-<br /> <br /> AD 1635 - Madeline Coventry sets out from the Winchester chantry in Old England at the order of her elders, seeking to evade Mithras after he resumes his old feud against their Clan<br /> <br /> Notably she is supposed to have been the first Kindred in Boston (and to have been ousted, along with the Brujah, not long thereafter as the Ventrue sweep in - though the exact period of time is unspecified, one might assume that the Ventrue victory in the English Civil War had something to do with it)<br /> <br /> <br /> AD 1692 - Coventry establishes her chantry in the wake of the Witch Hunts (Apparently embracing mortal mages of some sort, to the point where she is described as having several childer: Mention of something called the \u2018Ur Codex\u2019 playing a key role in their rituals)<br /> <br /> <br /> AD 1783 - Ventrue ousted in New England, Coventry having allied with the Brujah and others to ensure that this would be the case, after which point Sabbat (Operating from what is now Maine) launched their own efforts to exploit the disruptions of the Revolutionary War to fill a perceived leadership vacuum; it is at this time that the Tremere Reestablish themselves in Boston and create their chantry (Even as the Sabbat attack Camarilla holdings in the Boston area)<br /> <br /> <br /> 1783-1795 - At some point in this period Sprenger, a local (It\u2019s not specified in my source whether \u2018local\u2019 means \u2018New England\u2019 or \u2018Salem\u2019) Sabbat leader wages what appears to be a personal, though unspecified Grudge against Madeline Coventry; it is possible she diablerises him at some point during this period<br /> <br /> Given that the \u2018Chantry War\u2019 is said to have lasted almost half a century, despite Baladin and Coventry being known to have contested for the supremacy only between AD 1795 and some point before 1831, I wonder if the divide between Salem and Boston may have begun at some point during this period, possibly due to objections to Coventry\u2019s conduct of operations during the conflict.<br /> <br /> N.B. I\u2019m assuming that Coventry split her time between Salem and Boston during this period, which may or may not have helped.<br /> <br /> <br /> AD 1795 - One Baladin, a Tremere Elder, is sent out by the Winchester chantry to replace her as leader of the Clan in New England; feeling betrayed, Coventry engages Baladin in a spectacular duel, but is wounded and flees to Salem, where she enters torpor.<br /> <br /> Despite Baladin\u2019s best efforts he cannot locate her and when Coventry arises again, she \u201cbuilt her own chantry\u201d and a coven loyal to her, entering into a long conflict with Baladin and Boston.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, the exact phrasing of the original suggests that either the Salem chantry had been abandoned by this point (and Coventry rebuilt it) or that Madeline Coventry, under the very noses of the existing Salem chantry, built her own establishment.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also unclear as to how long her torpor lasted.<br /> <br /> <br /> AD 1831 - At some point prior to this Baladin has been found dead in the Boston chantry, presumed dead through the efforts of Madeline or the Black Hand (Known enemies of his); in this year Madeline Coventry disappears and is also presumed dead.<br /> <br /> Shortly afterwards the Sabbat launch a raid on the Salem Chantry: rumours that the Inner Circle of the Camarilla become involved after this point abound, but in any case the Chantry War is over.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, I hope you can see why all this set my antennae a-twitching: the timing of Coventry\u2019s disappearance and the ensuing raid on the Salem chantry is \u2018interesting\u2019 and the Tremere elders deciding to replace her after their woman in New England has played a key role in restoring their fortunes in the region (After a century or so in the wilderness) is also curious, especially after her apparent destruction of a Sabbat leader of real significance.<br /> <br /> In all honesty, I\u2019m wonder if somebody in the late 1700s assumed that Madeline Coventry accused her of being hand in glove with the Sabbat and the Tremere elders of Winchester (An ocean away, it must be said) decided there was enough substance to the allegations for a replacement to be sent out, which may or may not have ultimately led to Coventry actually joining the Sabbat (Willingly or unwillingly), with her disappearance and the ensuing raid being used to cover her tracks.<br /> <br /> Either that or her defeat of Baladin might have left her exposed to observing Sabbat with grudges lingering from the days after the Revolutionary War \u2026 or elements within the Camarilla itself might have decided to get rid of her on the quiet, possibly to make sure there would be no purges by the victors of this bitter struggle.<br /> <br /> <br /> In any case, there are quite a lot of question marks hanging over this conflict and the characters involved: I\u2019m certainly going to offer my character sketches for Baladin and Sorenger at some point, since very little is known about either (Heck, we don\u2019t even know much about who Madeline Coventry WAS, as opposed to what she did, so that\u2019s another blank space that may need to be filled in).<br /> <br /> More on this later (and my apologies if I haven\u2019t explained my point as clearly as I would like to).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T12:32:07-07:00","id":1533835,"title":"","content":"The Tremere infighting is definitely underdeveloped. It's one of those things you think is going to play a large part in the regional setting, but then is just forgotten about. So it's minor local flavor. STs could definitely take it as a plot hook and develop it on their own, but one would think it'd be something the writers of Dark Colony should have provided more details on.<br /> <br /> I believe Dark Colony said Coventry's torpor lasted &quot;more than a year&quot; which implies it was between 1-2 years.<br /> <br /> I also have some questions about the Tremere during this time.<br /> <br /> First, when exactly did Councillor Meerlinda take over responsibility for North America and move there? The first Tremere clanbook is very vague. It says that as Puritan colonists arrived in New England in the 17th century, Meerlinda was responsible for her role of leading the Tremere in the British Isles. Then over 100 years as the potential of the New World grew, the Tremere would establish the rank of Pontifex and the geographic spheres of the Tremere Council would change with Meerlinda being given North America, and that she succeeded growing the clan there more than her counterpart Xavier de Cincao did with South America.<br /> <br /> The absence of any mention of Meerlinda in Dark Colony implies she went elsewhere - perhaps New York or Philadelphia before eventually moving on? But New England seems to have been very important to the Tremere, so it is somewhat surprising she decided not to go there. Though if we assume prior to the Revolution that New England was a stronghold of Mithras aligned Ventrue, it would make sense Meerlinda would have wanted to go elsewhere to set up shop given the problems the Tremere had with Mithras in Britain. Or maybe Meerlinda did not pack up and leave until after the 1831 feud ended and the Tremere had already lost much power in New England. I'm leaning towards that second option.<br /> <br /> Incidentally in her character description at the back of the clanbook, it's mentioned that Meerlinda's Tremere have had several failures in New England including the destruction of the Boston Chantry several years ago (as of 1994). While this could possibly have referred to the 1831 feud resulting in Boston chantry Tremere fleeing to Hartford (along with the survivors of the Salem Chantry), a 150 year old even is unlikely to be described as &quot;several years ago&quot;. But Dark Colony only mentions a Boston chantry post-1831 in the context of Zachariah Slane wanting to rebuild it, but denied by John Reiss.<br /> <br /> I suspect despite Dark Colony coming out before the Tremere Clanbook, that the clanbook was not really written trying to incorporate the lore of the other, and there's just a lot of cracks if trying to view them as a whole.<br /> <br /> Second, when did House Goratrix of the Tremere anti-tribu arrive in North America? The first Tremere clanbook says it was only in the mid-18th century that it was discovered that Goratrix joined the Sabbat. When Goratrix actually joined is more of a mystery. But certainly there could have been secret Tremere anti-tribu in New England very early posing as Camarilla loyal Tremere. That might be one explanation behind the &quot;Chantry War.&quot; It's possible some members of Coventry's chantry were secretly of House Goratrix and that this was finally revealed after the rite was done to reveal the Tremere anti-tribu. Coventry might have tried to hide that and pass it off as apprentices infighting. Maybe Meerlinda got suspicious, sent Baladin to take charge, and asked Coventry to return to Britain. Coventry, fearing she'd be killed as a traitor, then tried to kill Baladin and remain in North America.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T12:42:48-07:00","id":1533840,"title":"","content":"Right after I posted this, I found relevant information in the first Tremere clanbook.<br /> <br /> John Diamond from Marblehead, MA was embraced by Meelinda shortly after her arrival in North America. So it seems Meerlinda was in fact in New England.<br /> <br /> John Diamond dwells in a chantry in Bridgeport, CT. He seems to be a Pontifex interested in North American trade &amp; business who visits Wall Street often, so this may be a unique chantry to him and he's not actually part of the Hartford chantry (which we moved to Providence in this thread). <br /> <br /> So we might consider his interests to reside mostly outside the region, but it's important to note he dwells within, albeit at its SW edge near NYC. As a 5th generation Tremere or around 150-250 years, it's kind of important to note his presence there. Of course, coming from the Tremere clanbook published a year afterwards, the writer of Dark Colony likely did not intend of such a powerful and potent blooded Tremere being in the region.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T13:19:55-07:00","id":1533844,"title":"","content":"There are excellent points - and it\u2019s interesting that Melinda Coventry and Meerlinda of Wessex have such similar names (At least as I understand their pronunciation, \u2018MEH-lin-da\u2019 and \u2018Mere-Linda\u2019 respectively): could \u2018Melinda Coventry\u2019 have been an alias adopted to throw possible rivals off the scent of a much older vampire? (Probably as a decoy, rather than a nom-de-plume).<br /> <br /> - A related thought: could Meerlinda of Wessex have originally headed for Mexico, rather than for New England, when she was sent to North America? (After all, in the early nights of European settlement Spanish North America would have seemed the richer prospect by far and the Camarilla - or at least elements within same - might well have wanted to take steps to prevent Sabbat domination, however unsuccessfully).<br /> <br /> <br /> If Meerlinda were not already in-country at that point, then showing her arrive in North America circa AD 1831 would make a great deal of sense: in this version of things the death of Baladin and the disappearance of Melinda Coventry would represent the new Head Wizard quietly cleaning up an old and embarrassing mess, while putting the pieces into place for a triumphant arrival in the United States (Free from any potential for such unpleasantness as greeted Baladin on his arrival).<br /> <br /> This take on things would work especially well if Melinda Coventry were herself a childe of Meerlinda sent to keep an eye on the American colonies of her sire\u2019s troublesome British assignment: Coventry\u2019s success in ousting the Ventrue might therefore prove a dangerous success under the circumstances, requiring her sire to send out a replacement as a sop to the overmighty British Ventrue (Nursing a grudge over the American Revolution aggravated by the much more directly dangerous French Revolution that was it\u2019s direct sequel).<br /> <br /> Melinda Coventry\u2019s sense of betrayal under these circumstances would therefore be all the more acute - especially if she had some reason to dislike or distrust Baladin, or at least regard those Tremere willing to support him with particular suspicion.<br /> <br /> Honestly, a lot depends on the exact personalities involved, so we\u2019d have to work out the key players involved before we could say more in detail: I do like the idea that Meerlinda only arrived in the United States after AD 1831: it would have probably taken that long for Kindred elders to be convinced that the United States was destined to be not only Big, but enduring (and by that point Mithras would have been absent from London on one of his sojourns for almost thirty years, allowing Meerlinda much more freedom to relocate than would have been the case if a Big, Angry Methuselah were watching the Tremere like an angry buzzard).<br /> <br /> <br /> One scenario that I think might work especially well would be if Melinda and Baladin were both from the line of Meerlinda, probably as rough contemporaries: My assumption is that Melinda Coventry would be an ancilla at the time of her passage to the New World (Probably a fairly young one whom Meerlinda herself could depend on to handle independent operations, but not so valuable her services were indispensable) suggesting she had been a vampire between 50-100 years (I would suggest placing her at the younger end of that range, young enough to understand, and possibly have family connections to, the Pilgrim Fathers), probably embraced in the mid-to-late 1500s.<br /> <br /> If Baladin were an elder in 1795, he\u2019d probably have been Embraced no later than the mid-1500s: it\u2019s possible he may have been her broodmate, but an even more interesting possibility is that he was her sire and she was his first childe - their dynamic becomes even more interesting and their rivalry more painful if there\u2019s a blood connection.<br /> <br /> Even if they were broodmates, rather than Sire and Childe, the idea that he was her \u2018handler\u2019 (Keeping her updated on European affairs, pleading her case to the Elders and receiving her information from North America) is an angle that I think would help make the selection of Baladin as her replacement institutionally-logical and personally-painful.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll try to post my character sketches for Melinda Coventry, Baladin and Sprenger tomorrow: my only addition for tonight is to suggest that Sprenger (With that Germanic name) might work best as an antitribu from a Clan with reasons to hold a grudge against the Tremere (Gangrel or Nosferatu?) possibly even an individual with personal connections to the Omen War, though not necessarily personal experience of that era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T13:22:28-07:00","id":1533845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1533840#post1533840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right after I posted this, I found relevant information in the first Tremere clanbook.<br /> <br /> John Diamond from Marblehead, MA was embraced by Meelinda shortly after her arrival in North America. So it seems Meerlinda was in fact in New England.<br /> <br /> John Diamond dwells in a chantry in Bridgeport, CT. He seems to be a Pontifex interested in North American trade &amp; business who visits Wall Street often, so this may be a unique chantry to him and he's not actually part of the Hartford chantry (which we moved to Providence in this thread).<br /> <br /> So we might consider his interests to reside mostly outside the region, but it's important to note he dwells within, albeit at its SW edge near NYC. As a 5th generation Tremere or around 150-250 years, it's kind of important to note his presence there. Of course, coming from the Tremere clanbook published a year afterwards, the writer of Dark Colony likely did not intend of such a powerful and potent blooded Tremere being in the region.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there anything more fun than playing \u2018Join the Dots\u2019 with many, many years of oft-contradictory canon?\ud83d\ude09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28339,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","user":"Atticus Cleanclaw","date":".  Used exclamation mark in place of a question mark 04-08-2024, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T15:34:40-07:00","id":1533908,"title":"","content":"I wanted to pop in and apologise for not posting anything substantial today - other commitments and my own tendency to distraction hit me right in the work ethic!<br /> <br /> One did, however, learn the interesting fact that at least one theatre of the First Sabbat Civil War actually began in New England (Under the cover of Shay\u2019s Rebellion in AD 1786), which makes me wonder if Sabbat attacks on Camarilla holdings around Boston were a bid to shift all that aggression onto an outside party (That the period of war between 1786 and 1803 saw major gains for the Camarilla in North America, but Ivory Tower assets in New England apparently suffer serious reverses may help explain why Melinda Coventry was supplanted by Baladin).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-11T13:27:20-07:00","id":1534044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1533908#post1533908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One did, however, learn the interesting fact that at least one theatre of the First Sabbat Civil War actually began in New England (Under the cover of Shay\u2019s Rebellion in AD 1786)</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the first time I have ever heard of this. I reviewed my old copies of the original Sabbat Players and Storyteller's Guides and then the Revised era Guide of the Sabbat. Scratching my head, I finally looked up the White Wolf Wiki's entry on the Sabbat Civil Wars, saw it mentioned, and looked up the reference that put this in Giovanni Chronicles III (published in 1998)!<br /> <br /> When it comes to the Sabbat Civil Wars, we're definitely at the point where we need to ask are we on Earth-II where Alan Scott is Green Lantern with a magic lamp, Earth-I where it is Hal Jordan as part of the space faring Green Lantern Corps, post-Crisis where both exist, or one of the other resets of the DC universe with its own continuity, because the details of the Sabbat Civil Wars are all over the place.<br /> <br /> The original Sabbat guides had little details on how many civil wars occurred or when they happened. What little we do have implies there was a civil war during the great Camarilla-Sabbat Jyhads in the &quot;early years&quot; (likely during the 17th century or so, because we must remember it took quite some time before the Anarchs who rejected the Convention of Thorns to turn into the Sabbat) which resulted in the original Code of Milan, another one that lasted around 1800s to early 1900s (roughly) that resulted in the revised Code of Milan of 1933, and the &quot;last&quot; war which saw the creation of the Panders in the 1950s. But it's not clear if these were the only civil wars.<br /> <br /> Guide to the Sabbat introduced the Revised era's canon of three civil wars. The first started in the late eighteenth century and lasted around 30 years ending with the Purchase Pact. The second lasting seventy years between 1863-1933, and a third civil war lasting 100 days in 1957. The two timelines are not actually compatible, but do bear some similarities. (This is not unusual as the Revised era saw a lot of writers creating backstory but didn't seem to read previous sourcebooks very closely or perhaps purposefully retconned stuff.) So STs will need to pick what they like as they create their own history for their games.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like the earlier version which seemed to describe a situation where the newly formed Sabbat grew large, tried to take on the Camarilla directly in the 17th-18th centuries, got almost destroyed, and the survivors either escaped to distant areas of Europe like northern Scandinavia, retreated to certain strongholds like Milan, or fled to the New World. They then lost hold of much of the New World from a concerted Camarilla expansion, and this lead to another civil war that saw the sect centralize in response. But everyone will have their own preferences for the timeline.<br /> <br /> Giovani Chronicles III's idea of the Sabbat Civil War beginning from Shay's Rebellion doesn't hold for the original canon. Not only is the timeline different, but the history of Dark Colony (and geography) would not allow for a Sabbat civil war to erupt in western Massachusetts. But if you want to reconcile the two, perhaps some feud between the Lasombra and Sabbat at that time would eventually lead to the second civil war. The big problem I have with this idea is that this period saw the Camarilla expanding in the New World, New England was a Camarilla stronghold as several clans conspired to remove the local Ventrue from leadership, and the Sabbat would not really become a threat until post Civil War 1860s-1890s. The main Sabbat danger to New England before the Civil War likely came from its &quot;control&quot; of Canada, particularly Montreal, and having lots of nomad packs of Country Gangrel in the wilderness. Sticking the Lasombra and Tzimisce in western Massachusetts that somehow survived so they could start a Sabbat Civil War is kind of silly IMO. It creates more problems than it solves, and it isn't necessary to include the Sabbat in the history of New England.<br /> <br /> Now Dark Colony's own history is not perfectly aligned with the general Sabbat outline in the original guides either. Their period of greatest threat to the New England Camarilla (and takeover of New York City) for a thirty year period post-Civil War is when both versions of the timeline place a huge civil war that almost destroys the sect (and won't end until around 1933). But maybe we could attribute it to Dark Selina's manipulation (while torpored in Switzerland!), as blow back from the civil war as losing Sabbat seek to find a safe place for their side by conquering New England, a plan by the Black Hand to reunite the sect by leading a successful crusade, or an indication that the Sabbat of NYC and Canada were among the first centralizers and imposed some kind of order among the local Sabbat and attempted to conquer New England to showcase their strength.<br /> <br /> That's how I would approach it, but everyone will have their own preferences on what tidbits, lore, and trivia to include. We all have different tastes and different things inspire different people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T08:23:54-07:00","id":1534643,"title":"","content":"In all honesty Camarilla expansion in the New World coinciding with - or being launched in reaction to opportunities presented by - a Sabbat Civil War seems a plausible enough scenario.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, you will most definately know more about variations in the timeline than I do (As I am obliged to work from a handful of physical references, the White Wolf wiki, and whatever one can sniff out online), so I defer to you as \u2018Senior Partner\u2019 and an opinion it is wise to defer to.<br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, I\u2019d argue that these sort of contradictions in a Setting\u2019s backstory are invaluable to writers seeking to give the sense of an actual history, as opposed to writing a novel without actually writing a novel - if nothing else, being able to puzzle over various versions of a historic event and being obliged to admit that it\u2019s very possible NONE of them are accurate, but this is all we have to go on, is an experience every historian can relate to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T08:27:50-07:00","id":1534644,"title":"","content":"Also, is it just me or did anyone else read that name \u2018Baladin\u2019 and start wondering if the similarity between this name and the likes of \u2018Saladin\u2019 \u2018Saphadin\u2019 et al might suggest a refugee from the fall of the Ayyubid dynasty who may or may not have left the Middle East one hop ahead of the Mamelukes? (The tale of how he ended up attached to the Winchester chantry might be an adventure in it\u2019s own right!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T12:48:51-07:00","id":1534655,"title":"","content":"Saladin is the Western transliteration of Salah ad-Din, the actual name of the historical figure. &quot;Baladin&quot; is a French word meaning wandering performer, and it's a rare French last name. There are, of course, other varieties of Baladin out there. It is an ordinary Turkish last name as well. Most likely the original intent of Dark Colony was for a French origin Tremere.<br /> <br /> Setting contradictions between editions always leads to ST decision whether to embrace one version or the other, to split the difference, or create new information that explains why different versions exist. That can be a fun part of being the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-25T08:31:48-07:00","id":1534695,"title":"","content":"It is, in fact, one of the great pleasures of working in any shared universe - or, indeed, working with History (Indiana Jones is an exaggeration for effect, but I think it\u2019s safe to say that any real historian worth their salt loves to solve mysteries quite as much as they love to collect and share old anecdotes, artefacts &amp; Trivia.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I wasn\u2019t aware that \u2018Baladin\u2019 was a French surname, but given that Saladin <i>et al</i> are Medieval French versions of Arabic names (I sometimes think history ought to be described as one long game of \u2018Spanglish Whispers\u2019 rather than \u2018Chinese Whispers\u2019) that actually makes a good deal of sense.<br /> <br /> In all honesty I do like the notion that the Tremere Baladin is someone using a French name to obscure a still more exotic (By the standards of Federalist-era New England) origin: In fact making this character someone born a Turk who adopted a French name and wound up associated with the Winchester chantry before heading out to the New World suggests a pretty darned intriguing history (Of the sort that can very reasonably be associated with an elder vampire).<br /> <br /> One assumes that, according to this version of events, \u2018Baladin\u2019 might have been born (or lived most of his mortal life) in the Ottoman Sultan\u2019s European possessions (Possibly of mixed parentage), was recruited by the Tremere and (Either as a result of that transformation or through the very actions that made him an attractive subject for The Embrace) made his homeland too hot to hold him, entered Christian Europe and moved to an area of same where being a Turk was less inherently dangerous (So France after Francis I made an alliance with the Sultan would be as likely a place as any) and from there made a hop across the English Channel.<br /> <br /> Whether he was originallyTurkish or not, I do like the idea that Baladin was a childe of Meerlinda and himself the sire of Madeleine Coventry (With the latter being the first vampire he embraced): it helps make his promotion over Coventry at least somewhat politic, rather than a crude insult of the sort I don\u2019t appreciate with the Tremere (and also positions Baladin himself as an \u2018Advance Party\u2019 and proxy for Meerlinda in New England, which would help explain why the latter seems to have set up somewhere else in the United States.<br /> <br /> This version of things does beg the question of why Meerlinda didn\u2019t intervene during the Chantry War: my best attempt to win a \u2018No Prize\u2019 would be to suggest that Meerlinda preferred to avoid drawing attention to this unedifying spectacle by intervening directly, was too busy with more productive labours to get caught up in this sorry business or was patiently allowing Baladin a chance to settle his own affairs (Intervening only after the murder of her Childe and then only covertly).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-07T23:59:25-07:00","id":1536940,"title":"","content":"Go whole Lovecraft, and have your coterie fight the false Changing breed Werefrogs, and their kinfolk. Call them Dagons<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Anurana\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Anurana</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-10T03:23:37-07:00","id":1537142,"title":"","content":"Well if you want your VAMPIRE to go all hairy, you do you!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T18:23:59-07:00","id":1538454,"title":"","content":"I just read some interesting trivia on canonical New England vampire characters in an unlikely source. I was checking Necropolis: Atlanta for something, and in the section on the vampires of Atlanta saw some characters had ties to New England.<br /> <br /> Aunt Bedelia (6th generation Malkavian vampire embraced in Brighton, England in 1760) and her sire Alabaster moved to Boston area relatively soon after her embrace. She didn't like the city, broke free from her sire, and then moved down to Atlanta with a Ventrue ancillae named Herbert. Elsewhere it says she began her journey from Plymouth, MA so it's likely she moved to there after breaking things off with her sire, probably taking her &quot;boy&quot; Herbert (Bedelia's derangement is fixating on young men and becoming an overprotective mother to them.)<br /> <br /> She arrived in Atlanta when it was still known as &quot;Terminus&quot;, so her arrival was somewhere between 1836-1845. So she and Herbert might have been in New England from around 1760-1840.<br /> <br /> We don't know what happened to Alabaster, but he isn't mentioned in Dark Colony. But a 5th generation Malkavian isn't someone you just forget. He'd also be the first of a large number of exceptionally potent Malkavians to be in Boston. While canonically William Biltmore did not migrate to Boston until 1895, in this thread I moved him there pre-American Revolution. So I'd just make him, not Alabaster, as Bedelia's sire and adjust her generation accordingly. <br /> <br /> There's also the possibility that she could have sired one or more vampires. Biltmore is 6, so Bedelia would not be 7th. We know Skarvan was originally 8. Perhaps Skarvan was Bedelia's first childe. Perhaps Skarvan's antics was a reason Bedelia and her sire split.<br /> <br /> Since the Ventrue ancilla Herbert is a cipher (he only exists to demonstrate Bedelia goes nuts and destroys her &quot;boys&quot; if they become too independent), we don't have anything to go by. But willingly going with a Malkavian fixated on him indicates a level of desperation. So I'd have him be the childe of the deposed Ventrue Prince of Boston overthrown in 1783. That still gives him about 50-60 years still living in New England, but if Aunt Bedelia became fixated on him prior to the revolution, it's possible her sire - and new Prince of Boston - Biltmore would have accepted it. It would also provide a reason why Bedelia broke with Biltmore if eventually he considered Herbert's survival to be a threat to him.<br /> <br /> Herbert was said to be Ancilla by the time he and Bedelia arrived in Boston, so he was embraced prior to 1730-1740 or so. Boston was first settled in 1625, so it's quite possible he was a colonist in Boston embraced by a newly arriving Venture looking for a local person to assist his rule. I would keep him separate from the Rowlands lineage of Ventrue in Connecticut, but might plug him into the lineage of any Ventrue characters left in Boston or perhaps our Barnabas Collins analogue.<br /> <br /> Then there is also &quot;Thelonious&quot; an African slave originally brought to Virginia who was then bought and emancipated by abolitionists. He was educated, became involved in the Underground Railroad, and eventually embraced in 1859 by the Brujah Isaac in New York. He soon rose in power among the New York Brujah before moving to Atlanta to help the freedman after the end of the Civil War. Unfortunately, this history is quite a mess. Thelonius was 26 when he was embraced meaning he was born in 1833. However, the US abolished the international slave trade in 1808 meaning Thelonious could not have directly from Africa. His parents would need to be existing slaves in the US if we want to keep to the timeline. It's a minor change, but wanted to mention it. It's also a bit weird to have the character be tied to Boston but then have his embrace happen to New York. There are several canonical Brujah in Boston around this time that could serve as logical sires. Thelonious is 8th generation, but if we wanted Crispus Attucks or Pug Jackson to be his sire, we would adjust that to be a weaker generation. Thelonious would be merely a curious part of Boston's history, but it would help establish that underground railroad network Crispus Attucks established while he was still in Boston and give Pug Jackson another out of state contact to have that an ST could use if ever needed.<br /> <br /> Another bit of trivia is that Boston hosted a conclave in 1850 which sent several Archons down to the American south to investigate the rumors about the Southron Lords (an alliance of powerful vampires ruling from plantations in the South rather than the cities). All but one Archon failed to return. There's no mention of an 1850 conclave in Dark Colony, but no reason why we should not have had one and make it part of the revised history of New England.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T13:55:24-07:00","id":1538861,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, you\u2019ve proved yet again why your are a Senior Partner and I barely qualify as a wolf, a ram or a hart!<br /> <br /> It definitely seems sensible to treat \u2018Alabaster\u2019 as an alias.<br /> <br /> I tend to assume that by the time a Cainite has outlived their mortal generation they\u2019ve already adopted and discarded a significant number of aliases for practical reasons - and, given the nature of the World of Darkness, it makes perfect sense to prefer to become known by an Alias rather than what one might call a True Name, at least in the long term.<br /> <br /> Given the Malkavian tendency to embrace eccentricity, this probably goes double for the Mad Oracles (and quite possibly treble for the apparently extra-theatrical Malkavians of Boston).<br /> <br /> <br /> However, I do feel that you may be over-emphasising the importance of a vampire being embraced in the city with which they will become most closely associated: to my mind it makes perfect sense for a certain sort of vampire to prefer making their long-term home and hunting run somewhere with which they were not closely associated in their breathing days or the earliest nights of their career as a vampire (All the better to cover their tracks \u2026 and, just possibly, outrun the embarrassments of their own learning curve).<br /> <br /> After all, with the exception of the Tzimisce Cainites are not tied to the soil of their homeland (and some may prefer to prey on a population with which they have no lingering ties of mortal sentiment, blood descent or worldly obligation).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T14:17:58-07:00","id":1538867,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, \u2018Terminus\u2019 is a city name that absolutely begs to be turned into a \u2018City of Adventure\u2019 (Whether for the World of Darkness or any Urban Fantasy setting with sufficiently strong horror undertones and a greater willingness to run with some tongue in cheek humour).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T18:31:52-07:00","id":1538882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1538861#post1538861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I do feel that you may be over-emphasising the importance of a vampire being embraced in the city with which they will become most closely associated: to my mind it makes perfect sense for a certain sort of vampire to prefer making their long-term home and hunting run somewhere with which they were not closely associated in their breathing days or the earliest nights of their career as a vampire (All the better to cover their tracks \u2026 and, just possibly, outrun the embarrassments of their own learning curve).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there's no reason why someone can't move cities either as a mortal or as Kindred. I just find it frustrating that so many characters in World of Darkness products have very little ties to the region whose sourcebook they are in. It doesn't seem very organic. Why make Quention King III from New York instead of Boston for example? It robs you of the ability to integrate the individual characters of the sourcebook to each other. I think the first Chicago By Night did a much better job integrating foreign characters who arrived in Chicago with Kindred from Chicago. Outer sourcebooks not so much.<br /> <br /> As a character in Necropolis: Atlanta, it's immaterial whether Thelonious was from New York or Boston. As long as he's an outsider to Atlanta, mission accomplished for that specific character's role. But if you are going to have a character be from New York, why not just have the character's mortal history be from New York too? Or if you put his mortal self in Boston why not have him embraced there? What is being gained by changing things?<br /> <br /> So given Thelonious's mortal history with Boston, his involvement in the underground railroad, and canonical characters in Boston who were also involved there, I just decided it'd be good to steal him and use it as part of the setting's history. I might even just move the character away from Atlanta and back to Boston.<br /> <br /> There's something like 120 Camarilla/Anarch characters in New England plus 30-40 Sabbat. That's double the total number of Kindred in Chicago. Even assuming you don't want to fill out every single NPC - you want room for the PCs, some unknown NPCs, and some extra space to create new NPCs to fill in the blanks between PCs and established NPCs - an ST will likely need to have at least 100 NPCs. Dark Colony gives you less than 20. Some STs are perfectly fine creating 80-100 new NPCs from scratch, but I'd rather reduce that burden to a more reasonable number. It's just easier to make revisions to existing NPCs (especially ones that are mostly generic rather than specifically important or vital to the setting) or repurpose them, rather than start from scratch for every single one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-23T20:42:16-07:00","id":1542539,"title":"","content":"I found some other mentions of New England in other Vampire sourcebooks. Finally have time to post it here.<br /> <br /> In New Orleans by Night, we are introduced to several Tremere with history in the New England region. It describes three renegade Tremere - Antonio Calbullarshi, Nigel Poter, and Sebastian Wolcott - who arrive in New England in the late 1700s before they eventually move to New Orleans. I think the best way to integrate them into the history of Dark Colony is that these three would have joined Madeline Coventry's Salem Chantry since it was already on the outs with the clan, and thus they would have participated in its war with the Boston Chantry. Antonio would quickly disappear, but Nigel and Sebastian assisted Madeline Coventry in the hopes of establishing themselves as accepted Tremere should she win. In 1831 the Sabbat overrun the Salem Chantry. Madeline Coventry disappears. Nigel Porter and Sebastian Wolcott are among the survivors and flee south and disappear.<br /> <br /> Antonio would eventually return to New England after the Anarch Free State was established. There he embraced the awakening mage Marie Richet in 1991 and presented her to the Hartford Chantry (which in this thread we moved to Providence) in the hopes an embraced mage would fix things with the clan and welcome him back. Instead it got them both blood hunted. Marie's backstory is very complicated.<br /> <br /> I am a bit surprised that all the Tremere in New Orleans are 1) essentially all renegades and 2) tied to New England. It must have been a deliberate design choice.<br /> <br /> The next sourcebook is Giovanni Chronicles IV which provides more detail on the Milliners. Now I must say I do not like GCIV as a sourcebook. It internally contradicts itself, contradicts\u200b the Giovanni clanbook, and does things differently than what I would have them. But in one spot it establishes Francis Milliner's embrace in 1954 (though in another section it moves this to 1959). 1954 is a good match for the clanbook's original description of mid-fifties. Jason Milliner, Francis's nephew, is embraced in 1959 although in GCIV, his sire is not Francis but the same sire as Francis which I think is just silly. Again a family of aristocratic Venetian financiers are portrayed as simply Sicilian mobsters. How the Giovanni embrace these people without permission by Prince Quention King and never suffer any blowback is never adequately explained. Also despite the clanbook clearly stating ALL the Milliners are generation 10 and above, both Francis and Jason start as 9th generation.<br /> <br /> So in my version once the Giovanni decide on embracing Francis, the Giovanni struck a deal with Quentin King. They'll make up influence and business support he lacks from the Connecticut Ventrue's rivalry. Quentin agrees up front that Francis will be embraced in 1954 (10th generation), and that Francis can create one or two more children which he does in 1959 by embracing his nephew (11th generation). The Milliners officially keep out of Kindred politics per the Promise of 1528, but secretly provide Quentin some support that he needs.<br /> <br /> The last thing is Chicago by Night 2nd edition which has some trivia. The 11th generation Caitiff Victoria Longwood is said to come from an old money family in New England. Torrence, a 10th generation Toreador, embraces her in 1984, but being annoyed by him she manages to stake Torrence and then flee, eventually running into some anarchs and she eventually makes her way to the Free State.<br /> <br /> So this rather throwaway text gives us some nice things. We have the mortal Longwood family that is extremely old and powerful family in New England. We have a known 10th generation Toreador vampire named Torrence (who could easily have survived his staking though CbN shows him as destroyed). We could place the Longwoods anywhere, either in Boston or Connecticut depending on whether we wanted Torrence to be in either city.<br /> <br /> Dark Colony only gives us Elsa Linden, but Swansong provides various Toreador that we could use in Boston. So just to cover all our bases, I'd probably put Torrence and the Longwoods in Connecticut to be part of Upton Rowland's domain. Torrence might be unrelated to any existing vampires, or we could make him part of a lineage that goes back to Elsa Linden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-26T23:06:00-07:00","id":1542752,"title":"","content":"This is a more speculative post.<br /> <br /> In Milwaukee by Night, we are told that Edward, the Black Prince of Cornwall embraced Akawa in Missouri in 1770. Otherwise we are given very little about his past between his embrace and his current status in Milwaukee.<br /> <br /> Presumably, Edward being in Missouri is a result of St Louis (founded in 1764). He does not have Protean or any other Disciplines which makes overland wilderness travel easy, so presumably he made safe passage through the existing French fur trade routes in the Midwest (though by 1770 French North America had been ceded to either Britain or Spain). How did Edward get there though? Missouri is a long way from Cornwall.<br /> <br /> Although not detailed, Dark Colony says there were early Brujah in New England, but that the Ventrue arrival in Boston and Connecticut pushed them to northern New England, and that eventually Sabbat attacks in turn pushed them back south which lead to fights that erupted during the American Revolution. We also know from World of Darkness 1e that the Brujah were one of the lesser clans of England/Great Britain. The Ventrue, lead by Mithras, dominated, and their only real challenges came from the Tremere and Toreador.<br /> <br /> So Edward, being a Brujah, could very well have left England early for more opportunities in North America. Or if he stayed longer, he might have been one of the Brujah who rallied to Pendragon's struggle against Mithras in the 18th century. In either case, he would have left the region some time before the actual War of Independence. Edward arriving in New England, as opposed to Virginia or Pennsylvania, would have easier access to New France which would allow him to follow the trade routes to St Louis. He could have arrived some time in the first half of the 18th century (or earlier) and then made his way down the Ohio River after the end of the French and Indian War.<br /> <br /> Edward would not have been any real factor in New England's history, but he could be an alternative source of a Brujah lineage in New England that does not issue from Pendragon or the Anarchs (MacNeil or Foccart) that fought during the revolution. Someone, after all, needed to sire some of those Brujah who fled north. Some of the might still be around, though individuals could easily be followers of Pendragon, Anarchs, or independent Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T19:05:44-07:00","id":1543310,"title":"","content":"I have to be awe in the care you took in world building.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T23:45:20-07:00","id":1543329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1543310#post1543310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to be awe in the care you took in world building.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. Because of this thread, I am actually compiling my posts (and others) in a document if I ever wanted to run a New England chronicle. It's important to note I have never run a chronicle in New England, and despite my notes I will probably never do so. (Sometimes such things do prove useful even in chronicles set elsewhere.) I actually have some intended posts that will address another character in Boston and the role of New York City as the &quot;flank&quot; in any New England chronicle as a result of reading the Ventrue Chronicle and NYBN. But that will need to wait a while.<br /> <br /> I have a love-hate relationship with canon. I think much canon is crap, but I always want to reconcile my own ideas with canon as much as possible. However, it's been fun to notice various references to New England in other sourcebooks and try to fill in the blanks with what's been established in Dark Colony, and some of the thread's contributors versions of an improved setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T16:46:48-07:00","id":1543800,"title":"","content":"Found some additional mentions of New England in sourcebooks.<br /> <br /> In World of Darkness: Sorcerer, the section on the Ancient Order of the Aeon Rites mentions their Boston temple is a well respected charity called Saint Simon's Rest. And that the local Bone Gnawers have taken it upon themselves to protect it. So not directly relevant, but for those STs who like to include elements of other games, or just want an Easter egg to include, that's there.<br /> <br /> Of more importance is that it reminded me that the Arcanum has a Boston chapter house there. In the original corebooks, they just mention that Boston is one of three foundation houses of the Arcanum. However, in the revised (and V2) corebook it mentions that the Boston chapter house was burned down by Cainites in 1910. Intrigued by the change, I checked a friend's copy of Halls of the Arcanum and discovered that this was first mentioned there and provided some real information. (The same sourcebook seems to have decided that rather have three foundation houses, the Arcanum now had a single foundation house in London and Boston was downgraded to a chapter house.)<br /> <br /> First, I believe the use of the term Cainite rather than Kindred indicates the intent that it was the Sabbat who burned down the Arcanum's Boston chapter house.<br /> <br /> Second, the actual Arcanum sourcebook says that vampires torched the Arcanum chapterhouse in Boston on either July 16 or 17, 1910. Robert Brooks, a member of the Arcanum, had infiltrated a mystic group called the Children of Hecate who had eleven members. At his third meeting with them, he attended a magical sex rite in a remote grove outside Boston that summoned an ebon-skinned Dark Lady - the cult\u2019s Hecate - from the ground who joined the orgy. Brooks later noticed that her love bites was from blood drinking. Brooks escaped from the orgy and returned to the Boston chapterhouse, but was followed. The next night the chapterhouse was burned down probably by people associated with the blood cult.<br /> <br /> This &quot;Dark Lady&quot; could be either Sabbat or Camarilla. Blood cults are not unheard of within the Camarilla, and Sabbat rarely utilize humans as pawns. Furthermore, the Dark Lady seemed to operate along and not as part of a pack. If not for the use of the term Cainite in the corebook (a term not used in Halls of the Arcanum), I personally would assign this vampire to being of the Camarilla. Although the Boston Kindred could believe it was the Sabbat who did it.<br /> <br /> The powers used by the Dark Lady indicate Protean (Earth Meld allowing her to rise up from the ground), Potence, and Presence. She may or may not have had any Blood Magic. She didn't seem to use any, but the Children of Hecate viewed her as a goddess of magic and were performing rituals for her. I'm inclined to think she just used Disciplines and the cultists didn't learn any kind of real magic.<br /> <br /> The use of Protean suggests Gangrel, but the use of Presence and her description of beautiful make me think she's more likely Toreador. Not unusual for vampires to know out-of-clan Disciplines. Entirely possible it could have been a vampire of any other clan like Brujah. Assuming the Dark Lady survived, we have a female vampire with possibly her blood cult, the Children of Hecate, still around. Her description as ebon-skinned could mean the vampire was either dark skinned African woman, that the vampire had used black body paint because black furred or skinned animals were sacred to the goddess, or possibly a result of arising from the ground and covered her body with the dark (likely wet) earth. I have my own preference, but STs will decide on their own.<br /> <br /> So STs can create whatever character they'd like to correspond to the few known facts. I do think this is important because the 1910 attack on the Arcanum seems to be the reason the Camarilla forbid Kindred from interacting with it. It seemed to have created a big problem. Earlier sourcebooks stated that the Inner Circle proclaims - and that this was backed by Brujah Justicar Ryland - that the Arcanum was not to be interfered with. I don't think &quot;Ryland&quot; ever gets mentioned again. My personal interpretation is that Ryland was probably the Brujah Justicar around 1910, and that he held a Conclave in Boston that investigated and addressed the issue. So that is a good bit of history to drop. If a Justicar actually investigated the incident, he either would have likely found and destroyed the Dark Lady, or it shows the Dark Lady was either powerful enough to hide her involvement, escaped, or was too powerful to be officially punished and possibly just reprimanded and her involvement covered up. Perhaps that is why it was blamed on the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> For my own purposes, I'd rather have the Dark Lady and her cult still be around. It is just too interesting an angle to not have for an existing character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T06:28:09-07:00","id":1544460,"title":"","content":"I can only wonder if the Justicar Ryland failing to survive his investigation (or coming through it badly mauled) might explain his lack of mention in other sources.<br /> <br /> Ha! Perhaps he simply became too obsessed with tracking the Dark Lady to hold down his night job?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T13:09:00-07:00","id":1544489,"title":"","content":"If Dark Selina was actually in New England rather than being in torpor in Switzerland, I'd be tempted make her the Dark Lady. She'd definitely have enough power to destroy a Justicar or evade him. Then again, I would also imagine that the Arcanum would not have gotten anywhere close to her or its members merely lose their chapterhouse.<br /> <br /> So overall, I'd probably have this be part of some new NPCs background, and just have Ryland stick around long enough to assist the Masquerade and make sure the existing power structure commits to leaving the Arcanum alone from now on.<br /> <br /> I wonder if Ryland was originally meant to be the current (as of the early nineties) Brujah Justicar. Justicar Carlak was specifically mentioned by name when the Anarch Cookbook was published, but I don't think his clan was established as Brujah (I could be wrong, feel free to correct me). Perhaps Carlak was intended to belong to another clan, but he was established as Brujah by accident later on because the writers remembered his name, but had forgotten Ryland's.<br /> <br /> It would have made more sense if the current Brujah Justicar was enforcing the rule against interference with the Arcanum, but I think it does work as a historical pronouncement as well. Presumably actions against the Arcanum would be justification for the closest Justicar to arrive in a domain and investigate and if needed render judgment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T11:56:51-08:00","id":1547598,"title":"","content":"Especially if the Justicar in question were looking for an opportunity to assert their authority in a territory where there\u2019s no outstanding emergency (and the Justicar sees no outstanding reason to precipitate one).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-12T15:28:00-08:00","id":1547705,"title":"","content":"Found more references to New England is canon sources. A while back <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28339\" data-vbnamecard=\"28339\">Atticus Cleanclaw</a> mentioned the New England ties of Christopher Houghton and his sire Matthew Lubbock, but Los Angeles By Night has at least one additional connection to New England. <br /> <br /> The Ventrue Edward Vignes and his brood (his wife and butler) were originally from Boston, but had to flee the city after they &quot;backed the wrong faction in a war among the Boston Kindred.&quot; We're not given any other information except we know Edward was embraced in 1882 by &quot;Sir Andrew McCardle&quot; and subsequently embraced his wife that same year and his butler in 1894. We can derive certain things logically that are not mentioned outright. That Edward was able to legally embrace his wife the same year as his own embrace and his butler a decade later ought to mean that hire sire must have had some pull. I imagine Sir Andrew obtained permission both for him to embrace Edward and for Edward to embrace his own wife at the same time. For Edward to be able to legally embrace again twelve years later is also proof he had impressed the Prince in some fashion. Politically unimportant neonates just don't get legal permission to embrace much. Late nineteenth century Boston did see explosive population growth and the Great Boston Fire happened in 1872 so there may have been some room to allow for more embraces, but I still see Edward having two childer to be noteworthy. This was also done at a time and place when the Ventrue overall were not powerful. The Boston Ventrue had been emasculated since the end of the American Revolutionary War. So Sir Andrew was either very skilled and/or cooperated with a known power, like Prince Quention King. Now in actual truth, I don't think the writer of the Los Angeles By Night sourcebook gave much thought to this backstory. He likely only wanted to set up his little family soap opera within the Vignes brood, but having done so we need to fill in the details.<br /> <br /> The other big thing is what exactly was this &quot;wrong faction in a war among the Boston Kindred&quot; that drove the Vignes all the way to southern California for their lives? It had to be after 1894 when he embraced his butler, and before 1944 when the Anarchs overthrow Don Sebastian as we know the Vignes brood's arrival predates the Free States. The big event that happened in New England during that time was Operation Longbow of Pendragon, Warwick, and Biltmore. So I will go with that and state that the Boston Ventrue of Sir Andrew opposed them and paid the price. Sir Andrew most likely died, and Edward decided it was best for him and his small brood to flee.<br /> <br /> So while this is only a brief period of time, I do think it provides some more knowledge on the intrigues of Boston leading up to Operation Longbow, and the names of some Ventrue who could act as sires for other Ventrue characters (particularly Sir Andrew McCardle). I'd probably make Sir Andrew (of the 8th generation) the sole surviving Ventrue of the original British Ventrue who ruled Boston until the American Revolution. He'll be the progenitor of most of the Ventrue embraced in Boston, and he'd have had earlier childer than Edward embraced between 1783-1895.<br /> <br /> Probably not relevant to a New England chronicle, there are some things we can speculate base on the character sheets of the Vignes brood. While the 62 year old Edward's profession is stated as &quot;gentleman&quot;, he his Abilities include Finance 3, History 3, Law 3, Linguistics 3, and Politics 3. I would say his career was most likely as a lawyer with strong ties to the business community. He also has surpisingly strong combat Abilities in Brawl 3, Firearms 2, and Melee 2. That is probably just because the sourcebook writer wanted a strong enough martial character to survive in the Anarch Free States. While we could say that these developed while he was a vampire (particularly after 1944), we also have another convenient way to explain them: the American Civil War. Edward would have been in his forties at the time of the war, but there are plenty of historical examples of men in their late thirties and forties enlisting. As a college educated lawyer, he likely would have immediately become a commissioned officer like captain, major, or colonel with one of the Massachusetts volunteer regiments. He probably served in a combat role, not just as a staff officer. While this service might just have been out of patriotism, it might also mean that Edward was involved in the abolitionist movement to some degree and he might have offered his legal services to cases resisting the Fugitive Slave Law and others. If so, then it's possible that Crispus Attucks might have remembered Edward's work as a mortal and appreciated it. In the aftermath of the 1944 revolt that established the Anarch Free States, Crispus might have intervened to make sure Vignes and his brood survived unmolested in Pasadena. And in our version of Operation Longbow that showed Pendragon finally &quot;betraying&quot; the Brujah Anarchs by his personal tyranny, having Vignes be an exile because of his opposition to Pendragon would be another reason why Crispus would vouch for him. Edward Vignes might be a Ventrue, but he also had a history of doing the right thing in Crispus's eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-13T10:52:31-08:00","id":1547713,"title":"","content":"Now this is another fascinating bit of trivia with potentially-intriguing implications for the setting - I wonder if the New England Ventrue made something of a comeback in the mid to late Victorian era in part because Pendragon was diverting local Brujah resources towards his attempted coup in Old England? (Which I assume took place during the period when Mithras was absent from his demesne and his seneschal was holding things together in his absence*).<br /> <br /> Given the failure of that effort, it\u2019s not impossible that either Brujah losses in that conflict or Ventrue retaliation for same (Presumably with assets from elsewhere in the world being diverted to New England, discreetly or blatantly) might have played some role in a significant population increase that would, however, ultimately prove to be short-lived as Pendragon et al executed a major comeback.<br /> <br /> <br /> *In fact I wonder if the failed coup in London 1848 (that seems to have persuaded Valerius to finally start reaching for the crown in his own right) might have been the work of Pendragon - or at least the precursor to his own effort to overthrow the Clan Ventrue in the British Isles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-13T15:46:34-08:00","id":1547721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1547713#post1547713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if the New England Ventrue made something of a comeback in the mid to late Victorian era</div> </div> </div> </div>Per Dark Colony, the Ventrue did seem to stage a comeback during this time. The sourcebook tells us that the Ventrue managed to retake control of Rhode Island during the Civil War as many Brujah went south to feed on battlefield casualties. The Ventrue would control Providence and the rest of the state until Warwick eliminates all non-Nosferatu vampires there in 1900.<br /> <br /> I also assume that the &quot;Wingate Initiative&quot; proposed at the Newport, RI conclave (post Civil War) that would create a regional primogen council (the Congress of New England) to coordinate anti-Sabbat activities was also a Ventrue initiative. It's the kind of thing they liked to do, and it's unlikely a conclave would be held at a place (Rhode Island) controlled by the Ventrue that the clan did not support. The Ventrue would have been the dominant clan in Connecticut and Rhode Island, and if we believe they were coming back in strength in Boston because of our speculation around Edward Vignes, then it would make sense to try something like it at this time. No date is given for this conclave, but it had to have been held between 1865-1895. Wording seems to apply it was held soon after the end of the Civil War, but there's enough vagueness that an ST could hold it later with the idea that Vignes might have participated. Even if held earlier, it doesn't mean internal domain politics in Boston could not have been going the local Ventrue's way. Upton's sire Georgia Rowlands is still Prince of Hartford at this time and likely the clan elder. She might have been working hard to unit the clan regionally. She disappears in the first decade of the 20th century. Given the Ventrue prince of Providence being killed at this time, we could set the departure of the Vignes around the same time as the Ventrue suddenly lose a lot of power because of Operation Longbow.<br /> <br /> In the version of Dark Colony that I am building where Pendragon (and his allies in Longbow) arrives much earlier, I'll probably have the failure of this initiative be the start of his plotting to take over by force so that he can stop the Sabbat his way. However, in Dark Colony canon there's no reason why local Brujah might not voyage to Britain to help him fight Mithras as he does not leave until 1885.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1547713#post1547713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*In fact I wonder if the failed coup in London 1848 (that seems to have persuaded Valerius to finally start reaching for the crown in his own right) might have been the work of Pendragon - or at least the precursor to his own effort to overthrow the Clan Ventrue in the British Isles.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not familiar enough with the details to have a good chronology of British/London Kindred history so I don't know the event you are referencing, but it seems very plausible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-14T07:21:40-08:00","id":1547737,"title":"","content":"I admit that the history of Victorian Vampire London is something I\u2019ve pieced together from various entries on the White Wolf Wiki, but the most relevant section may be found on the \u2018Valerius\u2019 article linked to below - whilst Mithras was absent from London &amp; Britain between AD 1798 and 1885, with Valerius being left in charge throughout his absence, it was only after an incident in 1848 (I was mistaken, this was actually a Sabbat attack) that Valerius seems to have started acting as more than a steward, moving away from Mithras\u2019 policies and making London a more open city, with consequences intended and unintended (In fact London under Valerius between 1848-1985 strikes me as far more interesting than the official setting for VICTORIAN AGE: VAMPIRE, which takes place after the return of Mithras).<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Valerius\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Valerius</a><br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, it\u2019s possible that this relative liberalisation of London by Valerius may have been a key precondition for the schemes of Roman Pendragon that saw the latter ousted from Great Britain by his own clan in AD 1885 (Presumably because the unexpected return of Mithras and his immediate murder of the Tremere primogen persuaded potential backers that denial preferable to being murdered by an angry Vampire demigod).<br /> <br /> Incidentally, going by the history of Roman Pendragon as presented on the White Wolf wiki, it would seem that he became \u201cthe most prominent Brujah in England\u201d at some<br /> point between AD 1768 (Having been sired in 1708, it took his sire sixty years to be convinced he was fit to be introduced to Cainite society) and 1885, after betraying his sire and leaving Switzerland (Where she had kept him, rather against his will, apparently employing him against Guillaume, Prince of Geneva).<br /> <br /> The exact period of his departure from Switzerland and arrival in England is unclear: We only know that he\u2019d spent a century working himself into a position of preeminence amongst the English Brujah by AD 1885, suggesting that he betrayed his sire and headed back to Britain at some point in or after the 1780s (It\u2019s possible he headed to New England first, using the American Revolution and/or it\u2019s aftermath to start making a name on the international scene, then parlaying that prestige into some sort of position back on Old England).<br /> <br /> I think we can safely say that the departure of Mithras and his increasingly long absence after AD 1798 would have piqued Pendragon\u2019s interest and I would bet money that the abortive Sabbat attack of 1848 was the point at which his star really began to rise - given his later career as Anti Sabbat par excellence - suggesting that the period between 1848 and 1885 might well have seen increasing tensions and a series of manoeuvres as the respective ambitions of Valerius of Clan Ventrue and Roman Pendragon of Clan Brujah began to collide.<br /> <br /> At least before Mithras upset that particular chess board.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-14T07:23:08-08:00","id":1547738,"title":"","content":"P.S. apologies for stating things in such a rambling, untidy fashion - I\u2019m very much prone to \u2018done in one\u2019 posts and have a bad habit of typing things up on my phone, rather than something with a monitor of decent size to boot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-14T15:29:04-08:00","id":1547747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1547737#post1547737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, it\u2019s possible that this relative liberalisation of London by Valerius may have been a key precondition for the schemes of Roman Pendragon that saw the latter ousted from Great Britain by his own clan in AD 1885 (Presumably because the unexpected return of Mithras and his immediate murder of the Tremere primogen persuaded potential backers that denial preferable to being murdered by an angry Vampire demigod).</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually fits the canonical timeline very well. It may have been unintentional because as far as I know, London By Night makes no references to Pendragon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1547737#post1547737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(In fact London under Valerius between 1848-1985 strikes me as far more interesting than the official setting for VICTORIAN AGE: VAMPIRE, which takes place after the return of Mithras).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds very true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-21T04:43:59-08:00","id":1547871,"title":"","content":"Now I just have to work out which other vampires might have been - or verifiably were - in London between AD 1848 and 1885, without any large reserve of VTM material.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-29T15:42:47-08:00","id":1548038,"title":"","content":"I was re-reading this thread and stumbled onto the suggestion that a small town in Maine had suffered the fate of SALEM\u2019S LOT <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> style at some point in the early to mid 1970s.<br /> <br /> For some reason the name \u2018Blueberry ME\u2019 popped into my head not long afterwards (Probably because it\u2019s so very innocuous-sounding).<br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, I did some digging into a list of ghost towns in Maine: it\u2019s a fairly short list, but of the towns with at least a snippet of fact associated with them, most were gone by or before the mid-20th century.<br /> <br /> The only ones for which I\u2019ve been unable to dig up a date of demise as yet are Freeman (Franklin county) and Ligonia village (But that\u2019s now in South Portland).<br /> <br /> As a note, I\u2019m fond of consulting the Wikipedia lists of ghost towns when looking to name a fictional town in an Urban Fantasy or Horror setting (For reasons that should be obvious).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-29T22:24:42-08:00","id":1548044,"title":"","content":"It wouldn't be a bad idea to move in time any &quot;Salem's Lot&quot; style town to a fictional (and isolated) ghost town that died prior to WWII. It could be more believable than one that happened in the seventies and eighties before certain technologies became widespread. Not only could it be vampirized by Sabbat without breaking the Masquerade, it could be wiped out by Garou without breaking the Veil. A small town that disappeared during the Great Depression would not be seen odd.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it was meant as the prologue of a big crusade against Boston and some packs got too enthusiastic about a shovelhead party and eradicated the town. Perhaps just after the ending of the second Sabbat civil war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-06T04:38:57-08:00","id":1548249,"title":"","content":"Now at least one of those ghost towns became a ghost town because it was sitting on land that would be flooded by the construction of a dam, which I think we can all agree has that proper \u201cWe are going to bury this Bad Idea and then we are going to DROWN IT\u201d enthusiasm one associates with the aftermath of a horror movie.<br /> <br /> Admittedly this means somebody\u2019s drinking water quite possibly contains a worrisome trace of vampire ash, but such is life in Horror Movie New England!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-06T16:30:50-08:00","id":1548272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1501560-regional-settings-new-england?p=1548249#post1548249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Now at least one of those ghost towns became a ghost town because it was sitting on land that would be flooded by the construction of a dam, which I think we can all agree has that proper \u201cWe are going to bury this Bad Idea and then we are going to DROWN IT\u201d enthusiasm one associates with the aftermath of a horror movie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! That is an excellent idea.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-07T12:24:51-08:00","id":1548301,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, you\u2019ll absolutely love this: the submerged town I was thinking of is/was called \u2018Flagstaff\u2019.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flagstaff,_Maine\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/aa/Main_Street%2C_Flagstaff%2C_ME.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flagstaff,_Maine\" target=\"_blank\"> Flagstaff, Maine - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flagstaff,_Maine\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flagstaff,_Maine </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The fact this settlement was quite near the Canadian border also makes it a plausible target for Sabbat schemes (and the town being disestablished in AD 1950 allows us to suggest that it was swallowed up and spewed forth demons sometime shortly after the Second World War - when the world was worrying too much about the atomic bomb and the Cold War and the aftermath of WWII to pay much attention to horror movie madness in rural Maine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-13T04:38:30-08:00","id":1548467,"title":"","content":"Stumbled onto a New England Ventrue by accident (Interestingly, his name suggests First Nations ancestry).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Stephen_Thunderhorse\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Stephen_Thunderhorse</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-20T17:48:25-08:00","id":1548639,"title":"","content":"<br /> There's one thing about New England that most people don't understand is, it snows there, a lot; As Stephen King put it, &quot;New England's nice, if you want to spend half the year inside&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-21T04:18:24-08:00","id":1548662,"title":"","content":"Well quite a bit of New England is right next door to Canada, so that rather goes without saying, eh?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}